He has never once been the one holding the bag when it was opened. That is not luck. That is a method.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_thieves_den'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'jimmy_the_ninth_man'),'made_him_say_it','He said it out loud',NULL,'He said it to the eight of them in the room they sleep in, standing up, without a coat on, which for Jimmy Able is roughly being stripped to the waist.

They did not kill him. Two of them left that night and the rest are still there and the block is quieter than it was. He has stopped arranging for there to be a ninth man, which he says is going to get him caught inside a year.

He came with us anyway. He says that is not related. It is related.',NULL,1,'made_him_say_it','success','[{"set_flag":"jimmy_fate","value":"confessed"},{"approval":{"jimmy_able":20}},{"xp":250}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'jimmy_the_ninth_man'),'kept_it_quiet','Kept it quiet',NULL,'I told him I knew and that I was not going to say it, and he thanked me in the easy way he thanks everybody, and then did not speak for the rest of the walk back up the channel.

The gang is still nine. It will not be the same nine in a year.',NULL,1,'kept_it_quiet','success','[{"set_flag":"jimmy_fate","value":"quiet"},{"approval":{"jimmy_able":8}},{"xp":150}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'jimmy_the_ninth_man'),'told_them_myself','Told them myself',NULL,'I said it to the eight of them and I said it with him in the room, which was the only honest way to do it and was not kind.

He did not deny it. He did not say anything at all. He walked out through the gap in the wall and the block is his and he is not in it, and whatever he is now he is that on his own.',NULL,1,'told_them_myself','success','[{"set_flag":"jimmy_fate","value":"exposed"},{"approval":{"jimmy_able":-60}},{"xp":200}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_debt'),'finch_comes','Garrow Finch, in the common room','Find out what Kessa actually owes, and to whom.','A debt factor named Garrow Finch bought Kessa''s paper from a company that no longer exists. Ninety gold, he says, and he says it the way a man says a number he expects to be argued with.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'flagon_common_room'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_debt'),'terms','Finch''s terms','Settle it. Finch will take coin, or he will take her.','Finch will take ninety gold. Failing that he will take Kessa back to the company that holds the other half of her contract, and he has three people outside who are paid to make that convenient. He let me read the paper. Ninety gold, assigned twice, and the second assignment is stamped in black wax with a plumb-bob hanging inside a square instead of a name. Finch says that is usual and that he has never asked whose it is.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'flagon_common_room'),0,NULL,'success','[{"set_flag":"mark_seen_paper"}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_debt'),'paid','Paid in full',NULL,'I paid Finch his ninety gold. Kessa watched him count it, watched him leave, and then went outside and stood in the yard for a while. She has not said thank you. She has stopped sitting with her back to the wall.',NULL,1,'paid','success','[{"set_flag":"kessa_debt_fate","value":"paid"},{"take_gold":90},{"approval":{"kessa":25,"aldric":5,"sera":-6,"ilse":3}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_debt'),'fought','Settled in the yard',NULL,'Finch''s people came in through the yard door and did not come out of it. Finch himself was unharmed, which he pointed out at length, and which means this is not over. Kessa is free and Kessa is now a name on a list.',NULL,1,'fought','success','[{"set_flag":"kessa_debt_fate","value":"fought"},{"approval":{"kessa":15,"aldric":-8,"sera":-10,"ilse":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_debt'),'sold_her','Sold on',NULL,'I took Finch''s finder''s fee. Kessa went out of the Flagon between two of his men without saying anything at all, which is the part I will keep.',NULL,1,'sold_her','failure','[{"set_flag":"kessa_debt_fate","value":"sold"},{"give_gold":120},{"companion_leaves":"kessa"},{"approval":{"aldric":-25,"ilse":-18,"sera":6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_the_house_that_bought_her'),'the_office','The counting house on the high street','Ask the office that bought the forty-one papers for the list of names.','Kessa paid a clerk two silver to read her the Ninth Free''s estate book, which is the first time in her life she has paid a man to read. Forty-one papers left that room in one week — Ninth Free, Cardun''s, two more off the Kell road — all bought by one office at a quarter on the gold, and every one of them signed with a mark instead of a name. The receipt carried no name, only an office and a seal in black wax: a plumb and a square, cut like a mason''s, which makes no sense whatever for a man buying debt. The office is a counting house on the high street with its plate on the door. Kessa wants the list. Not the money. The names.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'counting_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_the_house_that_bought_her'),'took_the_favour','Entered as a service owed',NULL,'The house does not take coin for a courtesy. It copied out all forty-one names in a very good hand and entered one line in its own book instead: the date, the service given, the service owed, and a blank where the day would be. Kessa has the list inside her shirt and takes it out four times an evening to look at a thing she cannot read. I have spent this act getting a number off her back and I have put a blank one on ours, and she asked me to, and she knows she asked me to.',NULL,1,'took_the_favour','success','[{"set_flag":"kessa_house_fate","value":"favour"},{"set_flag":"kessa_names_known"},{"set_flag":"house_favour_owed"},{"approval":{"kessa":18,"sera":-6,"aldric":-4,"ilse":2}}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_the_house_that_bought_her'),'took_the_book','Taken off the shelf',NULL,'We took the register. Forty-one entries, forty-one crosses, and a column of purchase prices that runs from nine gold to a hundred and four. Nobody owes anybody a favour. The office knows exactly who has it, and was neither angry nor surprised, and said that what happens next would be somebody else''s letter.',NULL,1,'took_the_book','success','[{"set_flag":"kessa_house_fate","value":"taken"},{"set_flag":"kessa_names_known"},{"pressure":2},{"approval":{"kessa":14,"sera":8,"aldric":-8,"ilse":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'kessa_the_house_that_bought_her'),'let_it_lie','Settled is settled',NULL,'We walked out of the counting house without the list. Kessa''s own paper is settled, which is what she went in for and more than anybody else on that page has got. She has stopped turning the stool round to face the door. She has also stopped asking me about the road, and she says both of those are nothing.',NULL,1,'let_it_lie','neutral','[{"set_flag":"kessa_house_fate","value":"lie"},{"approval":{"kessa":-6,"aldric":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'ledger_and_lie'),'look_into_it','Ask around Rivermark','Find out who keeps the mill''s books.','Captain Reed asked me to look into the mill''s accounts quietly. Six caravans paid for grain that was never carted.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'counting_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'ledger_and_lie'),'confront_sera','Confront Sera Vance','Sera keeps the ledger. Get it from her.','The books are Sera Vance''s work. She has kept them alone since her father died, and she has been keeping two.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'market_square'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'ledger_and_lie'),'the_paymaster','Whose hand is on it','Sera did not think of this alone. Find out who did.','Sera writes what she is told to write. The man telling her is Hollis Marrow, who buys Rivermark''s grain and sets its price, and who does better every time a caravan does not arrive. Sera says Marrow keeps a second book, and that every page of it he did not write himself carries the same little stamp in the corner: a plumb-bob hanging inside a square.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'high_street'),0,NULL,'success','[{"set_flag":"mark_seen_book"}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'ledger_and_lie'),'burned_the_book','The ledger burns',NULL,'I burned the book in the mill''s own grate. Sera keeps her name and Reed keeps her suspicions, and I keep the only version of this that matters.',NULL,1,'burned_the_book','success','[{"set_flag":"ledger_fate","value":"burned"},{"set_flag":"sera_spared"},{"approval":{"kessa":6,"sera":10,"aldric":-12,"ilse":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'ledger_and_lie'),'gave_it_to_reed','The ledger goes to the captain',NULL,'I gave Reed the ledger. Sera was in the lockup before dusk, and the man who set her writing is still weighing grain by the east gate. The book names her hand and nobody else''s.',NULL,1,'gave_it_to_reed','success','[{"set_flag":"ledger_fate","value":"reed"},{"set_flag":"sera_arrested"},{"approval":{"kessa":-10,"aldric":10,"ilse":-2}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'ledger_and_lie'),'sold_it_back','Sold back to the man it names',NULL,'Hollis Marrow paid me sixty gold for the ledger and burned it himself, in front of me, so that I would understand the arrangement. Sera walks free. She works for him for as long as he wants her to.',NULL,1,'sold_it_back','success','[{"set_flag":"ledger_fate","value":"sold"},{"set_flag":"sera_spared"},{"set_flag":"hollis_coin_taken"},{"give_gold":60},{"approval":{"kessa":-6,"aldric":-18,"ilse":-8,"sera":-5}}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nakkas_plate'),'three_suits','Three suits','Ask Nakka Skarn where the armour came from.','Up close the plate is worse than it looks from a distance: it is three suits, cut for three different men, none of them her size. Two of the three she can account for down to the field they were taken off. The third she cannot, and she says so without being asked twice.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'warlord_hall'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nakkas_plate'),'the_crate_it_came_in','The crate it came in','The stores still have the crate. Go and look at it.','The warren keeps a dry store with a door that still hangs true, and along the back wall of it there are crates that never came off a burned wagon: planed pine, clean straw, opened carefully from the top. The best of the three suits came up the trail in one of them four winters ago, and Nakka was told to take it, and the person who told her was not a goblin.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'warren_stores'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nakkas_plate'),'traced_the_crate','Traced',NULL,'The crate is carter''s work and carters mark their own: three notches on the batten and a route-scar where the strapping bit. It came up the east road, and before the east road it came off a river landing, and the landing it came off is not Rivermark''s, because Rivermark''s quay does not use strapping. That is as far as it goes. Nobody I asked would take it further and two of them stopped talking to me.',NULL,1,'traced_the_crate','success','[{"set_flag":"plate_fate","value":"traced"},{"set_flag":"mark_seen_plate"},{"set_flag":"crate_came_downriver"},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"sera":12,"ilse":10,"aldric":6,"kessa":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nakkas_plate'),'she_took_it_off','She took it off',NULL,'She unbuckled the left pauldron in front of us and handed it over, which took a while, because the straps have been shortened three times. Inside, on the lining plate where nobody would ever look, there is a small clean mark punched into the steel: a plumb-line and a square. She has been wearing it for four years. She asked me what it was. I did not know and I said so, and she said that was the first honest answer she had had off the valley all year.',NULL,1,'she_took_it_off','success','[{"set_flag":"plate_fate","value":"given"},{"set_flag":"mark_seen_plate"},{"give_item":"marked_pauldron","quantity":1},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"ilse":16,"aldric":10,"kessa":4,"sera":6}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nakkas_plate'),'let_it_be','Left buckled',NULL,'She wears three men''s armour and none of it fits and she has kept the helm for the shape it makes in a doorway. I decided that where the third suit came from was her business, and she let me decide that, and looked at me for slightly too long afterwards.',NULL,1,'let_it_be','neutral','[{"set_flag":"plate_fate","value":"unasked"},{"approval":{"kessa":4,"ilse":-6,"sera":-8}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'night_soil'),'find_the_nightman','Find a nightman','Ask the men who go down there what stopped them.','A notice on the Flagon board, in the town clerk''s hand and posted by the council: the emptying of the cesspits and gratings is in arrears and the contractors decline to proceed. Nobody has written down why.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'river_stair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'night_soil'),'into_the_drains','Find the way down','Sib Marrell will not take you. Find your own way in.','Sib Marrell has emptied Rivermark''s pits for twenty years and will not go down this month. He says the gratings are being used. Not blocked — used, from below, by something that moves them and puts them back. He will not go and he will not let his boy go and he does not want the watch told, and he was careful to say all three.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'flagon_cellar'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'night_soil'),'what_is_down_there','Go and see','Find out what is coming up out of the drains.','There is a whole town''s worth of brickwork under Rivermark and it is not empty.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'low_conduit'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'night_soil'),'killed_it','Dead in the conduit',NULL,'There was a crawler in the low conduit, forty feet of it in the wrong shape, and it had been coming up through the gratings after the pit leavings and after anything else that was near them. It is dead in six feet of water under the High Street. The nightmen went back down inside the week. Sib Marrell shook my hand and did not thank me, which from Sib is thanks.',NULL,1,'killed_it','success','[{"set_flag":"night_soil_fate","value":"killed"},{"approval":{"kessa":8,"aldric":4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'night_soil'),'it_was_people','People',NULL,'What has been shifting the gratings is about sixty people who live in the flood tunnels and cannot come up through the gates after dark. They have been coming up the drains because that is the only door they have. I told the council that the tunnels are inhabited, which they knew, and that the nightmen had been frightened by neighbours, which they did not. The nightmen went back down. Nobody has decided what to do about Undertown and I do not think anybody intends to.',NULL,1,'it_was_people','success','[{"set_flag":"night_soil_fate","value":"people"},{"set_flag":"undertown_known"},{"approval":{"ilse":12,"aldric":8,"kessa":2,"sera":-2}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'night_soil'),'bricked_the_gratings','Bricked up',NULL,'Nine gratings on the High Street and Granary Row are bricked and barred and the nightmen work above them in perfect safety. It cost the council eleven gold and took two days. The first hard rain of the autumn came up through the cellars of everything between the market and the quay, because a drain that cannot take water is a wall, and Undertown lost the whole of its eastern side in a night.',NULL,1,'bricked_the_gratings','success','[{"set_flag":"night_soil_fate","value":"sealed"},{"approval":{"sera":4,"ilse":-14,"aldric":-10,"kessa":-4}}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nine_masts'),'count_the_pond','Count the pond','Take a pole and a tally-board out on the mast pond.','Gedda wants the count done again by somebody who is not a shipwright, because every shipwright in this city has a reason to come back with the number she already has.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_mast_pond'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nine_masts'),'the_dry_dock','Where nine masts could go','Nine great pines do not walk. Find out what moved them.','Nine short, and the pond has not been dragged, which means they went out on the surface in front of everybody. There is only one crane in Waerhaven that can lift a mast and only one dock warm enough to work one in.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_dry_dock'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nine_masts'),'the_beam_in_the_masts','The tenth mast','Ask about the beam at the Nine Masts.','Somebody painted a tenth mast on the beam over the fire and nobody will admit to it and nobody will paint it out, and a house of shipwrights does not leave a wrong thing standing over its own hearth for six months by accident.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_nine_masts'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nine_masts'),'found','Nine found',NULL,'They are in the dry dock, under the Drennmark boat, dunnaged and chocked and being shaped. Not stolen. Moved, by shipwrights, at the end of their own shifts, for nothing. Gedda listened to the whole of it without her face doing anything at all.',NULL,1,'found','success','[{"set_flag":"masts_fate","value":"found"},{"set_flag":"tenth_mast_seen"},{"xp":120}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'nine_masts'),'covered','Nine covered',NULL,'I gave the Moot a count of nine short and an honest account of the pond bottom, and left out where they went. The League will be told the pond lost them. Somebody in this city now has nine masts and a year.',NULL,1,'covered','success','[{"set_flag":"masts_fate","value":"covered"},{"set_flag":"tenth_mast_seen"}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_cutters_trove'),'the_rumour','The rumour','Find the workshop the thieves will not go near.','Jimmy Able says there is a cutter''s shop south of the low channel, sealed since the fall, everything still in it. He also says nobody in his gang will go and get it, and he says that part more carefully.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_spider_ante'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_cutters_trove'),'past_the_webs','What is in the way','Get through the webs to the sealed door.','The reason nobody goes: two caves of web between the channel and the door, the first one full of egg-cases and the second one furnished for keeping rather than catching. There is something in the second one considerably larger than the four in the first.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_spider_lair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_cutters_trove'),'opened_the_workshop','The workshop','Take what is worth taking.','Air that had not been breathed in three hundred years came out past us when the door gave. Wheels still clamped to the bench, trays graded rough to fine, a strongbox of old coin underneath, and the finished stones set into the wall plaster at chest height because the ceiling was the thing he did not trust. He was right about the ceiling.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_gem_cutters'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_cutters_trove'),'took_the_trove','Took it',NULL,'All of it, up the stair, past a Watch officer who looked at the weight we were carrying and decided he had questions he would rather not have the answers to.',NULL,1,'took_the_trove','success','[{"set_flag":"oldcity_trove","value":"taken"},{"xp":200}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_cutters_trove'),'left_it_sealed','Left it',NULL,'We put the door back as well as it would go. It is three hundred years of somebody''s working life and it has kept this long; it will keep until somebody comes for it who is not us.',NULL,1,'left_it_sealed','success','[{"set_flag":"oldcity_trove","value":"left"},{"xp":120}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_missing_children'),'ask_the_watch','Ask the Watch','Speak to Officer Bram at the guard house.','Sella Carrow''s daughter Nell went off Cobble Row eleven days ago and is the fourth this month. The Watch keep the only door into the Old City and keep saying they are looking into it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_guardhouse'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_missing_children'),'into_the_dark','Into the dark','Search the Old City for the children.','Bram will not send men past the lit causeways — he has seven and he is not losing any of them in the dark for a fourth time. The door is open to anyone fool enough to use it. Whatever is taking them is off the shored channels.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_drop_hole'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_missing_children'),'found_the_girl','One found','Look for the others, and get them out.','Nell Carrow, alive, in a cupboard-sized cave off the east crawlways with a crack of daylight in the roof. She got out of the pot. She says there are two boys who did not, and that the thing that keeps them has a dog.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_ogres_lair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_missing_children'),'found_the_boys','The pen','Get the boys out of the cave.','A cave off the ledge below the drop hole, a cauldron in the middle of it and a ring of small shoes around that. Two boys behind driven stakes at the back. An ogre in mail and a warg in a collar between them and the way out.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_ogres_lair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_missing_children'),'brought_them_up','Brought them up',NULL,'Three of them up the spiral stair and out into a street full of ordinary noise, which two of them had stopped expecting to hear again. The fourth child was never going to be found; the shoes in the ring outnumber the children anybody has reported missing, and most of those names were never given to the Watch at all.

Sella Carrow paid what she had said she would pay, which was more than she had.',NULL,1,'brought_them_up','success','[{"set_flag":"oldcity_children","value":"all"},{"xp":250},{"give_gold":60}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_missing_children'),'brought_the_girl','Brought the girl up',NULL,'Nell Carrow went up the stair on somebody''s shoulders and her mother did not let go of her for a long time afterward.

The boys are still down there, and everybody standing at the top of that stair knows it, and nobody says so.',NULL,1,'brought_the_girl','success','[{"set_flag":"oldcity_children","value":"girl"},{"xp":120},{"give_gold":30}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_missing_children'),'left_them','Left them',NULL,'You came back up without them and told Sella Carrow so yourself, which was more than the Watch had managed in eleven days. She thanked you for that, which was worse than if she had not.',NULL,1,'left_them','success','[{"set_flag":"oldcity_children","value":"none"},{"xp":40}]',6),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_short_tally'),'read_the_board','The tally board','Look at the Engineers'' tally at the works depot.','Foreman Dessel rules two neat columns, loads in and loads out, and they have not agreed since the spring. The difference goes one way and it goes every week.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_works_depot'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_short_tally'),'follow_the_stone','Where it went','Find who is taking the Works'' stone.','It is not being carried up — the grates are barred and the stair has a guard house at the bottom of it. It is being walled with. Somewhere off the channels there is a block of Old City houses with fresh dressed courses in it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'oldcity_thieves_den'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_short_tally'),'named_them','Named them',NULL,'They have walled themselves in with the Works'' own stone, which is why the block is the only structure down here still standing to two storeys. Dessel took the name, wrote it in the third column he had already ruled and not used, and said he would put it to the Watch in the morning.',NULL,1,'named_them','success','[{"set_flag":"oldcity_tally","value":"named"},{"xp":150}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'oldcity_the_short_tally'),'took_their_price','Took their price',NULL,'Jimmy Able paid, in coin, out of a chest under a pair of floorboards that lift together. Dessel is still eleven weeks short and will go on being short, and the columns will go on disagreeing until somebody who is not us tells him why.',NULL,1,'took_their_price','success','[{"set_flag":"oldcity_tally","value":"bought"},{"xp":80},{"give_gold":75}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'paper_town'),'whose_wages','Who pays the chainman','Ask Alder Pyke who actually pays him.','Pyke draws one and threepence a day at the Rivermark counting house. The counting house is not paying it. It is honouring a note for somebody who is.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'granary_row'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'paper_town'),'the_note','The note of hand','The wages are drawn at the counting house. Go and read what they are drawn on.','The counting house keeps the notes it has honoured for a year before it burns them. Pyke''s are in the tray with the rest, and there will be one with a mark on it instead of a name.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'counting_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'paper_town'),'followed_it','A name, and a river',NULL,'The note is drawn on a house downriver at Greyhythe and signed by its factor, and the factor''s name is Ludo Corse. I have asked eleven people in Rivermark whether they have heard of him. None of them has. Six of them are, one way or another, working for him.',NULL,1,'followed_it','success','[{"set_flag":"paper_town_fate","value":"followed"},{"set_flag":"knows_corse_name"},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"sera":10,"ilse":6,"aldric":4,"kessa":-3}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'paper_town'),'let_it_lie','Somebody''s money',NULL,'Somebody downriver is paying a chainman one and threepence a day to walk lines in a valley they do not live in. That is not a crime, it is not my business, and I have put the tray back where I found it.',NULL,1,'let_it_lie','neutral','[{"set_flag":"paper_town_fate","value":"lie"},{"approval":{"kessa":4,"sera":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'passage_downriver'),'the_second_and_the_fifth','The second and the fifth','Osgar Tull takes the packet down. Find out what it costs and what he carries.','Osgar Tull has taken the packet down on the second and the fifth for nineteen years. He will carry anything that pays, and he will remember everyone he carried, which is a different service and is priced separately.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'packet_stair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'passage_downriver'),'booked_passage','Booked',NULL,'Sixty gold and my name in Tull''s book. He asked whether I wanted the name in it, said the price was the same either way, and wrote what I told him. Downriver the hills give out and the water widens and there is a great deal of country that has never heard of Rivermark. That is where this has been going the whole time.',NULL,1,'booked_passage','success','[{"set_flag":"passage_fate","value":"booked"},{"set_flag":"passage_booked"},{"take_gold":60},{"approval":{"sera":8,"kessa":6}}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'passage_downriver'),'not_yet','Not on this one',NULL,'Tull says the boat goes on the second and the fifth whether I am on it or not, and that in nineteen years he has never once had to persuade anybody twice. I am not finished up here.',NULL,1,'not_yet','neutral','[{"set_flag":"passage_fate","value":"waiting"},{"approval":{"ilse":6,"aldric":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'quarry_pact'),'east_gate','Go east','Get to the quarry and see what is actually down there.','Reed has stopped asking the town council. She wants the warren dealt with, and she is not particular about the verb.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'east_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'quarry_pact'),'the_warren_mouth','The warren mouth','Get past the gate the goblins built in the quarry cut.','They have barricaded the old winding shaft with quarry timber and put a bugbear behind it. They are not raiding from here. They are holding this.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'warren_mouth'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'quarry_pact'),'the_warlords_hall','Nakka Skarn','The warren has a warlord. Decide what she is to you.','The warlord is a goblin called Nakka Skarn, in a suit of human plate that does not fit her. She is not stupid and she is not comfortable. She has three thousand mouths behind her and the deep tunnels are shut. The plate is human-made and does not fit her, and there is a mark punched into the inside of the left pauldron where a smith would put his own: a plumb-bob hanging inside a square. She has no idea it is there. Nobody has ever taken it off her to look.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'warlord_hall'),0,NULL,'success','[{"set_flag":"mark_seen_plate"}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'quarry_pact'),'steel','Steel',NULL,'We took the hall and Nakka Skarn died in the doorway she picked. What was left of the warren went down into the dark or out into the hills. Rivermark is safe. The east gate stays shut at dusk now, and Reed does not ask the council about anything any more.',NULL,1,'steel','success','[{"set_flag":"quarry_fate","value":"steel"},{"set_flag":"warlord_dead"},{"set_flag":"town_standing","value":"safe"},{"set_flag":"reed_absolute"},{"approval":{"kessa":15,"ilse":-25,"aldric":-8,"sera":4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'quarry_pact'),'pact','Pact',NULL,'Nakka took the truce and I took her tooth on a wire, and then we walked Hollis Marrow out onto his own weighing floor and read his own writ back to him in front of the town. Half of Rivermark thinks I sold them. The other half has started trading salt for quarry stone. Both halves are right.',NULL,1,'pact','success','[{"set_flag":"quarry_fate","value":"pact"},{"set_flag":"warren_truce"},{"set_flag":"town_standing","value":"divided"},{"give_item":"truce_token","quantity":1},{"approval":{"ilse":20,"aldric":10,"kessa":-12,"sera":-6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'quarry_pact'),'ash','Ash',NULL,'Marrow paid me to be somewhere else. He was very clear that it was not a bribe, it was a retainer, and that the distinction would matter later. I took the writ and the horses and went west. The smoke was visible for most of the first day.',NULL,1,'ash','neutral','[{"set_flag":"quarry_fate","value":"ash"},{"set_flag":"town_standing","value":"fallen"},{"set_flag":"hollis_coin_taken"},{"give_gold":400},{"give_item":"quarry_writ","quantity":1},{"approval":{"kessa":-20,"aldric":-30,"ilse":-30,"sera":12}}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'rats_and_better'),'the_way_in','Find the way in','Work out how four sacks got into a locked cellar.','Mara has thought about it for a month and has got as far as: it was not the door. There is a gap behind the north wall where the drain goes through, and it is not a gap any more, it is a way, and somebody has been widening it a course of brick at a time for years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'flagon_cellar'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'rats_and_better'),'the_grain_stair','The grain stair','Follow it back to wherever the grain comes down.','A brick stair under Granary Row up to a loading hatch, swept cleaner than anywhere else in Undertown. Grain comes down here in quantity and goes out along the conduit into half the cellars between the market and the quay, and none of it has crossed the weighing floor. It is not theft from the granary. The granary is where it starts. It is a way of moving grain in this town without any of it being weighed, taxed, tallied or seen.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'grain_stair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'rats_and_better'),'shut_the_route','Shut',NULL,'Two days'' work and eleven gold of brick and the hatch is a wall and the gap behind Mara''s north wall is a wall. Nothing comes down the grain stair now. Nothing came down it to Undertown either, and that turned out to be a great deal of what Undertown had been eating, which nobody mentioned to me while I was laying the brick.',NULL,1,'shut_the_route','success','[{"set_flag":"grain_route_fate","value":"shut"},{"pressure":2},{"approval":{"aldric":6,"sera":4,"ilse":-10,"kessa":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'rats_and_better'),'told_the_watch','The watch takes the stair',NULL,'Reed put four men on the hatch for a fortnight and took nine people at the bottom of it, and every one of the nine lives in the tunnels and was carrying somebody else''s grain for a cut of it. They are in the lockup. The granary''s books show nothing, because the granary''s books were never the point, and the man whose hatch it is has an excellent explanation involving a former employee. Reed knows exactly what she has caught and exactly what she has not.',NULL,1,'told_the_watch','success','[{"set_flag":"grain_route_fate","value":"watch"},{"approval":{"aldric":8,"ilse":-12,"kessa":-8,"sera":-2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'rats_and_better'),'kept_the_route','Kept open',NULL,'The route stays. Undertown goes on eating and I take eighty gold a season for making sure the hatch is not looked at, which I arranged with Aggie Slate in about six minutes and with Mara in rather longer. Mara''s four sacks stop. Everybody at this table is better off and I have become one of the reasons nothing in this town gets weighed.',NULL,1,'kept_the_route','success','[{"set_flag":"grain_route_fate","value":"kept"},{"give_gold":80},{"approval":{"ilse":6,"kessa":8,"sera":6,"aldric":-10}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'root_and_ash'),'find_the_root','Find fen-root','Osric wants a hand of fen-root. Find where one can be got.','Fen-root grows in one place within forty miles and Osric Fen will not name the place out loud, only the plant. He wants a hand of it. He has money ready in a dish on the counter, counted out, and has plainly had it counted out for some time.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'root_ash'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'root_and_ash'),'the_quay_dealer','The quay','What does not walk out of the fen comes up the river. Ask at the stair.','Mott Wenn says a boat comes up from the low water four or five times a year with fen goods and that the men on it do not come further than the bottom step. Dried fen-root is on it. It is four times the price it should be, and that price is not about the root: it is about who is willing to go and cut it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'river_stair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'root_and_ash'),'bought_it_up','Bought at the bottom step',NULL,'A hundred gold for a hand of black root tied with grass, which is robbery, and Osric paid me back thirty of it and looked ashamed of the shortfall. He put it straight into the mortar. He did not tell me what it was for and I did not push, and that is where it stands.',NULL,1,'bought_it_up','success','[{"set_flag":"root_and_ash_fate","value":"bought"},{"take_gold":100},{"approval":{"aldric":4,"sera":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'root_and_ash'),'he_said_why','He said why',NULL,'Osric Fen is not from Rivermark. He is from the village under the water in the Hollow Fen, and he was nine when the sluice went, and his people are still there in the sense that they were never taken out. Fen-root only grows where there is bone in the silt. He has made the same remedy every year for thirty-one years and given it away for nothing, and he will not go and cut the root himself because he knows exactly what he would be standing on.',NULL,1,'he_said_why','success','[{"set_flag":"root_and_ash_fate","value":"told"},{"set_flag":"osric_told"},{"give_item":"dried_fen_root","quantity":1},{"approval":{"aldric":10,"ilse":10,"kessa":4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'root_and_ash'),'left_it_unmade','Not made this year',NULL,'I left it. Osric took the money off the counter and put it back in the drawer, which he did without any expression at all, and that was the end of it. The remedy is a winter cough draught that he has given away free every year since before I was born. Wyke''s list has nine children on it this year.',NULL,1,'left_it_unmade','neutral','[{"set_flag":"root_and_ash_fate","value":"unmade"},{"approval":{"aldric":-10,"ilse":-6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'salt_and_silence'),'the_laced_sheets','The laced sheets','Find out what Hesk Dray is carrying and why he is camped the wrong way round.','Hesk Dray runs six wagons on four routes and has never had a complaint. Two of his wagons are standing on the caravan ground with the sheets laced instead of tied, and his men have put themselves between the load and the road rather than round the fire.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'caravan_ground'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'salt_and_silence'),'under_the_salt','Under the salt','Get a wagon open, one way or another.','Salt on top, to the depth of a forearm, because salt is what a searcher stops at. Under the salt: bar iron in bundles of ten, tied with wire. That is not a trade good. That is a specification.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'caravan_ground'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'salt_and_silence'),'opened_the_wagons','Opened on the ground',NULL,'We had the sheets off in front of his own carters and made him say what was under the salt out loud, with them standing there. He said it. Four of the six walked off the job before dawn. The iron is still on the ground at the caravan stand and nobody has come for it.',NULL,1,'opened_the_wagons','success','[{"set_flag":"salt_fate","value":"opened"},{"set_flag":"salt_iron_exposed"},{"pressure":2},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"aldric":12,"kessa":6,"sera":-6,"ilse":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'salt_and_silence'),'walked_it_up','Walked it up',NULL,'We let him run and walked the wagons up with him to see who took delivery. The delivery was taken at the warren gate at four in the morning by two goblins with a slate and a tally, who counted the bundles, signed nothing, and gave Hesk a token to carry back. Salt and iron, a quarter of the load. Somebody has been paying that price for four years and it is not Hesk.',NULL,1,'walked_it_up','success','[{"set_flag":"salt_fate","value":"followed"},{"set_flag":"salt_iron_exposed"},{"set_flag":"knows_paymaster"},{"pressure":2},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"ilse":14,"sera":8,"aldric":-2,"kessa":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'salt_and_silence'),'took_the_silence','Paid to look elsewhere',NULL,'Hesk paid us out of a purse he had ready before we arrived, which tells you he has been expecting somebody for a while and has costed us in. The wagons went up the trail at first light. I do not know what they were carrying and I have written down that I do not know.',NULL,1,'took_the_silence','neutral','[{"set_flag":"salt_fate","value":"paid"},{"give_gold":200},{"approval":{"sera":10,"kessa":2,"aldric":-14,"ilse":-10}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_leash'),'the_second_book','The book in the loft','There is a second ledger in the granary loft, in Sera''s hand, and it is the one that matters.','Marrow keeps a second book. Everything false in the mill''s accounts is written out fair in it, in Sera''s hand, dated and initialled. It is not evidence against him. It is a rope with her name on it. Sera says there is a stamp in the corner of every page of it that is not in her hand — a plumb-bob hanging inside a square — and that she asked once what it was and was told to get on.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'high_street'),0,NULL,'success','[{"set_flag":"mark_seen_book"}]',0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_leash'),'the_loft_stair','The loft stair','Get into the granary loft without Marrow''s people counting you in.','The loft stair is inside the weighing floor and the weighing floor has a man on it from dawn. Sera says the grain hatch on the north side has not been oiled since her father''s time, which is the closest she comes to volunteering.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'granary_row'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_leash'),'cut_the_leash','The leash cut',NULL,'We took the second book out of the loft and put it in the weighing-floor furnace, and Sera stood there until the boards of it went. She is not grateful. She is something more useful than grateful — she is out of reasons to lie to me.',NULL,1,'cut_the_leash','success','[{"set_flag":"sera_leash_fate","value":"cut"},{"approval":{"sera":25,"aldric":4,"kessa":2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_leash'),'held_the_leash','The leash, in my hand',NULL,'I took the second book and I kept it. Sera understood the arrangement before I had finished explaining it, which tells you how many times it has been explained to her. She does exactly what she is told now. She is never going to sleep in a room I am in.',NULL,1,'held_the_leash','success','[{"set_flag":"sera_leash_fate","value":"held"},{"give_item":"the_ledger","quantity":1},{"approval":{"sera":-20,"aldric":-20,"ilse":-12,"kessa":-8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_what_she_is_for'),'the_letter','The letter at the Flagon','Sera has been offered a post. She has never asked anybody what to do and she is asking.','A letter came for Sera at the Golden Flagon — for her, by name, at an inn she has slept at eleven times. Clerk of accounts at the landing at Greyhythe: forty gold a year, a room over the counting-floor, a twenty-gold bond returned at the year''s end, and a line at the bottom saying that neither the house nor any officer of it may require of the clerk any account, entry or copy other than the true one. Nobody signed it. It carries a seal in black wax, a plumb and a square cut small like a mason''s, which is a strange thing for a counting-house to put on its post. Sera says she has seen it before and cannot tell me where, and that this is not a sentence she has ever had to say.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'flagon_common_room'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_what_she_is_for'),'she_took_the_post','Downriver on the tide',NULL,'She took it. It was the best offer she has ever had and it was the one that was best for her, and she costed the alternative before she went and told me I had not said the cheap one. She left the dockets behind — seventy-one of them, counted, with the shut weeks marked in the margin and a note on the front saying which four matter. She was an hour early for the boat.',NULL,1,'she_took_the_post','success','[{"set_flag":"sera_post_fate","value":"took"},{"companion_leaves":"sera"},{"approval":{"aldric":6,"ilse":4,"kessa":-2}}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_what_she_is_for'),'she_stayed','She stayed',NULL,'She stayed. She keeps the figure current the way she used to keep the other one — forty gold a year, a room, and a bond — except that it has stopped being what she is worth and started being what she turned down, and she says those are very different columns and she did not expect to prefer the second one.',NULL,1,'she_stayed','success','[{"set_flag":"sera_post_fate","value":"stayed"},{"approval":{"sera":20,"kessa":4,"aldric":2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'sera_what_she_is_for'),'she_took_the_retainer','Eight lines on the first of the month',NULL,'She wrote back and took a retainer, and stayed. Eight gold a month for eight lines a month: where we have been, what we were paid, and who we spoke to. She reads every account aloud before it is sealed and says the arrangement starts immediately or not at all. She did not take it for the eight gold. She took it to be on the inside of somebody''s post, and she says that when they stop paying her they will start paying somebody else in this valley, and that a man who has just started being paid buys a coat.',NULL,1,'she_took_the_retainer','success','[{"set_flag":"sera_post_fate","value":"retained"},{"approval":{"sera":12,"kessa":-6,"aldric":-6,"ilse":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'stone_and_writ'),'the_fourth_face','The fourth face','Look at what has been cut into the mearing stone this year.','Where four holdings meet there is a stone with four faces. Three are worn nearly smooth. The fourth has been dressed back and re-cut this year with a proper mason''s chisel, and what is on it now is not a crozier, a ploughshare or a tower.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'boundary_stone'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'stone_and_writ'),'whose_name_is_on_it','Whose name is on it','Find out who holds the quarry writ now, and who held it in spring.','The writ went from the town, to a grain factor, to a name nobody at the counting house recognises, inside seven months. Each transfer is lawful and each one was cheap. The last one was not paid for in coin — it was paid for by taking on a debt that was already owed.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'quarrymans_hut'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'stone_and_writ'),'filed_the_copy','Filed',NULL,'I took a rubbing of the new face and a copy of the transfers down to the counting house and had both entered in the town''s own book with a date on them. It changes nothing about who owns the quarry. It means that in ten years, when somebody asks when it stopped being Rivermark''s, there will be an answer.',NULL,1,'filed_the_copy','success','[{"set_flag":"quarry_writ_fate","value":"filed"},{"set_flag":"mark_seen_writ"},{"give_item":"mearing_rubbing","quantity":1},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"sera":12,"aldric":6,"ilse":4,"kessa":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'stone_and_writ'),'cut_the_stone_back','The stone, re-cut',NULL,'We put the old mearing back on the fourth face with a borrowed chisel and a bad hand, and it looks like what it is: a repair. The ground now says one thing and the paper says another, and every boundary case in the valley for the next hundred years will start with an argument about which of them is lying.',NULL,1,'cut_the_stone_back','success','[{"set_flag":"quarry_writ_fate","value":"stone"},{"set_flag":"mark_seen_writ"},{"set_flag":"mearing_recut"},{"pressure":2},{"approval":{"kessa":12,"ilse":8,"sera":-12,"aldric":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'stone_and_writ'),'sold_the_reading','Sold',NULL,'A man came up the road two days later and asked, politely, what we had found on the stone, and paid for the answer without haggling, which is how I know I undercharged. He wrote nothing down. He thanked me by name.',NULL,1,'sold_the_reading','neutral','[{"set_flag":"quarry_writ_fate","value":"sold"},{"set_flag":"mark_seen_writ"},{"set_flag":"sold_to_the_polite_man"},{"give_gold":250},{"approval":{"sera":10,"kessa":-8,"ilse":-14,"aldric":-16}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'teeth_in_the_hills'),'walk_the_road','Walk the east road','Find where the raids happen and what they take.','Reed wants the east road made safe. Four caravans in six weeks, all inside two miles of the quarry cut.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'quarry_road'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'teeth_in_the_hills'),'find_the_warden','Find the hill warden','Somebody watches these hills for a living. Find her.','There is a warden in the eastern hills. Tobin says she comes in for salt and leaves before dark, and that she knows the ground better than the watch does.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'wardens_camp'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'teeth_in_the_hills'),'the_pattern','Count the wagons','Work out which caravans get hit, and which do not.','The raids are not random. Every wagon that was hit carried grain contracted to the Rivermark granary. Every wagon that got through carried anything else. The gear the raiders left in the cut is not goblin work. A jack, a helm and two shoulder-plates, all human-made, and all four punched on the inside with the same stamp: a plumb-bob hanging inside a square.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'broken_hills'),0,NULL,'success','[{"set_flag":"mark_seen_plate"}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'teeth_in_the_hills'),'ambushed_the_raiders','The road, taken back',NULL,'We set on the raiding party in the cut and left none of them standing. The road is quiet. The warren now knows exactly how many of us there are and what we did to the ones who came out.',NULL,1,'ambushed_the_raiders','success','[{"set_flag":"hills_fate","value":"ambush"},{"approval":{"kessa":12,"aldric":-4,"ilse":-14}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'teeth_in_the_hills'),'escorted_the_caravan','One wagon through',NULL,'We walked the next grain wagon through the cut ourselves. The raiders came for it, saw us, and went back up the slope — which told me the thing I wanted. They were sent for that wagon. Somebody in Rivermark told them which one it was.',NULL,1,'escorted_the_caravan','success','[{"set_flag":"hills_fate","value":"escort"},{"set_flag":"hills_pattern"},{"set_flag":"caravan_saved"},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"aldric":10,"ilse":8,"sera":-4,"kessa":-2}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'teeth_in_the_hills'),'turned_the_road','The road moved',NULL,'We had the carters take the northern ford instead. Nothing has been raided since. Nothing has come down out of the hills either, and the warren has been eating its own stores for eleven days.',NULL,1,'turned_the_road','success','[{"set_flag":"hills_fate","value":"reroute"},{"set_flag":"hills_pattern"},{"approval":{"sera":8,"kessa":-8,"ilse":-6,"aldric":2}}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_almoners_list'),'read_the_list','Read the list','Get Wyke to let you look at who he is feeding.','Eighty-one names on the parish dole. Forty of them were added in the last eight months, and thirty-six of those gave a holding west of the river as their last address. A bad year takes the weakest farms first, in no particular order. This is not in no particular order.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'high_street'),0,NULL,'success','[{"give_item":"almoners_list","quantity":1}]',0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_almoners_list'),'the_west_gate','Ask who came in','Somebody watched them walk into town. Find him.','Serjeant Ballow has kept the west gate four years and has watched every one of them come in. They came in families, in daylight, with their tools, which is not how people leave a farm that has failed — that is done at night, with nothing. Every one of them had sold. None of them will say to whom, and Ballow has stopped asking because of how they look at him when he does.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'west_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_almoners_list'),'fed_them','The dole holds',NULL,'I put seventy-five gold into the parish box, which is more than it has held at one time in Wyke''s life, and it will feed eighty-one people until about the middle of winter. Wyke wrote my name in the front of the book. He also said, without any edge on it at all, that he would need the same again in the spring and rather more the spring after.',NULL,1,'fed_them','success','[{"set_flag":"almoner_list_fate","value":"fed"},{"take_gold":75},{"take_item":"almoners_list"},{"approval":{"aldric":12,"ilse":4,"kessa":4,"sera":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_almoners_list'),'named_the_pattern','On the record',NULL,'I took the list to Reed and she read it twice and copied the thirty-six names into the watch day book with the date, which is the only power she actually has. Nothing is illegal. A man may sell his land and a man may buy it. It is written down now, in the town''s own hand, which is worth exactly nothing this year and may be worth a great deal later.',NULL,1,'named_the_pattern','success','[{"set_flag":"almoner_list_fate","value":"recorded"},{"set_flag":"west_holdings_recorded"},{"pressure":1},{"take_item":"almoners_list"},{"approval":{"ilse":10,"aldric":6,"sera":4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_almoners_list'),'found_them_work','Work, of a kind',NULL,'I got twenty-two of them taken on as labour — the granary, the quay, the stone yard. They eat. They are also, all of them, now men who work for wages in a town where they used to own four acres and a roof, and that is not a thing that reverses. Wyke crossed twenty-two names off his list and did not look pleased about it.',NULL,1,'found_them_work','success','[{"set_flag":"almoner_list_fate","value":"work"},{"take_item":"almoners_list"},{"approval":{"sera":8,"kessa":5,"aldric":-4,"ilse":-8}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_anvil_debt'),'see_the_paper','Look at what she signed','Get Brenna to show you the note.','Brenna Coalwright pays forty gold a quarter against a loan she took out on the forge in the fourth year of the road tax. She has never met the man who takes it. She is two days from the next quarter and eleven gold short.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_anvil'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_anvil_debt'),'the_assignments','Follow the assignments','The note has been sold on four times. Find out to whom.','The back of the note carries four assignments in four hands. Old Halloway sold it to a corn factor, who sold it to a man in Greyhythe, who sold it on again. The fourth entry is the interesting one: it is a house, not a person, and it is not witnessed.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'counting_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_anvil_debt'),'paid_the_note','The quarter is paid',NULL,'I put forty gold on Brenna''s counter and she took it standing very straight and did not thank me until I was halfway out of the door. The note stands. The next quarter is in twelve weeks and she knows exactly how many days that is.',NULL,1,'paid_the_note','success','[{"set_flag":"anvil_debt_fate","value":"paid"},{"take_gold":40},{"approval":{"kessa":8,"aldric":6,"sera":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_anvil_debt'),'voided_the_note','The fourth assignment is nothing',NULL,'The last sale of the note was never witnessed. Tibald Ashe read it twice, said so out loud in front of two clerks so that it would be heard, and struck it. The debt still exists. It belongs to a corn factor in Greyhythe who has been dead since the winter and whose estate will take years to find it. Brenna gets those years.',NULL,1,'voided_the_note','success','[{"set_flag":"anvil_debt_fate","value":"void"},{"set_flag":"ashe_helped"},{"pressure":1},{"approval":{"sera":10,"kessa":8,"ilse":4,"aldric":-2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_anvil_debt'),'bought_the_note','The note changes hands again',NULL,'I bought the paper. A hundred and twenty gold to a clerk who was pleased to be rid of a small account a long way from home. Brenna''s forge is mortgaged to me now. She said thank you. She said it the way you say it to a man who has just bought your house.',NULL,1,'bought_the_note','success','[{"set_flag":"anvil_debt_fate","value":"bought"},{"take_gold":120},{"give_item":"anvil_note","quantity":1},{"approval":{"kessa":-12,"aldric":-6,"ilse":-4,"sera":8}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_anvil_debt'),'let_it_stand','Her debt, her forge',NULL,'I left it. It is a real debt, honestly contracted and lawfully sold, and none of my business. Brenna made the quarter by selling the good steel out from under her own counter, which is how a smithy stops being a smithy over about four years.',NULL,1,'let_it_stand','neutral','[{"set_flag":"anvil_debt_fate","value":"stands"},{"approval":{"kessa":-8,"aldric":-4}}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_beam'),'the_drawing','The drawing','Get Doren to show you what he has been drawing for two years.','He carries it rolled inside his coat and has done since before I met him, and he unrolls it at the ropewalk, which is the only place in this city where nobody can come up behind you.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_ropehouse'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_beam'),'the_tenth','Under the beam','Decide what happens to the tenth mast.','It is a hull for ice. Double-framed forward, sheathed to the wale, short and deep, and drawn by somebody who has read three stolen charts of a shore the Charthouse has stopped admitting is there. He has not asked anyone for permission for any part of it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_nine_masts'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_beam'),'owned','Owned',NULL,'He stood up under the beam in front of the whole house and said he painted it, and said why, and put the drawing on the table. Gedda Halloway looked at it for a very long time and then asked him one question about the garboard, which is how a master shipwright says yes.',NULL,1,'owned','success','[{"set_flag":"doren_fate","value":"owned"},{"approval":{"doren_ferrow":15}},{"give_item":"the_tenth_hull","quantity":1}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_beam'),'painted_out','Painted out',NULL,'He painted it out himself, at night, with the same brush, and kept the drawing. He says it was the right thing and he is right, and he has not looked up at that beam once since, and he used to look at it every time he came through the door.',NULL,1,'painted_out','success','[{"set_flag":"doren_fate","value":"painted_out"},{"approval":{"doren_ferrow":8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_bottom_of_the_warren'),'the_hollow_gallery','The hollow gallery','Get down to the lowest gallery the warren still holds.','Below the shaft there is one more level and the goblins are propping it. The floor rings hollow for the whole width of the gallery, which means there is a void under a floor that was cut solid.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'broken_floor'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_bottom_of_the_warren'),'the_edge_is_cut','The edge is cut','Look at the edge of the hole.','Thirty feet across, and every foot of the rim is dressed. Stone that falls breaks along its bedding and leaves a shelf. This does not have a shelf. Somebody took this floor out from underneath, working upward, and stopped when they came through.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'broken_floor'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_bottom_of_the_warren'),'sounded_the_floor','Sounded',NULL,'We went down on the goblins'' rope as far as the first landing and there is a landing, which is the part that has stayed with me. Not a cave. A landing, cut square, with a stair going down off it and the stair swept. There is air moving up it and the air is warm and it smells of lamp-oil and rock dust. We came back up. The rope is still there.',NULL,1,'sounded_the_floor','success','[{"set_flag":"warren_floor_fate","value":"sounded"},{"set_flag":"deepworks_found"},{"set_flag":"deep_known"},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"ilse":16,"sera":8,"kessa":6,"aldric":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_bottom_of_the_warren'),'shored_it','Shored',NULL,'We spent two days on it with the warren''s own timber and a great deal of advice from goblins who have been mining longer than Rivermark has been a town. The gallery will hold now, which buys them the level, which buys them the winter. It also means nothing else comes up through it, and the rope is on our side of the hole.',NULL,1,'shored_it','success','[{"set_flag":"warren_floor_fate","value":"shored"},{"set_flag":"deepworks_found"},{"set_flag":"broken_floor_shored"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"ilse":18,"aldric":12,"kessa":8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_bottom_of_the_warren'),'let_it_go','Left propped',NULL,'Eleven props holding up a floor with a hole in it, and it is not our floor. We came back up and told Nakka what we had seen from the edge, which was: a great deal of nothing, moving air, and an edge cut square. She said thank you, which she does not often do, and went back to counting days on a slate.',NULL,1,'let_it_go','neutral','[{"set_flag":"warren_floor_fate","value":"abandoned"},{"set_flag":"deepworks_found"},{"approval":{"kessa":2,"ilse":-4,"sera":-6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_burnt_mill'),'go_and_look','Go and look','Walk out to the mill on the ford road and see what is actually there.','The mill is a fact in every conversation in Rivermark and nobody has walked the two miles. Three walls, a wheel-pit full of black water, and a race that still runs perfectly well past a building that has not needed it in four years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'mill_ruin'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_burnt_mill'),'the_counting_loft','Where it started','Work out where the fire began.','Every charred beam-end in the wall points inward. A kiln fire spreads out from the kiln and takes the floor above it; this one started high on the river side, in the counting loft, where the mill kept its paper and no fire was ever lit.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'mill_ruin'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_burnt_mill'),'found_the_cause','It started in the loft',NULL,'It started in the counting loft, on the river side, where the mill kept its books and nobody ever struck a light. The stones are scorched in a corner that had no lamp, no flue and no reason. I have written it down. It does not tell me who, and I have stopped expecting it to.',NULL,1,'found_the_cause','success','[{"set_flag":"mill_fate","value":"cause"},{"set_flag":"mill_fire_was_set"},{"pressure":1},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"sera":10,"aldric":6,"ilse":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_burnt_mill'),'made_it_a_shelter','A roof on the road',NULL,'We cleared the roof-fall out of the south end, put hurdles across the gap and a slate over the fire-back, and told the drovers at the fold that there was a dry wall two miles up the road. Four of them used it inside a week. It is not an answer to anything. It is a room.',NULL,1,'made_it_a_shelter','success','[{"set_flag":"mill_fate","value":"shelter"},{"set_flag":"mill_is_shelter"},{"approval":{"aldric":14,"kessa":6,"ilse":6,"sera":-2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_burnt_mill'),'left_the_mill','Left standing',NULL,'Three walls and running water. I went out, I looked, I came back, and I am now one more person in Rivermark who can say that the mill burned.',NULL,1,'left_the_mill','neutral','[{"set_flag":"mill_fate","value":"left"}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_carters_cellar'),'go_down','Down the trap','Find out what has been getting into the cellar.','Hesta says she is losing a barrel a week and it is not the carters. There is a drain in the cellar the width of a man''s shoulders and she has stopped going down alone.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_rest_cellar'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_carters_cellar'),'the_drain','The grate has been moved','Look at the drain properly.','The rats came up the drain, which is what rats do. What rats do not do is lift a grate that has been mortared in for thirty years and set it back down square.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_rest_cellar'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_carters_cellar'),'cleared','Dealt with',NULL,'Killed, cleared, and the grate wedged with a baulk of pine. Hesta paid out of the till and did not ask me what I thought about the mortar, and I did not tell her.',NULL,1,'cleared','success','[{"set_flag":"cellar_cleared"}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_carters_cellar'),'the_way_in_found','There is a way under the city',NULL,'The drain is not a drain. It runs twenty feet and drops into a cut stair under the outer quay, and there is a line hung on iron rings at the turn of it, and the line is dry, and it is used. Half of Waerhaven is standing on a floor that somebody else is walking about under.',NULL,1,'found_the_way','success','[{"set_flag":"cellar_cleared"},{"set_flag":"underquay_known"},{"give_item":"ropewalk_line","quantity":1},{"xp":80}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_dig'),'get_counted','Nobody stops anybody','There is no gate and no guard. Work out what is doing the job instead.','There is no gate on the Deepworks and nobody on the stair. What there is, is a bell, a painted line, and a board with a hundred numbered pegs in it. You are not kept out of this place. You are kept accounted for inside it, which turns out to work better.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'muster_yard'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_dig'),'the_board','The board of pegs','Wenna Coyle keeps the pegs and the hours. Get a number, or explain why you have not got one.','The timekeeper''s hut is warm, dry and better lit than anywhere else down here, and its window faces the muster line, and the window was positioned. Wenna Coyle can tell you where any one of two hundred people was standing at any hour of the last three years, and considers that an ordinary thing to be able to do.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'timekeepers_hut'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_dig'),'signed_on','Peg one hundred and four',NULL,'I am peg one hundred and four. I gave a name, was not asked for a second one, and was issued a lamp against the number. Nobody down here has looked at me since. Being counted is the same as being invisible, and it cost me nothing, and that is exactly how they get two hundred of us.',NULL,1,'signed_on','success','[{"set_flag":"dig_fate","value":"signed"},{"set_flag":"counted_in"},{"give_item":"deepworks_lamp","quantity":1},{"approval":{"sera":10,"ilse":4,"kessa":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_dig'),'walked_in_unasked','Uncounted',NULL,'I did not give a name and I did not take a peg, and Coyle wrote that down too, on a separate sheet, in the same hand. She was not annoyed. She said the works have a column for everything and it is better for everybody if the thing is in the right column.',NULL,1,'walked_in_unasked','success','[{"set_flag":"dig_fate","value":"unasked"},{"set_flag":"coyle_noted_us"},{"pressure":1},{"approval":{"kessa":8,"ilse":6,"sera":-6}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_dig'),'never_counted','Out before the bell',NULL,'I went back up the stair before the bell went. Whatever the works are, they are not a thing you find out by standing in the doorway of, and I have stood in the doorway of it twice now.',NULL,1,'never_counted','neutral','[{"set_flag":"dig_fate","value":"never"}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drovers_road'),'take_the_work','Take the work','Find Tull Barrow at the fold and take the escort.','Tull Barrow wants four swords for two days to walk sixty head from the fold to the fen road head. It is ordinary work at an ordinary price and there is no reason at all for him to be paying it, because nobody robs cattle: they are slow, loud, and impossible to sell twice.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'drovers_rest'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drovers_road'),'where_the_drove_is_going','Where the drove is going','Work out where sixty head are actually being walked to, and why.','The market is east. We are going west. Barrow is walking his whole herd out of the valley and not coming back, because the common grazing on Winter Field was bought in the spring by somebody who has not fenced it, stocked it, or come to look at it, and who has simply stopped renewing the commoners'' rights one name at a time as they fall due.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'fen_road_head'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drovers_road'),'walked_them_out','Walked out',NULL,'We walked them to the fen road head and Nesh Gray''s people took them across the causeway in three lots, which is a thing I did not know could be done and would rather not have watched. Barrow paid us at the horn-post and shook hands and went west. He is the fourth this year. Nobody in Rivermark has counted.',NULL,1,'walked_them_out','success','[{"set_flag":"drove_fate","value":"out"},{"set_flag":"grazing_bought_known"},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"sera":6,"kessa":4,"ilse":-8,"aldric":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drovers_road'),'turned_them_back','Turned east',NULL,'We turned the drove round at the fen road head and walked it into Rivermark market instead, which took a day longer and cost him the price he had been promised for them on the other side. He got a worse price and a hearing at the town''s own weighing floor, and by dusk there were three other holders in the room asking who had bought the common and when. That is not a victory. It is a room full of people who now know.',NULL,1,'turned_them_back','success','[{"set_flag":"drove_fate","value":"back"},{"set_flag":"grazing_bought_known"},{"set_flag":"commons_question_raised"},{"pressure":1},{"xp":120},{"approval":{"ilse":14,"aldric":10,"sera":-6,"kessa":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drovers_road'),'lost_the_drove','Lost on the field',NULL,'It went wrong at the thorn brake on Winter Field in the dark and we lost eleven head and both of the far dogs, and after that the herd would not be held. Barrow did not blame anybody. He counted what was left twice, said the number out loud, and started walking. He is not going to make the crossing with what he has.',NULL,1,'lost_the_drove','failure','[{"set_flag":"drove_fate","value":"lost"},{"approval":{"kessa":-6,"ilse":-6,"aldric":-4,"sera":-4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drowned_village'),'eleven_roofs','Eleven roofs','Get out to the village in the fen and look at it properly.','It is not a ruin. It is a village that was emptied, room by room, with time to spare, and then flooded. There is no furniture in any of the houses and no pots in any of the hearths.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'drowned_village'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drowned_village'),'the_chapel','The chapel','The chapel has a stone roof and something on the chancel step. Get to it.','The only building with a stone roof, and the only one with an inside. The water in the nave stops a hand''s width below the third step, and it has stopped there for forty years. There is a chest on the fourth step, which is dry. Somebody worked out where the water would stand before they carried it up there — which means somebody knew, in advance, how deep it was going to be.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'drowned_chapel'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drowned_village'),'raised_the_names','The village has a name',NULL,'The chest holds the parish register: baptisms, marriages and burials for a hundred and ninety years, dry, in order, and legible. The village was called Ashlade. Two hundred and six people were living in it the year it went under and every one of them is in the book. There is no burial entry for any of them, because they did not die. They were moved, and then the sluice was opened.',NULL,1,'raised_the_names','success','[{"set_flag":"village_fate","value":"named"},{"set_flag":"ashlade_named"},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"aldric":16,"ilse":10,"sera":8}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drowned_village'),'cleared_the_nave','The nave, cleared',NULL,'Forty years of standing black water in a stone room, and something in it that peat had kept in better condition than it had any business being in. It is down. The nave is a nave again. It is also, now, a room with a chest in it and nothing to stop anyone taking the chest, and I have thought about that more than once since.',NULL,1,'cleared_the_nave','success','[{"set_flag":"village_fate","value":"cleared"},{"set_flag":"drowned_nave_clear"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"kessa":12,"aldric":6,"ilse":4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_drowned_village'),'left_it_under','Left under',NULL,'Eleven roofs, two rows and a street. I did not go into the chapel. I have thought about the chest on the fourth step several times since and I have not gone back.',NULL,1,'left_it_under','neutral','[{"set_flag":"village_fate","value":"under"}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_factors_house'),'the_front_room','The front room','Corse keeps his own house and answers his own door. Go in.','The step is washed and the door is answered. Nothing in the hall is expensive and nothing in it is cheap. There is one desk facing the window so that whoever sits at it can watch the landing and be watched doing it, and one chair on the other side, worn through at the arms.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'factors_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_factors_house'),'the_long_room','The long room','The whole back of the house is paper, and the door to it is not locked.','Presses to the ceiling, every drawer labelled by year and by hundred in one hand, a lamp on a gimbal so it can be carried without being set down. The Concern keeps everything it knows in this room and the room is not locked, and I have stood in it for ten minutes working out why that frightens me more than a lock would.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_long_room'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_factors_house'),'asked_him_home','The whole conversation',NULL,'I asked him the questions in his own house with his own lamp lit and he answered all of them and offered me the run of the long room while he went to see about supper. He is not careless. He has simply never once met a person who could hurt him with a fact, and he has met a great many people.',NULL,1,'asked_him_home','success','[{"set_flag":"factors_house_fate","value":"asked"},{"set_flag":"long_room_open"},{"pressure":2},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"sera":14,"aldric":6,"ilse":6,"kessa":-6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_factors_house'),'walked_out','Out into the street',NULL,'I got as far as the front room, took the chair, and could not stay in it. He came to the door with me and told me to come back when I had something to ask, and to eat first, and he meant both.',NULL,1,'walked_out','neutral','[{"set_flag":"factors_house_fate","value":"out"},{"approval":{"kessa":4,"sera":-6}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_fen_wardens'),'the_stilt_camp','The stilt camp','Get into the camp without the planks coming up.','Nesh Gray''s camp is six platforms and about a dozen people, and every plank walk between them can be pulled up in four seconds. They have practised that against the watch. They watched us come the whole way in.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'stilt_camp'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_fen_wardens'),'one_run','One run','Gray will show you the work if you do a night of it. Do a night of it.','The run goes west across the black pools by punt at two in the morning: salt out, wool out, iron in, and a fifth of everything left at the fen road head for whoever is walking out of the valley that week with more than they can carry. They mend the causeway themselves, out of the takings, because there is nobody to ask and it is the road they live on.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'black_pools'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_fen_wardens'),'ran_with_them','Ran with them',NULL,'One night, two punts and eleven miles of water, and I have never been so cold or so useless. What crosses the fen is not what Rivermark thinks crosses the fen: it is people. Four families this month, walking west with what they could carry, off ground that was bought out from under them. Gray does not charge those. She charges the salt to pay for them.',NULL,1,'ran_with_them','success','[{"set_flag":"wardens_fate","value":"ran"},{"set_flag":"fen_road_known"},{"set_flag":"grazing_bought_known"},{"give_item":"fen_waders","quantity":1},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"ilse":16,"kessa":10,"aldric":6,"sera":-6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_fen_wardens'),'turned_them_in','Turned in',NULL,'Reed took the camp in the second week of the month with eleven of the watch and two boats borrowed from the quay, and it went cleanly, and she was pleased with it. The fen road has had nothing spent on it since. Eleven weeks later the causeway is under at four points and the west of the valley is a place you cannot get to.',NULL,1,'turned_them_in','success','[{"set_flag":"wardens_fate","value":"turned"},{"set_flag":"fen_road_closing"},{"give_gold":250},{"approval":{"sera":6,"kessa":-8,"ilse":-18,"aldric":-10}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_fen_wardens'),'bought_the_road','The road, bought',NULL,'We paid the season''s toll for the causeway in one payment, on Rivermark''s behalf and mostly out of our own purse, and had it agreed in front of both camps that the fen road is open to anyone with legitimate business and no questions asked at either end. It is a bad deal. It is also a road, in a season when four other things in this valley have quietly stopped being anybody''s.',NULL,1,'bought_the_road','success','[{"set_flag":"wardens_fate","value":"bought"},{"set_flag":"fen_road_open_paid"},{"take_gold":250},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"aldric":14,"ilse":12,"sera":8,"kessa":-4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_flood_gate'),'look_at_the_gate','Look at the gate','Find out how new the work on the flood gate really is.','New pintles, new packing, and grease on the worm-screw that has not gone grey. The gate is shut and holding four feet of water off a cut that runs east and stays dry. Nothing else at this depth is dry.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'flood_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_flood_gate'),'who_pays_wat','Ask the gateman','Somebody turns the wheel. Find out who tells him to.','Wat Fenner turns the wheel. He is paid four silver a month to keep the gate shut except on the second day of each month, when he raises it for two hours and lowers it again, and he does not know why and has never asked. The money comes wrapped in paper and is left in the same place. He has done it for a year and two months. He was a lock-keeper on the river before the barges stopped, and he is very good at the job nobody has explained to him.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'flood_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_flood_gate'),'opened_the_gate','The cut floods',NULL,'I wound the gate up and the water went east and did not stop going for two days. Whatever was being kept dry down there is not dry now. Undertown lost the two lowest bays of the Low Court and a man''s whole winter store with them, which I did not think about until Aggie Slate made me stand in the water and look at it. Wat Fenner''s money did not come the next month.',NULL,1,'opened_the_gate','success','[{"set_flag":"flood_gate_fate","value":"opened"},{"approval":{"kessa":4,"ilse":-10,"aldric":-8}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_flood_gate'),'left_it_shut','Left as it was',NULL,'I left the gate shut and Wat Fenner keeps turning the wheel on the second of the month for two hours, and the cut beyond it stays dry, and somebody a long way from here goes on paying four silver for that. It is the cheapest arrangement I have ever seen and I have been thinking about it since.',NULL,1,'left_it_shut','neutral','[{"set_flag":"flood_gate_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"sera":4,"ilse":-2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_flood_gate'),'took_the_wheel_key','The key changes hands',NULL,'I have the key to the worm-screw. Wat has the other one and Wat does what Wat is paid to do, but the gate cannot be worked hard against him now without me, and it cannot be worked hard against me without him. He was relieved when I took it. He said it was the first time in a year and two months that there had been two people in the arrangement.',NULL,1,'took_the_wheel_key','success','[{"set_flag":"flood_gate_fate","value":"key"},{"give_item":"gate_wheel_key","quantity":1},{"approval":{"sera":8,"kessa":6,"ilse":4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_in_the_record'),'the_fourth_press','The fourth press','Get Ovid to open the press for the fourth winter.','Every deed, grant, boundary and account this house has held since it was founded, bound by decade, in order. Ovid keeps them and dusts them and lets the rest of the priory look after itself. The fourth winter is in the fourth press and nobody has asked for it in four years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'priory_scriptorium'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_in_the_record'),'eleven_lines','Eleven lines','Read the priory''s own entry for the ford.','Eleven lines, in the infirmarer''s hand, dated. Four huts on the west bank. Nineteen sick, of whom eleven were already dying and eight were not. The order to fire the huts was given by the house, in the house''s own words, to stop the fever crossing the river. One brother would not carry it out. The entry gives the name of the hut he would not fire, and the name of the person in it. It is Bettony Frayle. Nowhere in the eleven lines does the word murder appear.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'priory_scriptorium'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_in_the_record'),'copied_the_record','Copied',NULL,'Ovid found me a good pen and better paper and did not ask what I wanted it for, which is a form of help. The fair copy is eleven lines and it is exact, and I checked it against the original twice, and Ovid checked it once more after that without being asked. The press still holds the original. Now there are two.',NULL,1,'copied_the_record','success','[{"set_flag":"ford_record","value":"copied"},{"set_flag":"priory_record_read"},{"give_item":"ford_record_copy","quantity":1},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"sera":14,"aldric":8,"ilse":6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_in_the_record'),'read_and_left_it','Read and left',NULL,'I read it twice and put the volume back in the press and Ovid closed it and marked the page with a strip of leather, the way she marks everything. It is in the house. It has been in the house for four years and will be there in forty. It says what it says whether or not anybody outside the room has been told.',NULL,1,'read_and_left_it','success','[{"set_flag":"ford_record","value":"read"},{"set_flag":"priory_record_read"},{"approval":{"aldric":4,"ilse":4,"sera":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_in_the_record'),'took_the_leaf','The leaf, taken',NULL,'One leaf, cut out at the gutter with a knife, clean, in about four seconds while Ovid was at the other end of the room with her back to me. The priory''s record of the fourth winter now has a gap in it where the ford was. Nobody can produce their version any more. Neither can anybody else, ever, and that is the part I did not think about until I was on the track going down.',NULL,1,'took_the_leaf','neutral','[{"set_flag":"ford_record","value":"taken"},{"set_flag":"priory_record_read"},{"set_flag":"priory_record_cut"},{"give_item":"ford_record_copy","quantity":1},{"approval":{"kessa":4,"sera":-8,"aldric":-14,"ilse":-10}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_itself'),'the_four_rectangles','The four rectangles','Find out what stood on the west bank of the ford.','Four patches of bare ground, laid out square, in a row, on the west bank of the crossing. Grass reaches the edges and stops. Nobody using the ford will talk about them and everybody using the ford knows exactly where they are, because they all water their horses upstream.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_ford'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_itself'),'the_standing_stone','The standing stone','There is a flat grey stone on the near bank that is not a milestone. Find out what it is.','The stone on the near bank has no cutting on it at all. There are river-stones piled against its foot, hundreds of them, put there one at a time. A man called Joss Frayle comes twice a year and adds one, and he has been doing it for four winters, and he is not the only one.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_ford'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_itself'),'named_the_dead','Nineteen names',NULL,'There were four fever-huts on the west bank in the fourth winter and nineteen people in them when they went up. We got the count off Frayle and the names off the carters who use the road, one at a time, over three days, and we cut them into the standing stone in a hand that will embarrass a mason and last as long as the stone does. It is the first time the place has said anything.',NULL,1,'named_the_dead','success','[{"set_flag":"ford_fate","value":"named"},{"set_flag":"ford_ground_seen"},{"set_flag":"ford_dead_named"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"aldric":18,"ilse":8,"kessa":6,"sera":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_itself'),'cleared_the_crossing','The crossing, cleared',NULL,'The ford has been silting for four years because the burnt timbers went into the water and stayed there, and everybody has been crossing round the fouled part and calling it the crossing. We got the timbers out. It runs clean over laid stone again and takes a wagon at any hour, which is worth more to the west road than anything else I did out here.',NULL,1,'cleared_the_crossing','success','[{"set_flag":"ford_fate","value":"cleared"},{"set_flag":"ford_ground_seen"},{"set_flag":"ford_road_open"},{"approval":{"kessa":8,"sera":10,"ilse":4,"aldric":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_ford_itself'),'left_the_ford','Crossed and went on',NULL,'Four rectangles, a stone with no cutting on it, and a river. I crossed at a trot like everybody else does.',NULL,1,'left_the_ford','neutral','[{"set_flag":"ford_fate","value":"left"},{"set_flag":"ford_ground_seen"}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_forty_one'),'the_list','The list','Get Aske Vorn to show you what she has been carrying.','Sixty names, forty-one ticked, and nineteen with the same mark against them nineteen times. She has never shown it to anybody in four years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_grey_hall'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_forty_one'),'the_two_names','Two who should not be here','Find the two names that are in Waerhaven.','Two of the nineteen are on the city''s own rolls: one in the Tar Gaol, held for existing, and one in the long room at the lazar house who came south later than everyone and further.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_lazar_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_forty_one'),'the_gaol','The one in the gaol','Get to the second name before the Houses move him.','Held by the Tarrow Houses on an authority nobody has ever produced, in a room he can see the oakum shed from. He answers to the name. He answers to it in the wrong accent.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_tar_gaol'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_forty_one'),'named','Named out loud',NULL,'We read the nineteen out at the Chapel of the Grey Road, by village, in the order they were lost, and Aske Vorn stood up and said what happened to each of them in front of forty people who had been waiting four years to be told. Two of them are here and they are not what she wrote down, and she said that out loud too, which is the part I did not expect.',NULL,1,'named','success','[{"set_flag":"forty_one_fate","value":"named"},{"xp":180}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_forty_one'),'buried','Left unsaid',NULL,'The list went in the stove at the Grey Hall and the two names went out of Waerhaven the same night, on a cart, south, with money. Nobody in the Wardenswatch will ever be told, which is what Vorn asked for, and she thanked me, and she has not looked at me properly since.',NULL,1,'buried','success','[{"set_flag":"forty_one_fate","value":"buried"}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_indentured'),'the_canteen_board','The second column','The price board in the canteen has two columns. Find out what the second one is.','There are two columns of prices chalked in the Deepworks canteen. The first is cash. The second is against wages, and it is a halfpenny dearer on every line, and the halfpenny is the whole of it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'deepworks_canteen'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_indentured'),'the_arithmetic','The other sheet','Corrin Dale''s indenture is perfectly fair. Find the sheet that does the arithmetic.','Corrin Dale signed for three years against a cottage, a cow and the carriage of both. He is in his fourth year. Every clause of what he signed is fair. The unfairness is entirely in the arithmetic, and the arithmetic is kept on a second sheet in the timekeeper''s hut, and he has never been shown it and has never asked to be.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'timekeepers_hut'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_indentured'),'bought_him_out','Paid off',NULL,'A hundred and fifty gold closed Corrin Dale''s account and the clerk thanked me for making the column balance. He walked up the stair and stood at the top of it for a long time. There are a hundred and ninety-odd others and I have a hundred and ninety-odd fewer reasons than I had this morning to think well of myself.',NULL,1,'bought_him_out','success','[{"set_flag":"indentured_fate","value":"bought"},{"pressure":1},{"take_gold":150},{"approval":{"aldric":16,"ilse":12,"kessa":10,"sera":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_indentured'),'read_it_back','Read back to him',NULL,'I read Dale his own indenture and then I read him the arithmetic, in the canteen, out loud, with sixty men listening. Nobody threw anything. Nobody walked out. A man at the end said he had worked that out in his second year and asked me what exactly I thought he was supposed to do about it. I did not have an answer and he did not expect one.',NULL,1,'read_it_back','success','[{"set_flag":"indentured_fate","value":"read"},{"set_flag":"diggers_told"},{"pressure":3},{"give_item":"indenture_paper","quantity":1},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"kessa":14,"ilse":10,"aldric":8,"sera":-8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_indentured'),'left_them_to_it','Left to it',NULL,'It is a contract. They signed it. Every clause of it is fair and every man down there is a grown man, and I have said all of that to myself twice on the way up the stair, which is once more than I needed to.',NULL,1,'left_them_to_it','neutral','[{"set_flag":"indentured_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"aldric":-12,"ilse":-8,"kessa":-6,"sera":4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_landing'),'the_quay','The new landing','Half the common wharf is idle and the new landing is not. Ask why.','Greyhythe has two quays. The old one has four hundred years and four hundred opinions on it and half its berths are empty. The new one has a crane, a bonded shed, an iron fence with an open gate, and men who are paid weekly. Nobody at the old quay will say a word against it and every one of them looks at it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'corse_landing'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_landing'),'the_shed','The bonded shed','Count what is in the shed, and what it is all for.','Salt, iron, lamp oil, sawn timber, rope, sailcloth and eleven hundred yards of chain. Every one of them a thing you would want if you were going to put two hundred men underground and keep them there. None of it is for sale. All of it is going somewhere, and the somewhere is upriver.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'tally_shed'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_landing'),'counted_the_chain','Eleven hundred yards',NULL,'Gillian Petch showed me the book because nobody has ever told her not to, and there is nothing in the book: it is honest to the yard. That is the point of it. Eleven hundred yards of chain, dated, tallied twice, going up a river to a place that does not appear in any document in Greyhythe, because the place does not have a name yet.',NULL,1,'counted_the_chain','success','[{"set_flag":"landing_fate","value":"counted"},{"set_flag":"landing_read"},{"pressure":1},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"sera":12,"ilse":6,"aldric":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_landing'),'left_it_alone','A quay is a quay',NULL,'A merchant house built a quay. It is the least suspicious thing a merchant house has ever done and I have spent an afternoon looking at it as though it were a body.',NULL,1,'left_it_alone','neutral','[{"set_flag":"landing_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"kessa":4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_last_quarryman'),'the_cottage_on_the_spoil','The cottage on the spoil','Find the man who was below the fall and get him to talk about it.','There is a cottage on the spoil heap above the old quarry, built out of offcuts by somebody who knew how to lay stone. The door faces north. The quarry is south. He has not turned round in eleven years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'quarrymans_hut'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_last_quarryman'),'what_he_heard','What he heard','Hear his account of the day it fell.','Ackley says the fall did not start at the face. He was below it, in the sump gallery, and it came up at him from underneath — the floor first, then the face, in that order, with a count of about four between them. Every account the town has says the face went and took the floor with it. He has told nobody, because eighteen men on the rim all saw the face go and he was the only one who was not looking at it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'quarrymans_hut'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_last_quarryman'),'he_went_down','He went back',NULL,'He came with us as far as the old adit and stood in the entry and told us where the water used to run and where it runs now, and the difference is thirty feet of new fall in the wrong direction. Then he sat down on the spoil and could not get up for a while, and we walked him home, and he asked us not to tell anyone he had gone.',NULL,1,'he_went_down','success','[{"set_flag":"quarryman_fate","value":"went"},{"set_flag":"quarry_fell_upward"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"ilse":10,"aldric":12,"kessa":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_last_quarryman'),'he_told_it_sitting','Told from the bench',NULL,'He told it from the bench outside his own door, facing north, in about eleven minutes, and did not stop once. I have the account and I do not have the place. He would not go and I did not push him, and I think that was the right call and I am not certain.',NULL,1,'he_told_it_sitting','success','[{"set_flag":"quarryman_fate","value":"told"},{"set_flag":"quarry_fell_upward"},{"approval":{"aldric":8,"ilse":6,"sera":4,"kessa":-2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_last_quarryman'),'left_him_alone','Left on the spoil',NULL,'He asked us to go and we went. Eleven years is a long time to sit facing the wrong way and he has got good at it, and I decided that was his to keep.',NULL,1,'left_him_alone','neutral','[{"set_flag":"quarryman_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"aldric":6,"kessa":4,"ilse":-2,"sera":-4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_light_goes_out'),'up_the_point','Up the point','Talk to the keeper.','Ellsa Waer will not send her own people up the point to ask her own grandson what he has been doing, and she has been very clear that this is not because she is afraid of the answer.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_waer_light'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_light_goes_out'),'four_nights','Four nights','Find out what came ashore.','Four dark nights, four boats, all on the deep side where there is forty fathoms right up to the rock. Nothing was landed on the quay and nothing went through the Counting Boom, and the oil store up there is fuller than it has any business being in spring.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_waer_light'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_light_goes_out'),'stopped','The light stays lit',NULL,'It burns every night now, and Nel Waer told his grandmother himself, in the Fish Hall, standing up, which cost him more than the money did. Whoever was landing on the deep side will have to land somewhere with a witness.',NULL,1,'stopped','success','[{"set_flag":"light_fate","value":"stopped"},{"xp":120}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_light_goes_out'),'joined','Four more nights',NULL,'I took the arrangement over rather than closing it. The light goes dark when we say and the boats come in on the deep side and nothing goes through anybody''s book, and Nel Waer is very grateful and slightly frightened of me now.',NULL,1,'joined','success','[{"set_flag":"light_fate","value":"joined"},{"give_gold":200}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_miller_who_stayed'),'somebody_lives_here','Somebody lives here','Find out who is living in the mill ruin.','A cooking pot, a cleared corner under the sound gable, and a path worn to the race. Wick Lorrimer milled here for eighteen years and has not left in the four since it burned.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'mill_ruin'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_miller_who_stayed'),'the_race_he_keeps','The race he keeps','Ask him why he still clears a mill race that turns nothing.','He clears the race every week. It turns nothing and it has turned nothing for four years. He does it because a race that is kept is a race that still has a right attached to it, and the right is worth something to somebody, and he worked that out about eleven months after the fire, from a letter he was sent by mistake.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'mill_ruin'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_miller_who_stayed'),'brought_him_in','Brought in',NULL,'He came into Rivermark with us and is sleeping in the Flagon''s back room on Mara''s charity, which she will call rent within a fortnight to spare him. He has not been indoors at night in four years and he sat up in the common room until the fire went out because he could not work out what to do in a room.',NULL,1,'brought_him_in','success','[{"set_flag":"miller_fate","value":"in"},{"set_flag":"wick_in_town"},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"aldric":14,"kessa":6,"ilse":2,"sera":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_miller_who_stayed'),'let_him_stay','Let stay',NULL,'We put a roof over the sound gable, re-hung the door and swept the wheel-pit, and he did not thank us and did not stop us. He said the race would want doing again on Thursday. He says that about everything.',NULL,1,'let_him_stay','success','[{"set_flag":"miller_fate","value":"stayed"},{"set_flag":"mill_is_shelter"},{"approval":{"ilse":12,"kessa":8,"aldric":4,"sera":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_miller_who_stayed'),'took_it_to_paper','Taken to paper',NULL,'The letter he was sent by mistake was an instruction to a clerk about the mill race, dated three weeks before the fire. We took it to the counting house and had it copied and entered. The debt on the mill was discharged twice: once by the mill, once by whoever bought it after it stopped existing. Wick does not care about any of this. He asked whether it meant he had to move.',NULL,1,'took_it_to_paper','success','[{"set_flag":"miller_fate","value":"paper"},{"set_flag":"mill_fire_was_set"},{"set_flag":"mill_race_letter_filed"},{"pressure":1},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"sera":14,"aldric":6,"ilse":4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_nineteen'),'she_says_it','The eleventh night','Let Yrsa get to the end of a sentence.','She starts this story about once a month and stops it in the same place, and everybody in the Bough lets her stop, kindly, which is why she has been stopping there for four years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_green_bough'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_nineteen'),'the_road_south','What she carried','Go with her as far as she is willing to go.','Nineteen did not arrive. Aske Vorn''s mark against all nineteen is the same mark. Yrsa knows what the mark means because she was the one holding the lamp.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'chapel_of_the_grey_road'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_nineteen'),'told','Told',NULL,'She said it in the chapel, out loud, by name, and nobody died of hearing it. She was furious afterwards for about an hour and then she was not. What she wanted was not comfort and was never comfort — it was somebody who would let the sentence finish.',NULL,1,'told','success','[{"set_flag":"yrsa_fate","value":"told"},{"approval":{"yrsa":15}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_nineteen'),'unsaid','Unsaid',NULL,'I told her she did not have to say it, and meant it, and she took that, and she has been easier since and further away since, both. She says the same three sentences about the eleventh night now and she says them like a thing she has agreed to say.',NULL,1,'unsaid','success','[{"set_flag":"yrsa_fate","value":"unsaid"},{"approval":{"yrsa":8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_order_that_threw_him_out'),'the_gate','The gate','Go up the priory track and pull the bell-rope.','The priory gate is good stonework with a new pine door in it, cut to fit an opening it was never meant for, because the original went for something. The alms slot in the wall has been plugged with rag from the inside.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'priory_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_order_that_threw_him_out'),'what_the_house_is_for','What the house is for','Find out what the priory actually does all day.','The rest of the priory is an arrangement that exists to keep one room open: twelve beds, six of them made up, both hearths in, and a door straight out to the yard so nobody has to be carried through the cloister. They take anyone. They have taken anyone for a hundred and forty years, and the reason they own eight fewer relics than they did in spring is that linen and lamp oil have to be bought.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'priory_infirmary'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_order_that_threw_him_out'),'heard_them_out','Heard out',NULL,'I asked the prior about the brother they put out four winters ago and she answered the question I asked, which was not the question I meant. They did not expel him for what he did to a sick woman. They expelled him for refusing an instruction, in front of the house, at the ford, and she would not say what the instruction was, and she said ''would not'' rather than ''cannot'', and looked at me while she did it.',NULL,1,'heard_them_out','success','[{"set_flag":"priory_fate","value":"heard"},{"set_flag":"priory_seen"},{"set_flag":"priory_refusal_known"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"aldric":10,"sera":8,"ilse":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_order_that_threw_him_out'),'took_their_side','Their account, accepted',NULL,'Eleven men, a hospice, and a house that has sold eight relics to buy linen. The prior gave me her account of the ford and I took it, and I told her so, and she thanked me and looked tired rather than relieved. Whatever else this order is, it is not the thing anyone in Rivermark thinks it is.',NULL,1,'took_their_side','success','[{"set_flag":"priory_fate","value":"priory"},{"set_flag":"priory_seen"},{"set_flag":"priory_account_accepted"},{"approval":{"aldric":-10,"sera":6,"kessa":-4,"ilse":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_order_that_threw_him_out'),'asked_nothing','Asked nothing',NULL,'I walked the cloister, stood in the infirmary door, watched eleven men keep the hours, and did not ask the question I came up the track with. I have no account of that house except the one I was given by a man who is not allowed in it, and I have now seen the house and still only have his.',NULL,1,'asked_nothing','neutral','[{"set_flag":"priory_fate","value":"unentered"},{"approval":{"aldric":4,"sera":-6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_overseers_office'),'the_ladder','Up the ladder','Bael Rourke runs the works from a hut above the headings. Get into it.','Bael Rourke came up through the headings and has the hands to prove it. He runs two hundred people on time and under cost and is extremely proud of the first half of that. His office is up a ladder and its shutter faces the works, which means everybody can see who is standing in it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'overseers_office'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_overseers_office'),'the_strongbox','The strongbox and the rack','The strongbox is bolted through the joist. The rack beside it is not locked at all.','There is a strongbox in Rourke''s office bolted through the floor and through the joist, and there are eleven pounds in it, and it is the only thing in the room anybody has ever thought to secure. The rolled paper in the rack next to it is working paper. Nobody at the works has ever considered it worth anything.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'overseers_office'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_overseers_office'),'talked_your_way_in','Asked, and shown',NULL,'Rourke showed me the office because I asked to see it. He is proud of the works and nobody has ever been proud of them at him before. He walked me through the props, the pump schedule and the cost of a bucket of sand, and left me alone in the room for four minutes to go and shout at somebody about a barrow.',NULL,1,'talked_your_way_in','success','[{"set_flag":"office_fate","value":"talked"},{"set_flag":"office_open"},{"approval":{"sera":12,"aldric":6,"ilse":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_overseers_office'),'took_the_office','Taken',NULL,'Rourke leaned out of the shutter and said a number, and the number was how many wardens came up the ladder. It is his office now in the sense that his name is on the door and it is mine in the sense that I am standing in it and he is not. He was paid weekly and so were they. I keep thinking about that.',NULL,1,'took_the_office','success','[{"set_flag":"office_fate","value":"took"},{"set_flag":"office_open"},{"set_flag":"works_alarmed"},{"pressure":3},{"approval":{"kessa":12,"aldric":-10,"sera":-8,"ilse":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_overseers_office'),'stayed_out','Left on the ladder',NULL,'I went up as far as the platform, looked in at the shutter, and came down again. Everybody on the floor below saw me do both. That is what the platform is for.',NULL,1,'stayed_out','neutral','[{"set_flag":"office_fate","value":"out"}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_pit_champion'),'take_a_bout','Take a bout','Get Vessa Dann to quote you a number, and find out what the number is for.','Vessa Dann keeps the board at the fighting pit. She looked me over on the way down the ladder and decided on a number before I opened my mouth. The pit has one draw worth betting on and he has not lost in fourteen months.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'fighting_pit'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_pit_champion'),'the_undercroft','Behind the gate','Go through the gate and find out why the pit''s man never leaves.','Orm Lisser sleeps in the second stall. He is not chained and the door is not locked and he has not been outside in fourteen months, because there is a bond with his mark on it: forty-one gold advanced against eighteen months of bouts, at a rate of forfeit that has quietly made the eighteen months into four years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'pit_undercroft'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_pit_champion'),'took_the_belt','The twelfth name',NULL,'I fought him and I won it, on the sand, in front of forty people making the noise of three hundred. The belt has my name punched into it now. So does the board. Orm''s bond is discharged by the terms of it — a champion who loses is a champion nobody pays to see — and he walked up the ladder at dusk with nothing, which he says is more than he had at noon.',NULL,1,'took_the_belt','success','[{"set_flag":"pit_fate","value":"belt"},{"set_flag":"pit_champion_is_you"},{"give_item":"pit_belt","quantity":1},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"kessa":15,"sera":4,"aldric":-6,"ilse":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_pit_champion'),'bought_the_bond','Bought out',NULL,'Forty-one gold and eleven in accrued forfeit, paid on the rim in front of witnesses, and Vessa wrote ''discharged'' on the bond herself because she is not a thief and never claimed to be. She was also not pleased. The pit still stands and it still has a gate, and it now has nobody to put behind it.',NULL,1,'bought_the_bond','success','[{"set_flag":"pit_fate","value":"bought"},{"set_flag":"orm_free"},{"take_gold":120},{"give_item":"pit_bond","quantity":1},{"approval":{"aldric":16,"ilse":8,"sera":-6,"kessa":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_pit_champion'),'broke_the_pit','Read out on the rim',NULL,'I read the bond out loud from the rim, all of it, including the rate of forfeit, to forty people who had come to bet on the man it belonged to. The pit did not close because somebody closed it. It closed because you cannot sell a bout to a crowd that has just done the arithmetic.',NULL,1,'broke_the_pit','success','[{"set_flag":"pit_fate","value":"broken"},{"set_flag":"orm_free"},{"set_flag":"pit_closed"},{"approval":{"ilse":12,"aldric":12,"kessa":-10,"sera":-8}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_polite_man'),'go_downriver','Greyhythe','Ludo Corse keeps house at Greyhythe. Go and look at him.','Ludo Corse, factor, of Greyhythe. Pyke says he has been down twice in three years, was perfectly civil both times, and paid on the day.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'factors_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_polite_man'),'the_chair','The chair on your side of the desk','Sit down. Ask him whatever you like.','He answered the door himself, put me in the chair, and asked whether I had eaten. There is a chair on my side of the desk and it is worn through at the arms, which means a great many people have sat in it, which means a great many people have come here to ask him something.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'factors_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_polite_man'),'asked_everything','Everything, honestly',NULL,'I asked him what he buys and he told me. I asked him who he buys it for and he told me. I asked him what the mark on the note was and he said it was the house''s mark and had been since his grandfather. He did not lie once and I came out into the street knowing nothing I could say aloud to Reed. That is not an accident. That is a method, and he has been using it on better people than me for a long time.',NULL,1,'asked_everything','success','[{"set_flag":"polite_man_fate","value":"asked"},{"set_flag":"met_corse"},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"sera":12,"aldric":6,"ilse":4,"kessa":-6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_polite_man'),'asked_nothing','Nothing worth asking',NULL,'I sat in the chair for a quarter of an hour and could not think of a question that would not have made me look like a fool. He was very kind about it. He said most people find the second visit easier.',NULL,1,'asked_nothing','neutral','[{"set_flag":"polite_man_fate","value":"nothing"},{"set_flag":"met_corse"},{"approval":{"kessa":2,"sera":-6}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_reliquary'),'eight_empty_shelves','Eight empty shelves','Get into the reliquary and find out where the eight went.','Nine reliquaries, seventeen spaces, eight small cards in a careful hand. Brother Venn is the almoner. He buys the flour, the linen and the lamp oil for a house with no income, and he has been keeping receipts where the relics used to stand because he refuses to pretend they were stolen.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'priory_reliquary'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_reliquary'),'what_else_he_offered_for','What else he offered for','Find out what the buyer asked for besides the relics.','The buyer''s agent pays well, pays on the day, and does not haggle. On the third visit he asked whether the house had any old paper it wanted rid of — the deeds, the boundary rolls, the cartulary — and offered a price for the lot that Venn thought was generous, because Venn has never once thought of the cartulary as being worth anything at all.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'priory_reliquary'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_reliquary'),'stopped_the_sale','Stopped',NULL,'We put it to the prior in front of Venn, which was not kind and was necessary, and the sale is stopped: no more relics and, specifically and in writing, no paper. The house will be short by midwinter and everybody in the room knew it while they were agreeing to it. Venn shook my hand afterwards and could not look at me.',NULL,1,'stopped_the_sale','success','[{"set_flag":"reliquary_fate","value":"stopped"},{"set_flag":"priory_paper_kept"},{"pressure":2},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"aldric":14,"ilse":8,"sera":6,"kessa":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_reliquary'),'let_it_sell','Sold',NULL,'It is their house and their paper and their winter, and I said so, and the sale went through in the second week: three more reliquaries and the fourth press of the cartulary, for eighty gold, which kept the infirmary in linen and oil until spring. The buyer''s man collected it himself and was extremely polite about the whole thing.',NULL,1,'let_it_sell','neutral','[{"set_flag":"reliquary_fate","value":"sold"},{"set_flag":"priory_paper_sold"},{"approval":{"sera":4,"aldric":-12,"ilse":-8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_reliquary'),'bought_the_paper','The paper, bought',NULL,'I outbid him for the fourth press by ninety gold, which is an absurd amount of money for a decade of a small house''s leases and boundary rolls, and Venn took the coin with the expression of a man who has just been let off something. The buyer''s agent was told the lot had gone. He asked, very politely, who to. Venn told him. I would have told him too.',NULL,1,'bought_the_paper','success','[{"set_flag":"reliquary_fate","value":"paper"},{"set_flag":"priory_paper_kept"},{"set_flag":"cartulary_held"},{"pressure":2},{"take_gold":90},{"give_item":"priory_cartulary","quantity":1},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"sera":14,"aldric":10,"ilse":6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_same_mark'),'two_places','Two places','Nothing to do about it. Keep your eyes open.','A plumb-bob hanging inside a square, cut or stamped or painted. I have seen it twice now, in two places that have no business sharing anything. It is probably a maker''s mark. Most things are.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'granary_row'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_same_mark'),'asked_the_chainman','Ask the man who paints them','Alder Pyke walks lines for whoever is paying. Ask him what the mark is.','There is an old chainman on Granary Row with a hundred feet of chain over his shoulder and a plumb-bob in his pocket, and the plumb-bob has the mark stamped on the flat. He paints them. He has painted a great many.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'granary_row'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_same_mark'),'started_counting','Counting them',NULL,'It is a survey mark. Pyke was quite clear and quite bored: a chain is dragged, a line is walked, a mark is painted, and a man is paid one and threepence a day for it. There is nothing to it. I have started writing down where I see them anyway, and I could not tell you why.',NULL,1,'started_counting','success','[{"set_flag":"same_mark_fate","value":"counting"},{"set_flag":"counting_the_marks"},{"give_item":"surveyors_plumb","quantity":1},{"approval":{"ilse":5,"sera":6,"aldric":3}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_same_mark'),'let_it_alone','A maker''s mark',NULL,'It is a survey mark. Somebody is measuring something, which is what people with money do before they buy it, and it is no more sinister than a milestone. I asked, I was answered, and I have let it alone.',NULL,1,'let_it_alone','neutral','[{"set_flag":"same_mark_fate","value":"let_alone"},{"approval":{"kessa":3}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sealed_arch'),'find_the_arch','Find the arch','Aggie Slate says a passage that used to go somewhere does not any more. Go and look at it.','Aggie Slate has sat the Low Court eleven years and lived in the tunnels for nineteen. She walked the passage south of the weir as a girl and it came out somewhere. It does not come out anywhere now.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'bricked_arch'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sealed_arch'),'the_far_side','Read the wall','Work out when the arch was closed, and from which side.','The arch is old, soft, lime-set and hand-made. The fill is hard grey brick in a cement that has not weathered, laid plumb, laid by somebody who was paid properly. The joints are struck smooth on the far face and rough on this one, which is what a wall looks like when the mason was standing on the other side of it: nobody finishes the face they are walking away from. Whoever bricked this up did not come back this way. One brick near the springing of the arch carries a small cut mark, a plumb-line crossed by a square, cut before the brick was fired.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'bricked_arch'),0,NULL,'success','[{"set_flag":"mark_seen_brick"}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sealed_arch'),'broke_through','Through',NULL,'Two hours with a bar. Behind the fill the passage runs on about thirty feet and then turns down, and it has been timbered — new pine, sawn square, set by somebody who intends the roof to stay up for years. There is a ladder. The ladder is worn in the middle of every rung and dry, which means it is used and used often and not by anyone coming up through water. We went down four lengths and then came back, because I had a lamp and about an hour of oil and no idea at all how deep it went. I went back eleven days later. The arch was bricked again, in the same grey brick, and the joints were struck smooth on the far side.',NULL,1,'broke_through','success','[{"set_flag":"sealed_arch_fate","value":"opened"},{"set_flag":"arch_reopened"},{"pressure":1},{"approval":{"ilse":10,"kessa":8,"sera":6,"aldric":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sealed_arch'),'left_it_sealed','Left standing',NULL,'I left the wall up. I paced it out from the weir and from the Low Court stair and wrote both counts down, so that if it ever matters I can put my hand on the place in the dark. Aggie Slate watched me do it and said nothing, and then said that in nineteen years I was the second person to write anything down about that wall, and did not say who the first was.',NULL,1,'left_it_sealed','neutral','[{"set_flag":"sealed_arch_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"ilse":4,"aldric":4,"kessa":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sealed_arch'),'took_a_rubbing','A rubbing of the brick',NULL,'Paper on the brick and the flat of a charcoal, and it came up clean: a plumb-line crossed by a square, no bigger than a thumbnail. I took it to Brenna, who deals with people who work stone, and she said it is a mason''s mark, that every mason cuts one, that this one is a good clean job and she does not know the hand. She turned it over twice. Then she gave it back and asked me, in a completely ordinary voice, where I had got it, and I told her, and she said hm, and went back to the bellows.',NULL,1,'took_a_rubbing','success','[{"set_flag":"sealed_arch_fate","value":"rubbing"},{"give_item":"arch_rubbing","quantity":1},{"approval":{"sera":8,"ilse":6,"aldric":2}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_seers_coin'),'sit_for_a_reading','Sit down in front of her','Pay Nan Vetch a copper and listen to what she says.','Nan Vetch reads water and weather on the High Street for coppers. She told me the river is coming back for the west bank, that it has done it twice before in her life, and that a wise man sells while the ground is still worth something. She said it the way a woman says a thing she has said four hundred times.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'high_street'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_seers_coin'),'follow_the_coin','Who pays her','She is paid in something. Find out by whom.','Nan is paid two silver a week, in advance, by a clerk who walks down from the counting house on a Tuesday, hands it over without stopping, and has never once given a name or asked her a question. She has never had to say anything untrue. That is what she wants understood: the flats will go under, they always go under, and she has been paid to keep saying so at exactly the moment it is worth the most to somebody.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'counting_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_seers_coin'),'she_stopped','She stopped',NULL,'Nan gave the last week''s silver back, which cost her more than it sounds, and reads only weather now. There is a girl doing cards outside the Flagon within the fortnight who tells anybody from the west bank that the water is coming. Nan says she is not very good and will get better.',NULL,1,'she_stopped','success','[{"set_flag":"seers_coin_fate","value":"stopped"},{"approval":{"aldric":8,"ilse":6,"sera":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_seers_coin'),'traced_the_hand','Down to the clerk',NULL,'I waited on the corner three Tuesdays and followed the man with the satchel. He is a hired copyist who works out of a room over the counting house, he is paid by the letter, and he has never met the person whose instructions he carries out. He was frightened of me and had nothing at all to be frightened about. There are, he says, five other standing payments on the same list. He is not allowed to say what they are and had clearly never wondered.',NULL,1,'traced_the_hand','success','[{"set_flag":"seers_coin_fate","value":"traced"},{"set_flag":"copyist_found"},{"approval":{"sera":8,"ilse":6,"kessa":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_seers_coin'),'turned_her','Turned',NULL,'I pay Nan Vetch thirty gold and she reads what I like. She still takes the silver on Tuesdays. She was quite clear that she would, and quite clear that I would want her to, and she was right about both before I was.',NULL,1,'turned_her','success','[{"set_flag":"seers_coin_fate","value":"turned"},{"take_gold":30},{"approval":{"kessa":4,"sera":10,"aldric":-12,"ilse":-6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_short_weight'),'ask_the_weighmaster','Ask Corran Sedge','The Weighmaster holds one of the three keys. Find out what he will say.','Ilber will pay to have the League standard weight put on a true beam. It lives in a sealed box on the Counting Boom''s wall with three locks: the Factor, the Master Shipwright, and the Weighmaster.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_weigh_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_short_weight'),'the_three_keys','Three keys, three people','Get the box open, or get round it.','Sedge will not open it and will not say why in a room with a door. Whatever else he is, he is not a thief — he is a careful man who has worked out something and has nobody safe to tell.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_counting_boom'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_short_weight'),'the_box_open','On a true beam','Weigh the standard against something honest.','Vennik has a beam under a glass dome that will read a letter. Put the League''s weight on it and the argument is over in the time it takes the pointer to stop.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'venniks'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_short_weight'),'proved','Four ounces',NULL,'Four ounces light, and the filing is on the underside where the stamp is, and it is six years old. Six years of grain weighed against it, every quarter, every barge. Waerhaven has not been cheating Lathmere. Waerhaven has been paying for grain by weight and receiving it by a lie, and the lie is in this city''s own box and was cut with somebody''s own file.',NULL,1,'proved','success','[{"set_flag":"weight_fate","value":"proved"},{"give_item":"league_standard_weight","quantity":1},{"xp":150}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_short_weight'),'sold_the_proof','Sold back',NULL,'I took the weight to the people it would have ruined, and they paid, and it went back in the box, and the box was sealed again with a seal that is a very good copy. Everything in Waerhaven is still weighed against it.',NULL,1,'sold','success','[{"set_flag":"weight_fate","value":"sold"},{"give_gold":250}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_short_weight'),'let_it_lie','Left in the box',NULL,'I put it back and said nothing. Ilber will keep buying by it, and so will the granary, and in eleven weeks it will not matter what anybody buys by.',NULL,1,'lie','neutral','[{"set_flag":"weight_fate","value":"lie"}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sluice'),'the_gate_is_up','The gate is up','Get down to the sluice and look at the ironwork.','Two stone piers, a paved apron, an oak gate in an iron frame, and a screw-jack that has been greased this month. It is the first square corner west of the causeway and every part of it has been maintained continuously for forty years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'sluice_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sluice'),'who_pays_the_keeper','Who pays the keeper','Find out who has been paying the sluice-keeper, and for what.','Gubb Wrayne keeps the gate. He cannot write, so he keeps his accounts in notches and coin-rubbings: forty years of quarterly wages, every one paid, none late. He has never met anyone who pays him. The money is left in the same place on the same day and he has never once waited up to see who leaves it, because he was told at the start that if he ever did, the wage would stop.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'sluice_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sluice'),'shut_the_sluice','Shut',NULL,'It took four of us on the screw and most of an afternoon and the gate came down as sweetly as if it had been shut last week, because it has been maintained by a man who has nothing else to do. The fen will take two years to drain and about a hundred people are going to discover that ground they have been using was not theirs. Wrayne watched us do it and did not stop us and did not help, and asked afterwards whether he should still expect his wage.',NULL,1,'shut_the_sluice','success','[{"set_flag":"sluice_fate","value":"shut"},{"set_flag":"fen_draining"},{"pressure":3},{"give_item":"sluice_ledger","quantity":1},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"ilse":10,"sera":10,"kessa":8,"aldric":-6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sluice'),'left_it_open','Left open',NULL,'Four thousand acres, a village under it, a road across it and about forty people living off it, and one gate that could undo all of that in an afternoon. I left the gate where it has been since before I was born. Wrayne greased the screw while we were still standing there, which he does every month, and it is very hard to explain why that was the thing that decided it.',NULL,1,'left_it_open','neutral','[{"set_flag":"sluice_fate","value":"open"},{"approval":{"aldric":8,"ilse":6,"sera":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_sluice'),'took_the_keepers_wage','The wage, taken',NULL,'The quarter''s coin is left in a slot in the west pier on the second day after the quarter, in a purse, with no writing on it. We waited two nights and nobody came, and on the third morning it was there. We took it, left Wrayne his share, and put the purse back empty. Somebody now knows that somebody is watching the sluice. That is a message I sent without meaning to and cannot take back.',NULL,1,'took_the_keepers_wage','neutral','[{"set_flag":"sluice_fate","value":"kept"},{"set_flag":"sluice_wage_intercepted"},{"pressure":1},{"give_gold":180},{"give_item":"sluice_ledger","quantity":1},{"approval":{"sera":10,"kessa":6,"aldric":-10,"ilse":-6}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_survey'),'the_rack','Not in the strongbox','The strongbox holds the wages. The rack holds the working paper. Look in the rack.','Rourke''s strongbox is bolted through the floor and through the joist and there are eleven pounds in it. The rolled paper in the rack beside it is not locked up at all, because nobody at the works has ever thought of it as worth anything. It is only the survey.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'overseers_office'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_survey'),'in_hand','In hand','You have it. Now decide what it is for.','Every field, road, weir, seam and roof between the ford and Greyhythe, measured and valued and totalled in one hand. Rivermark is on sheet six. It is not drawn as a town. It is entered in the margin under the head ''clearance'', as a cost, and the figure beside it has been revised downward twice — which means somebody sat down twice and worked out that we would come cheaper than that.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'factors_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_survey'),'took_the_survey','Kept',NULL,'I have it, and Corse knows I have it, and he was neither angry nor surprised. He said that a document is only worth what the man holding it can do with it, and asked whether I would like a copy of sheet six for my own use, since I would find the original difficult to read by candlelight. I said no. I am not certain that was the right answer.',NULL,1,'took_the_survey','success','[{"set_flag":"survey_fate","value":"took"},{"set_flag":"act_two_open"},{"pressure":3},{"approval":{"sera":12,"ilse":8,"aldric":6,"kessa":6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_survey'),'burned_the_survey','Burned',NULL,'Three years of chain-work, nine sheets, and about four hundred days of somebody''s wages, gone in the time it takes paper to go. It will all be done again. It will take them three years to do it again, and for three years nobody will know what this valley is worth, including us. Somebody is going to start asking who was standing next to the fire.',NULL,1,'burned_the_survey','success','[{"set_flag":"survey_fate","value":"burned"},{"set_flag":"act_two_open"},{"pressure":4},{"take_item":"the_valley_survey"},{"approval":{"kessa":16,"ilse":10,"aldric":-6,"sera":-10}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_survey'),'sold_it_back','Sold back',NULL,'Five hundred gold, counted out without a word of argument, and articles of retainer at forty a quarter for services not further described. He had them written before I came. Not for me — for whoever came. That is the part I keep going back to: the chair was worn through at the arms and the paper was already drawn.',NULL,1,'sold_it_back','success','[{"set_flag":"survey_fate","value":"sold"},{"set_flag":"act_two_open"},{"set_flag":"corse_retains_us"},{"pressure":1},{"take_item":"the_valley_survey"},{"give_gold":500},{"give_item":"corse_retainer","quantity":1},{"approval":{"kessa":-12,"ilse":-18,"aldric":-20,"sera":8}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_survey'),'warned_the_town','Read out on Granary Row',NULL,'Pyke read it out, because Pyke can read a survey and I cannot, and because it was his chain that made half of it. Forty people stood in the rain on Granary Row and listened to a man tell them what their roofs had been valued at. Reed wrote it all down. There is no law it breaks. There is nobody to arrest. The town knows exactly what is coming now, and knowing is the whole of what it can do, and Pyke is out of work.',NULL,1,'warned_the_town','success','[{"set_flag":"survey_fate","value":"warned"},{"set_flag":"act_two_open"},{"set_flag":"rivermark_warned"},{"pressure":3},{"approval":{"aldric":18,"ilse":14,"kessa":8,"sera":-6}}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_thing_under_the_quarry'),'past_the_pumps','Past the pumps','The old workings are along the launder, past the pump gallery.','Everything the Deepworks does is aimed at one place, and the place is not on the plank floor or under the lamps. It is past the pumps, along the launder, in the workings that were there before the Concern''s timber was.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'pump_gallery'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_thing_under_the_quarry'),'the_face','Four inches','The cutting is nearly through. Decide what to do about the last of it.','The hole the quarry made when it fell, three years of water in the bottom, and one face cut at very carefully with hand tools and no picks. The rock is the wrong colour and gives the wrong sound. There is a chalk line on the floor and no footprints past it, and there are about four inches of stone left.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_undercut'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_thing_under_the_quarry'),'cut_it_out','The last four inches',NULL,'We took the face down ourselves and what was behind it had been waiting for those four inches for three years. It is dead now, or the part of it in that chamber is. I do not know what it was. Nobody who paid to have it dug up knows what it was either — that is the thing I cannot put down. Three years, two hundred men and a whole valley bought, to find out.',NULL,1,'cut_it_out','success','[{"set_flag":"undercut_fate","value":"cut"},{"set_flag":"saw_what_it_is"},{"pressure":3},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"kessa":12,"ilse":-4,"sera":6,"aldric":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_thing_under_the_quarry'),'brought_it_down','Brought down',NULL,'We knocked the props and put forty feet of old quarry on top of the cut face. It will take them a year and a half to get back to where they were this morning, and it has cost them nothing they cannot afford, and every man who dug it will dig it again for the same one and threepence. But they are a year and a half further from it, whatever it is, and Ilse says a season is worth buying and she has never once been wrong about that.',NULL,1,'brought_it_down','success','[{"set_flag":"undercut_fate","value":"down"},{"pressure":4},{"approval":{"ilse":18,"aldric":10,"kessa":6,"sera":-8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_thing_under_the_quarry'),'left_it_cutting','Left cutting',NULL,'I stood at the chalk line, looked at four inches of the wrong-coloured stone, and went back along the launder. They will be through it inside the month. Somebody will be standing there when they are, and it will be a man on one and threepence a day who was told to keep cutting.',NULL,1,'left_it_cutting','neutral','[{"set_flag":"undercut_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"ilse":-10,"kessa":-8}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_undertown_court'),'go_down_with_rilk','Go down with Rilk','Rilk is offering to walk you in. Decide whether to let him.','Rilk stands at the east gate looking at hands and has never had a night''s trouble from the watch, which I had put down to luck. It is not luck. He goes home through a grating. He says the Low Court has my name and would like it explained, and that people who make the Court come and get them do not enjoy the walk.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'east_gate'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_undertown_court'),'stand_before_the_bench','The bench','Aggie Slate sits the plank. Find out what the charge is.','A scaffold plank across two barrels, worn smooth in the middle, and about sixty people who have stopped what they were doing. Aggie Slate has sat that plank eleven years. The Court''s whole law is three lines long and the third line is that it is read out to your face before anything else happens.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'low_court'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_undertown_court'),'stood_trial','Tried',NULL,'I stood up in front of sixty people in a brick room and answered for what I had done down there, and the Court took an hour over it, and the finding was not what I would have given myself in either direction. I paid what they set. Aggie Slate filed a notch in a piece of slate and gave it to me, which means the book is closed and that I may come and go, and she made a point of saying that the second part is the smaller half.',NULL,1,'stood_trial','success','[{"set_flag":"undertown_court_fate","value":"tried"},{"give_item":"court_slate","quantity":1},{"approval":{"aldric":12,"ilse":10,"kessa":4,"sera":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_undertown_court'),'bought_the_bench','Paid off',NULL,'A hundred and twenty gold, handed over in front of everybody, which is how they do it — there is no such thing down there as a bribe taken quietly, because the whole point of the Court is that it happens in the room. It went into the Court''s box. The finding was recorded as bought. Aggie Slate says the record matters more than the money and that in eleven years exactly four people have chosen it, and that she can tell me what happened to all four.',NULL,1,'bought_the_bench','success','[{"set_flag":"undertown_court_fate","value":"bought"},{"take_gold":120},{"approval":{"sera":8,"kessa":-4,"aldric":-8,"ilse":-8}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_undertown_court'),'refused_the_court','Walked out',NULL,'I told sixty people living in a drain that they had no standing to try anybody and I walked out through the ones who tried to stop me. Nobody died. Two of them will not use that arm properly again. Undertown is shut to me now in the way a town is shut to you — nothing barred, everything simply not there when I arrive.',NULL,1,'refused_the_court','success','[{"set_flag":"undertown_court_fate","value":"refused"},{"set_flag":"undertown_closed"},{"approval":{"kessa":-6,"aldric":-14,"ilse":-14,"sera":2}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_undertown_court'),'sat_the_bench','On the plank',NULL,'The charge against me was dropped in about four minutes once it was said out loud, and then Aggie Slate asked me to sit the plank for the next case, because the next case was one of theirs against one of theirs and the Court''s rule is that the bench must be a stranger when it can get one. I sat on a scaffold plank for two hours and decided something about a stolen lamp and a broken hand, and I have thought about it more since than about anything else I did that month.',NULL,1,'sat_the_bench','success','[{"set_flag":"undertown_court_fate","value":"bench"},{"set_flag":"sat_the_low_bench"},{"give_item":"court_slate","quantity":1},{"approval":{"ilse":14,"aldric":10,"kessa":8,"sera":4}}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_wardens_count'),'the_tally','Read the tally','Find the watchman who carries the warden''s book and get him to open it.','The hill warden sends a count down to Rivermark every fortnight. It goes to the mearing stone with a watchman called Gest Pyle and from there to a shelf. Two years of it, and nobody has read a line.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'boundary_stone'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_wardens_count'),'count_them_yourself','Count them yourself','The book says one thing forwards. Go and see which way it should be read.','Read forwards, the tally says: more of them every spring. Read backwards it says the same families, one gallery further up the hill each year, and fewer of them arriving each time. It is not a count of an invasion. It is a count of a retreat, taken from the wrong end.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'warren_nests'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_wardens_count'),'counted_true','The count, corrected',NULL,'We recounted it in front of Pyle and put the correction in the front of the book in plain words, so that the next person to open it does not have to be clever. Four hundred and six above ground, of whom a hundred and ten are under six winters. Pyle carried it down. Reed read it. She did not say anything for a while.',NULL,1,'counted_true','success','[{"set_flag":"wardens_count_fate","value":"true"},{"set_flag":"warren_numbers_known"},{"give_item":"wardens_tally","quantity":1},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"ilse":18,"aldric":8,"kessa":-4,"sera":2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_wardens_count'),'counted_for_the_muster','The count, as a number',NULL,'Four hundred and six is a number a town can act on and I gave it to the watch as a number. Reed has the count, the gate is shut at dusk, and there is a muster list on the door of the Flagon with eleven names on it. Nobody down there has asked what the other column means.',NULL,1,'counted_for_the_muster','success','[{"set_flag":"wardens_count_fate","value":"muster"},{"set_flag":"warren_numbers_known"},{"set_flag":"rivermark_mustering"},{"give_gold":60},{"approval":{"kessa":10,"ilse":-20,"aldric":-8,"sera":4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_wardens_count'),'left_the_book','Put back on the shelf',NULL,'I gave Pyle his book back and told him it was the watch''s business. He agreed with me and looked relieved about it, and that is two of us who have now decided not to read it.',NULL,1,'left_the_book','neutral','[{"set_flag":"wardens_count_fate","value":"unread"},{"approval":{"ilse":-10,"kessa":2}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_warrens_children'),'the_nest_ledges','The nest ledges','Nakka has offered to show you the low galleries. Go and look.','Nakka Skarn has offered to walk us along the low gallery, which she has not done for anyone from the valley, and she said so in the tone of somebody stating a price rather than doing a favour.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'warren_nests'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_warrens_children'),'a_hundred_and_ten','A hundred and ten','Work out what the numbers mean for the winter.','Four hundred and six above ground. A hundred and ten of them under six winters. Goblin young cannot be walked more than four miles in a day and cannot be walked at all below freezing, which means the warren cannot move before spring and cannot feed itself where it is past midwinter. Nakka has known this since the summer. She has been buying salt and iron and not food, because you cannot store food you have not got.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'warren_nests'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_warrens_children'),'moved_them_north','Moved north',NULL,'The north ford is passable to a slow column for eleven days either side of midwinter and nobody in Rivermark holds it, which is why nobody in Rivermark had thought about it. We walked it, marked it, and got Reed to agree in writing not to post the crossing until spring — not to help, she was clear about that, but not to be the reason. A hundred and ten children went over it in three nights. Nakka did not thank anybody and did not sleep for the three nights.',NULL,1,'moved_them_north','success','[{"set_flag":"children_fate","value":"moved"},{"set_flag":"north_ford_open"},{"xp":200},{"approval":{"ilse":22,"aldric":16,"kessa":-8,"sera":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_warrens_children'),'fed_them_through','Fed through the winter',NULL,'Eleven wagons of pease, barley and salt fish over five weeks, bought at market price with our own money and one loan I would rather not describe, delivered to the warren gate in daylight where anyone could see it. Rivermark has an opinion about that and half of the opinion is that we are provisioning a siege against ourselves. They stay where they are. In spring the same problem will still be there and it will be four months older.',NULL,1,'fed_them_through','success','[{"set_flag":"children_fate","value":"fed"},{"set_flag":"warren_fed"},{"take_gold":200},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"aldric":20,"ilse":14,"sera":-10,"kessa":-6}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_warrens_children'),'told_the_watch','Told the watch',NULL,'I gave Reed the galleries: where they are, how to get to them, and what is in them. She wrote it down and asked me twice whether I was certain about the second column, and I said I was. She has not done anything with it. She has it, and she will have it in the spring, and having it is the whole of what I did.',NULL,1,'told_the_watch','neutral','[{"set_flag":"children_fate","value":"told"},{"set_flag":"warren_nests_known_to_watch"},{"give_gold":120},{"approval":{"kessa":6,"sera":6,"ilse":-28,"aldric":-22}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_watch_payroll'),'ask_the_clerk','Ask the counting house','Find out where the watch''s wages are coming from.','Reed signs the watch roll every quarter day and every quarter day the money is there. She has never once had to argue with the council about it, which she now finds remarkable, because she has had to argue about the price of lamp oil twice this year.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'counting_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_watch_payroll'),'the_standing_order','The shortfall','Somebody makes up the difference. Find out who.','The town account pays about two thirds of the watch roll. The rest arrives four days before each quarter day from a house account at Greyhythe, by letter, and the letters are not kept because the instruction each time is that they are not to be. Tibald Ashe has never met anyone connected with it. He has been putting it through the book for fourteen months and he has been unhappy about it for thirteen.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'counting_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_watch_payroll'),'refused_the_money','Sent back',NULL,'Reed sent the quarter back and told the council to find it. The council found about half. Four men left the watch inside the month — two of them to the granary, which pays better and always did — and the night patrol on the west side has been dropped. Reed says she will take a smaller watch that is hers over a whole one that is somebody else''s, and she says it like a woman who has thought about very little else for a fortnight.',NULL,1,'refused_the_money','success','[{"set_flag":"watch_payroll_fate","value":"refused"},{"set_flag":"watch_thin"},{"approval":{"ilse":10,"aldric":8,"kessa":-4,"sera":-6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_watch_payroll'),'let_it_stand','Nothing said',NULL,'Reed let it stand. Twenty-six men are paid on the day, the west side is patrolled at night, and the alternative was a watch of eighteen. She wrote a note of it in her own book, in her own hand, and did not put it in the day book where it would be read. We have not spoken about it since.',NULL,1,'let_it_stand','success','[{"set_flag":"watch_payroll_fate","value":"kept"},{"set_flag":"reed_took_it"},{"approval":{"sera":8,"kessa":4,"aldric":-8,"ilse":-6}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'the_watch_payroll'),'told_the_watch','The watch is told',NULL,'I told the watch themselves, in the guardroom, with Reed standing there because I was not going to do it behind her. They took it about as well as men take that. They have all kept the money. Six of them have stopped calling her Captain when she is not in the room, and Ballow, who has twenty-two years in, said the thing everybody was thinking: then who is it we work for, and how would we know.',NULL,1,'told_the_watch','success','[{"set_flag":"watch_payroll_fate","value":"told"},{"set_flag":"watch_knows"},{"pressure":1},{"approval":{"ilse":6,"kessa":8,"aldric":-4,"sera":-8}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'tobins_consignment'),'go_and_look','Look at the crate','Find out what is actually on the quay.','Tobin has been invoiced for twelve hundredweight of coarse salt he did not order. It is good salt and he could sell it in a week, which is the part that is bothering him: nobody plays a trick on a man by giving him something he can sell.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'river_stair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'tobins_consignment'),'the_quay_book','The quay master''s book','Find out who the salt was really for.','The bill of lading names a consignee in a clerk''s copperplate. Mott Wenn has never heard of him and Mott has carried up everything that has come off a boat here for nine years. The same name is on eleven other bills in the quay book going back to spring — salt, lime, lamp oil, rope, and two hundred feet of pine board. None of it was collected by anyone who signed for it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'river_stair'),0,NULL,'success','[{"give_item":"lading_bill","quantity":1}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'tobins_consignment'),'paid_and_kept','Paid, and sold on',NULL,'Tobin paid the carriage and sold the salt inside the fortnight at a profit he was not comfortable with. His name is now in the quay book as the man who received that consignment, in his own hand, next to eleven others he has nothing to do with. He said: I have made forty gold and acquired a history.',NULL,1,'paid_and_kept','success','[{"set_flag":"consignment_fate","value":"kept"},{"set_flag":"tobin_named"},{"take_item":"lading_bill"},{"give_gold":60},{"approval":{"sera":6,"aldric":-6,"kessa":-2}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'tobins_consignment'),'refused_the_crate','Refused, and watched',NULL,'Tobin refused it and the crate sat on the landing for four days going nobody''s. On the fifth night two men came up the stair with a handcart, produced no paper, argued with nobody, and took it away downriver. Mott watched them do it and did not stop them, because nobody had told him to, and because they were extremely ordinary men doing an extremely ordinary job.',NULL,1,'refused_the_crate','success','[{"set_flag":"consignment_fate","value":"refused"},{"take_item":"lading_bill"},{"approval":{"kessa":6,"ilse":6,"sera":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'tobins_consignment'),'gave_reed_the_bill','The bill goes to the captain',NULL,'Reed took the bill of lading and sent to Greyhythe about the name on it. The answer came back in nineteen days: the consignee is a real man, of a real address, and he has been dead for two years, and his estate has never been closed. She wrote it in the day book. There is nothing in Rivermark''s law that makes a dead man receiving salt an offence.',NULL,1,'gave_reed_the_bill','success','[{"set_flag":"consignment_fate","value":"watch"},{"pressure":1},{"take_item":"lading_bill"},{"approval":{"aldric":8,"ilse":4,"sera":-6,"kessa":-2}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_bottom_of_the_stair'),'go_to_the_bottom','As far down as it goes','Reach the fifth floor of the Undervault and come back to tell Orrin Bly.','Bly writes down who goes down and who comes up, and beside it how deep they say they got. The deepest figure on the slate is a four, entered six years ago by a woman who did not go down again. He wants to know whether there is a bottom or whether the stair just keeps offering.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'uv_mouth'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_bottom_of_the_stair'),'told_him','There is a bottom',NULL,'Five floors, and below the fifth the stair does not offer. Bly ruled a line under the four, wrote the five beneath it, and then sat for a while without writing anything else.',NULL,1,'told_him','success','[{"xp":200}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_first_step'),'go_down','Down the stair','Go down into the Undervault, and come back up.','The stove-keeper in the long tent keeps a board of names with a mark against each for every time they have come back. A name with no mark on it is somebody she is still waiting on. She would rather I were a mark.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'uv_mouth'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_first_step'),'came_back','Came back up',NULL,'One floor down and back out the same hole. Marda made the mark, said the number out loud the way she does, and put the chalk back on the ledge.',NULL,1,'came_back','success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_three_floors'),'go_deeper','Three floors','Get three floors down into the Undervault, and come back up to say so.','Marda has eleven accounts of the third floor and no two of them describe the same place. She has stopped expecting them to agree and started collecting them anyway, which she says is the only honest thing to do with a hole that will not hold still.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'uv_mouth'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_three_floors'),'came_back','Told her what was down there',NULL,'Three floors, and mine matched none of the eleven either. She wrote it down without arguing, the way somebody writes down a twelfth thing.',NULL,1,'came_back','success','[{"xp":100}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_where_they_were_left'),'look_for_him','Go and look','Get three floors down and look for the fourth gallery.','Tam Kell went down eleven weeks ago and did not come up. The three who did come up told his sister three different galleries — the fourth, the one under the fall, and one nobody else has heard of — and she has spent eleven weeks deciding they were lying. She has given me his crew tag. The other one is on him.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'uv_mouth'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_where_they_were_left'),'told_her','Told her the truth',NULL,'There is no fourth gallery. There is no third. What is down there is not the same twice and does not keep what you leave in it, and the three who came up were not lying to her — they were each describing the only place they saw. I told her that, and she took a while over it, and then she said that was the first thing anybody had said to her in eleven weeks that could not also have been a kindness.',NULL,1,'told_her','success','[{"xp":150}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'uv_where_they_were_left'),'let_her_believe','Let her believe it',NULL,'I said I found the fourth gallery and the marker at the head of it, and that he was past it, and that it was quick. She paid me out of a purse she had clearly been keeping ready for the answer. She will stop coming up the heap now, which was the point, and I do not know whose.',NULL,1,'let_her_believe','success','[{"give_gold":120}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_floats'),'the_black_pools','The black pools','Go out to the peat cuttings and see what is in them.','The old peat cuttings have flooded into a chain of pools deeper than a pole will find. Things come up in them and stay up, because peat water preserves what it takes and never gives it back.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'black_pools'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_floats'),'all_facing_one_way','All facing one way','Get them out of the water and look at them properly.','Seven of them. Not one is from the drowned village — the village went under forty years ago and these have been in the water for two years at the outside. All seven are men between twenty and forty, and all seven have the same wear in the same place: the right shoulder, in a band, the way a shoulder goes when it has carried a yoke or a pick for a very long time. They are all lying with their heads toward the sluice.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'black_pools'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_floats'),'named_them','Named',NULL,'Two of the seven had marks that could be read: a guild tattoo from a stone-cutters'' house four days downriver, and a wedding band with a date in it. Neither of them is from this valley. Neither of them was reported missing to anybody, anywhere, and both of them had been working with their hands until about a fortnight before they went in the water.',NULL,1,'named_them','success','[{"set_flag":"floats_fate","value":"named"},{"set_flag":"pool_dead_named"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"sera":12,"aldric":10,"ilse":6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_floats'),'gave_them_ground','Given ground',NULL,'There is no dry ground in the fen worth the name, so we took them up to the village and laid them in the chapel, which has a stone floor above the waterline and has not had anybody in it for forty years. Aldric''s order has words for this and I do not, so I said the ones I could remember and we shut the door.',NULL,1,'gave_them_ground','success','[{"set_flag":"floats_fate","value":"buried"},{"set_flag":"pool_dead_buried"},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"aldric":18,"ilse":10,"kessa":6,"sera":-2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_floats'),'left_them_floating','Left in the water',NULL,'Seven men in black water, all lying the same way, none of them anything to do with me. I know that the pools are two hours off the causeway and that nobody goes there, and I have decided that is the same thing as nobody knowing.',NULL,1,'left_them_floating','neutral','[{"set_flag":"floats_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"aldric":-12,"ilse":-6,"kessa":-4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_goes_out'),'find_the_way_under','Under the quay','Get into the Underquay.','Twenty women have watched the Great Crane lift the same kind of load twice a year for two years, and every time, the lighter it comes off is riding lower going out than it did coming in. Tam wants somebody to go and look at what is under the stone.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'underquay_stair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_goes_out'),'the_deep_store','The dry room','Find what the Underquay is actually for.','There is a room down there above the tide-mark with new boards on new joists, and it is a granary, and it is a better granary than the League''s.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_deep_store'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_goes_out'),'whose_grain','Whose grain','Find out who keeps the book.','Eighty quarters of League grain in League sacking, dunnaged, swept, kept properly. Not hoarded — held. Somebody in this city has been taking grain off the top for six years and storing it where the Factor''s seals are not, and doing it well, and I do not yet know whether that is a theft or a granary.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_quiet_charter'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_goes_out'),'seized','Taken back',NULL,'The Underquay store is the Factor''s now, on paper, in daylight, and the arrangement that fed the Wardenswatch for six years is finished. Eighty quarters into the granary. Nineteen hundred people off the only supply that was ever actually theirs.',NULL,1,'seized','success','[{"set_flag":"charter_fate","value":"seized"},{"xp":150}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_goes_out'),'bought_in','Bought in',NULL,'I did not close it. I got a share of it, and a key, and a share of the blame if it is ever opened. The Charter keeps running. It feeds the people the charter says are not there, out of grain that the charter says is not missing, and now I am in the arrangement rather than looking at it.',NULL,1,'bought_in','success','[{"set_flag":"charter_fate","value":"bought_in"},{"give_gold":180}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_goes_out'),'burned','Burned out',NULL,'The tide gate is down, the store is spoiled, and the Charter''s book went into the fifth hearth at the Boom Forge in front of a witness. Nobody will run grain under this quay again. Nobody will run anything under it again, including the people.',NULL,1,'burned','success','[{"set_flag":"charter_fate","value":"burned"},{"xp":150}]',5),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_rivermark_is_worth'),'the_figure','The figure','Every drawer in the long room is labelled by year and by hundred. Find the one Rivermark is in.','The long room is not locked and the drawers are labelled in one hand and there is no reason on earth why I should not open them. That is the third time this week that a thing has been left open to me and I have found it worse than a lock.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_long_room'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_rivermark_is_worth'),'found_the_number','Sheet six',NULL,'Rivermark: eleven hundred souls, four hundred and six roofs, a granary, a bridge, two mills of which one is burnt, and a total. The total is less than the crane on the new landing cost. It is not written cruelly. It is not written at all — it is added up, in a column, between a weir and a stand of oak, by somebody being paid by the day to add things up.',NULL,1,'found_the_number','success','[{"set_flag":"worth_fate","value":"found"},{"set_flag":"rivermark_valued"},{"pressure":1},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"aldric":10,"ilse":10,"kessa":8,"sera":6}}]',1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_rivermark_is_worth'),'did_not_look','Left in the drawer',NULL,'I stood in front of the drawer with my hand on it for a while. There is a version of this where I never know the number and the number does not exist, and I am aware that it is not a very good version, and I closed the press anyway.',NULL,1,'did_not_look','neutral','[{"set_flag":"worth_fate","value":"looked_away"},{"approval":{"sera":-8,"ilse":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_houses_owe'),'the_bench','The bench','Let Nessa show you the tally.','Six years, four hundred hands, paid in a tin token redeemable at one cart. She has the tokens issued and the oakum sold and the difference, and she has had the difference for a year and has not shown it to a living soul.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_oakum_house'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_houses_owe'),'the_reckoning','In front of her grandmother','Decide where the number gets said.','Mother Reth genuinely believes she is the only person in Waerhaven who feeds the poor. The tally does not say she is wrong. It says what she has charged them for it.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_pitch_yards'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_houses_owe'),'split','Split',NULL,'She read it out in the pitch yard in front of both her uncles and left the same evening with what she could carry. The Houses will not change. Four hundred people now know a number they did not know, and Nessa says that is not nothing and does not sound convinced.',NULL,1,'split','success','[{"set_flag":"nessa_fate","value":"split"},{"approval":{"nessa_reth":15}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_houses_owe'),'stayed','Stayed',NULL,'She gave the tally to her grandmother privately and the bread ration went up a third the following week and no reason was given for it. Nobody knows. Nessa knows. She says that is how it is actually done and she may be right, and she has not been sleeping.',NULL,1,'stayed','success','[{"set_flag":"nessa_fate","value":"stayed"},{"approval":{"nessa_reth":10}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_mere_gives_back'),'the_locked_room','The back room','Get Sister Nairn to unlock it.','She has been collecting them for six years because putting them back feels like an insult to something. She has not counted them. That is the sentence she said, and the way she said it was the thing worth noticing.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'temple_of_the_deep_mere'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_mere_gives_back'),'the_drowned_room','The room that does not drain','Go down into the Underquay and look at the bottom.','The Waerfolk have a name for one room under the old quay and use it about once a generation. What is on the bottom of it was put there rather than lost there, and it is laid out, and the laying out is recent.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_drowned_room'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_mere_gives_back'),'answered','Answered',NULL,'Six years of returned offerings went back over the rail in one afternoon with the whole of Old Waer standing on the shingle, and every one of them was named as it went, by the person who threw it, out loud. Nothing came back. Sister Nairn says that is not the same as being forgiven and she is right, and she is also the only person on this shore who looks like she slept.',NULL,1,'answered','success','[{"set_flag":"mere_fate","value":"answered"},{"give_item":"mere_token","quantity":1},{"xp":220}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_mere_gives_back'),'quiet','Kept quiet',NULL,'The room stays locked and the Temple stays quiet and the Waerfolk go on throwing things into forty fathoms and going down at dawn to see what is on the shingle. Sister Nairn was relieved. She was relieved in the way you are relieved when somebody agrees not to look at a thing you have been looking at alone for six years.',NULL,1,'quiet','neutral','[{"set_flag":"mere_fate","value":"quiet"}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_quarry_fell_on'),'the_floor_of_the_warren','Down what replaced the floor','The warren''s floor did not fall in. Go and see what took it out.','Ilse has been saying for two years that something is taking the bottom of the warren floor by floor. She was right about the fact and wrong about the verb. Nothing is taking it. Somebody is buying it out, a course at a time, and paying men to carry it away.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'spoil_stair'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_quarry_fell_on'),'the_works','Walk the works','Nobody has stopped you yet. Walk it, and count what you see.','Sawn treads. A handrail. A bucket of sand on every landing in case of fire. Below that, a plank floor the size of the market square, a bell, a board of numbered pegs, a canteen and two hundred people working in shifts. There is nothing hidden about any of it. It is simply eleven miles from anybody who would object.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'the_headings'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_quarry_fell_on'),'walked_the_works','Two hundred people',NULL,'I walked the whole of it and was stopped once, politely, by a woman with a water clock who wanted to know my peg number. Six faces being cut at a costed rate toward one point under the old quarry. Nobody down there knows what is at the point. Nobody down there has asked. They are paid by the day, and the day is the only unit anybody in that hole thinks in.',NULL,1,'walked_the_works','success','[{"set_flag":"quarry_fell_fate","value":"walked"},{"set_flag":"deepworks_known"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"ilse":14,"sera":8,"aldric":6,"kessa":4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_quarry_fell_on'),'turned_back','Back up the stair',NULL,'I got as far as the muster floor, watched a bell ring and forty people change direction, and went back up the stair. I have not told Ilse what is under her warren. I am not sure which part of it I am afraid of.',NULL,1,'turned_back','neutral','[{"set_flag":"quarry_fell_fate","value":"back"},{"set_flag":"deepworks_known"},{"approval":{"ilse":-6,"kessa":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_water_left'),'find_the_strongroom','Find the strongroom','Get into the drowned counting room.','Dov says there is a room off the low conduit that is not a drain — a proper room, with a cornice, under two feet of water, and an iron door at the back standing open. Dov has been in as far as the door twice and no further, and Dov goes everywhere.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'drowned_counting_room'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_water_left'),'the_boxes','The boxes','Find out what is still in the strongroom.','Forty-odd iron deposit boxes on racks, chest-deep, each with a brass plate and a name cut into it, and every one of them still shut. And a man, or what forty years of standing water leaves of one, who has never once come out past the door.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'drowned_counting_room'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_water_left'),'took_the_silver','Taken',NULL,'Two hundred and fifty gold in plate, coin and one very good ring, out of eleven boxes belonging to eleven people who are mostly dead. I told myself the whole way up the conduit that a bank that has been shut forty years has no depositors, only heirs, and that heirs who have not come for it in forty years are not coming. That is true. It also took me the whole way up the conduit.',NULL,1,'took_the_silver','success','[{"set_flag":"strongroom_fate","value":"took"},{"give_gold":250},{"approval":{"kessa":6,"sera":6,"aldric":-12,"ilse":-6}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_water_left'),'returned_the_boxes','Given back',NULL,'Nine of the forty-one names still have somebody in Rivermark answering to them. Three of those are on Dagen Wyke''s list. I carried nine boxes up a drain and gave them to people who had been told all their lives that the money was gone, and one of them, a woman of about seventy, sat down on the step and would not open hers, and said she would rather have the box.',NULL,1,'returned_the_boxes','success','[{"set_flag":"strongroom_fate","value":"returned"},{"give_gold":60},{"approval":{"aldric":14,"ilse":10,"kessa":6,"sera":-4}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'what_the_water_left'),'took_the_book','The deposit book',NULL,'I left the boxes and took the book, because the book is the thing that was worth carrying. Two hundred and six depositors, what each of them lodged, and the last eleven entries: one week, all withdrawals, all to the bank''s own partners, all dated before the flood. The Fennow did not fail in the water. It was emptied first and the water arrived in time to be blamed.',NULL,1,'took_the_book','success','[{"set_flag":"strongroom_fate","value":"ledger"},{"give_item":"fennow_ledger","quantity":1},{"approval":{"sera":12,"ilse":8,"aldric":4}}]',4),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'wolves_in_winter_field'),'the_far_corner','The far corner','Go out to Winter Field and see what the cattle are looking at.','The beasts on Winter Field are bunched in the far corner facing the thorn brake and will not graze within forty paces of it. Nobody has cut the thorn back in two years.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'winter_field'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,0),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'wolves_in_winter_field'),'the_thorn_brake','The thorn brake','Go into the thorn and finish it.','There is a channel dragged through the grass into the thorn, and it has been used more than once. Four of them: two big ones and two half-grown, all thin, all working the field from the fen side.',(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE location_key = 'winter_field'),0,NULL,'success',NULL,1),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'wolves_in_winter_field'),'killed_the_pack','Killed',NULL,'Four of them and all four down in the brake, which took longer than it should have because the thorn is on their side and not ours. The herd was grazing the far corner within the hour. That is the whole of it, and not everything needs to be more than that.',NULL,1,'killed_the_pack','success','[{"set_flag":"wolves_fate","value":"killed"},{"xp":100},{"approval":{"kessa":8,"sera":4,"ilse":-4}}]',2),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'wolves_in_winter_field'),'found_the_den','The den',NULL,'The den is on the fen side of the thorn, dug into the old bank, and it is dry — which it should not be, because it is four feet below the level of the winter field and the winter field is standing in water. The water is on the wrong side of the bank. They did not come up onto the grazing because they were hungry. They came up because their ground went under.',NULL,1,'found_the_den','success','[{"set_flag":"wolves_fate","value":"den"},{"set_flag":"fen_water_rising"},{"xp":150},{"approval":{"ilse":14,"aldric":4,"kessa":2}}]',3),
((SELECT id FROM quests WHERE quest_key = 'wolves_in_winter_field'),'left_them_to_it','Left in the thorn',NULL,'Four of them, all thin, and the field is common ground that nobody has paid me to keep. I walked away from it. The drovers will lose beasts and the beasts will be lost either way, and I am not going to pretend I worked that out at the time.',NULL,1,'left_them_to_it','neutral','[{"set_flag":"wolves_fate","value":"left"},{"approval":{"kessa":-6,"sera":-4}}]',4)
