"label":"How long have you gone without speaking to anybody?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_alone"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_alone"},{"label":"When were you last wrong about the hill?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_wrong"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_wrong"},{"label":"Eleven years is not long, for you.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_years"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_years"},{"label":"Teach me to read the ground properly. Not the tour — the work.","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_ground"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_teach"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_teach"}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"ilse"}],"pool":"cool","text":"Ilse looks up, and looks back at the ground, and moves her chin about an inch, which is where you may sit. She does not say anything after that.","choices":[{"label":"How do you read a hillside?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_ground"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_ground"},{"label":"Four pounds of salt, every fortnight.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_salt"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_salt"},{"label":"How did you come by this hill?","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":15},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"},{"label":"What did the first winter look like, from up here?","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":40},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_first_winter"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_first_winter"},{"label":"Where do you keep the book?","conditions":[{"flag":"deep_known"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_the_book"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_the_book"},{"label":"Reed wants a warden''s word on the raids.","conditions":[{"quest":"teeth_in_the_hills","stage":"find_the_warden"}],"next":"camp_ilse_the_road"},{"label":"The shaft. Do you sleep, since?","conditions":[{"flag":"deep_shaft_fate"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_fate_told"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_fate"},{"label":"Ground and weather are done. What''s the third thing?","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_locked":true}}],"next":"ilse_close"},{"label":"Stay by the fire tonight.","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}],"next":"romance_after"},{"label":"Get some sleep.","end":true},{"label":"You keep two books. What is in the other one?","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_the_book"},{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":15},{"not":{"flag":"ilse_names_known"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_the_names"},{"label":"There is nothing cut over Corran Vale.","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_corran_stone"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_corran_stone"},{"label":"When did anybody last act on your count?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_believed"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_believed"},{"label":"How long have you gone without speaking to anybody?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_alone"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_alone"},{"label":"When were you last wrong about the hill?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_wrong"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_wrong"},{"label":"Eleven years is not long, for you.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_years"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_years"},{"label":"Teach me to read the ground properly. Not the tour — the work.","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_ground"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_teach"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_teach"}]},{"expression":1,"text":"Ilse is sitting outside the firelight and upwind of it, where she can see the whole approach and you can barely see her. She does not object to being spoken to. She simply does not move any closer while it happens.","choices":[{"label":"How do you read a hillside?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_ground"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_ground"},{"label":"Four pounds of salt, every fortnight.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_salt"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_salt"},{"label":"How did you come by this hill?","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":15},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"},{"label":"What did the first winter look like, from up here?","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":40},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_first_winter"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_first_winter"},{"label":"Where do you keep the book?","conditions":[{"flag":"deep_known"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_the_book"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_the_book"},{"label":"Reed wants a warden''s word on the raids.","conditions":[{"quest":"teeth_in_the_hills","stage":"find_the_warden"}],"next":"camp_ilse_the_road"},{"label":"The shaft. Do you sleep, since?","conditions":[{"flag":"deep_shaft_fate"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_fate_told"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_fate"},{"label":"Ground and weather are done. What''s the third thing?","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_locked":true}}],"next":"ilse_close"},{"label":"Stay by the fire tonight.","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}],"next":"romance_after"},{"label":"Get some sleep.","end":true},{"label":"You keep two books. What is in the other one?","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_the_book"},{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":15},{"not":{"flag":"ilse_names_known"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_the_names"},{"label":"There is nothing cut over Corran Vale.","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_corran_stone"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_corran_stone"},{"label":"When did anybody last act on your count?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_believed"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_believed"},{"label":"How long have you gone without speaking to anybody?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_alone"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_alone"},{"label":"When were you last wrong about the hill?","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_wrong"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_wrong"},{"label":"Eleven years is not long, for you.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_years"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_years"},{"label":"Teach me to read the ground properly. Not the tour — the work.","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_ground"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_ilse_teach"}}],"next":"camp_ilse_teach"}]}],"camp_ilse_ground":[{"expression":3,"text":"\\"You do not read it. You count it.\\" She does not point; she moves her chin. \\"Three deer paths off that saddle and one of them has prints going both ways. Bracken standing on the north face means nothing has bedded there this week. The water out of the cut runs brown two days after rain and clear on the third, so if it is brown on the fourth, somebody upstream is digging.\\" She stops herself. \\"You asked a question that has an answer. I am aware I have given you a great deal of it.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_ground"}],"choices":[{"label":"Give me more of it.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":3}}],"next":"camp_ilse_ground_more"},{"label":"Nobody in that town has ever asked you that.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_ground_more":[{"expression":2,"text":"So she does, for the better part of an hour, and stops only because the fire wants building. It is the most words you have heard out of her at one sitting, and eleven of them are the names of grasses.","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_salt":[{"expression":1,"text":"\\"Four pounds does a fortnight. Two for the meat, one for the hides, and one that the road takes off me somewhere between the stall and the ridge, and I have given up finding out where.\\" She turns a stick in the fire. \\"It is the only thing I buy. The rest the hill gives me or I do without, and there is a great deal I do without, and I would rather you did not make a story out of that.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_salt"}],"choices":[{"label":"You walk nine miles for salt and you are home before dark.","next":"camp"},{"label":"I will carry it next time.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":2}}],"next":"camp_ilse_salt_carry"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_salt_carry":[{"expression":2,"text":"\\"You will not,\\" Ilse says, and then hears herself say it. \\"— You may. Yes. Thank you. I have been on my own long enough that the first answer arrives before I have looked at the question.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_eleven_years":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"}],"expression":4,"text":"\\"Corran Vale had it thirty-one years and I have had it eleven, and neither of us was paid for the back half,\\" Ilse says. \\"You have had that. I do not improve it by telling it twice.\\"","choices":[{"label":"No.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]},{"expression":4,"text":"\\"There was a warden before me and his name was Corran Vale and he had the hill thirty-one years.\\" She says it the way a date is cut on a stone. \\"He walked me the whole boundary twice, and then went down to Rivermark to argue for his stipend, and did not come back up it. They had voted the stipend away in the spring and nobody had thought to write and tell him.\\" She turns the stick over. \\"It has not been paid since. I have had the hill eleven years and been paid for none of them. I am not complaining. I am telling you what a warden is. A warden is whoever has not stopped.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_eleven_years"}],"choices":[{"label":"Then that town owes you eleven years.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":3}}],"next":"camp_ilse_owed"},{"label":"Nobody asked you to stay up here.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-4}}],"next":"camp_ilse_nobody_asked"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_owed":[{"expression":2,"text":"\\"It owes Corran Vale thirty-one,\\" Ilse says. \\"Start there. He is under the turf by the ford with nothing cut over him. I have thought about cutting something and have not, because he would have called it a wasted afternoon and he would have been right, and I would like to be wrong about it in front of somebody one day.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_nobody_asked":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"No,\\" Ilse agrees, pleasantly enough. \\"Nobody asked. That is the arrangement and I have never once misunderstood it.\\" She takes the bow and is forty feet out on the flank again inside a minute, and the fire is a good deal colder for the rest of the night.","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_first_winter":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_first_winter"}],"expression":5,"text":"\\"The ford, the fourth night, eighty yards,\\" Ilse says. \\"You have it. I have not found a way of telling it that comes out better, and I have tried in the dark a number of times.\\"","choices":[{"label":"You do not have to tell it better.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]},{"expression":5,"text":"\\"Six days, and I was on the north spur for four of them.\\" She is entirely level about it. \\"They did not come over as a column. They came over in families, at night, in snow, with the small ones tied on. I lay up in the bracken with a bow and a book and counted them, because that is the job, and by the second night I understood that nothing was chasing them — that whatever they were running from was underneath.\\" She stops long enough that the fire shifts. \\"On the fourth night one of them went through the ice at the ford, eighty yards from where I was lying. I counted her. I did not go down.\\" She looks at the flames rather than at you. \\"I have given this town four years of very good argument on their behalf and none of it is kindness. It is that I did not go down that night, and it is the only thing I have ever done that is not in the book.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_first_winter"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric: \\"A bow, a book, and eighty yards of black ice.\\" Ilse: \\"Yes. I have had four years to make that sound like a reason.\\""},{"companion":"kessa","text":"Kessa: \\"I''ve left people. It doesn''t get lighter. It stops being the first thing you think of, is all, and you''ll hate that when it happens.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"You have been going down ever since. Slowly.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":5}}],"next":"camp_ilse_going_down"},{"label":"You should have gone down.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-3}}],"next":"camp_ilse_should_have"},{"label":"Let it be, tonight.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_going_down":[{"expression":2,"text":"Ilse does not answer that for a long time. \\"That is a kind arrangement of it,\\" she says at last. \\"I am going to take it and not examine it, which is not like me, and you may draw whatever conclusion you please from that.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_should_have":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"Yes,\\" Ilse says. \\"I know. I have put it to myself in better words than yours.\\" She sets another stick on the fire, squarely, and does not look at you again that evening.","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_the_book":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"camp_ilse_the_book"}],"expression":3,"text":"\\"Under the third hearthstone, in an oiled bag,\\" Ilse says. \\"It has not moved and I have not improved the plan.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Improve it.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]},{"expression":5,"text":"\\"There are two,\\" Ilse says. \\"The one I carry, and one that lives in an oiled bag under the third hearthstone of the shelter on the ridge, because a shelter burns and a hearthstone does not.\\" She taps the carried one. \\"Counts, dates, weather, what has come up the shaft and when. If I am killed on this hill somebody will find the shelter inside a season, because the salt stall will notice I have stopped coming, and they will lift the stone, because everybody lifts the stone.\\" A pause. \\"That is the whole of my plan. I have had eleven years to make a better one and this is what I have.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_the_book"}],"choices":[{"label":"Then somebody had better read it while you are alive.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":4}}],"next":"camp_ilse_read_it"},{"label":"A hearthstone is not a plan.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_read_it":[{"expression":3,"text":"\\"That is what I have been asking for since I was given the hill,\\" Ilse says. \\"You are the first one to put it in that order.\\" She holds the book out across the fire without letting go of it for a moment, and then does. \\"Read it now, then. While I am sitting here. I would like to watch somebody do it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_the_road":[{"on_enter":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"teeth_in_the_hills","stage":"the_pattern"}}],"text":"Ilse does not look up. \\"You have had a warden in your camp for a fortnight and Reed has had none in his,\\" she says, and there is no edge on it at all, which is worse. The small book comes out of her coat and opens flat on her knee. \\"Four in six weeks. All of them on the stretch between the cut and the second ford. All of them loaded going out and none of them touched coming back empty.\\" She turns the book so the firelight is on it, though she does not expect you to read the hand. \\"Hungry men take the food wagon and go home. These ones let the food wagon pass. Somebody is reading the manifests before the wheels turn, and I can show you where they wait for the ones worth taking. It is not where the watch has been looking.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Show me.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":2}}],"next":"camp"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_the_names":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"ilse_names_known"}],"text":"\\"Eleven names, dated, with what I said and what they answered,\\" Ilse says. \\"That is the second book and you have had it out of me once, which is once more than anybody else has managed.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then let''s decide what happens to it.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"ilse_second_book_fate"}},{"level_at_least":4}],"next":"the_second_book_choice"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]},{"on_enter":[{"set_flag":"ilse_names_known"}],"text":"Ilse does not answer at all for long enough that you assume she is not going to. Then she says, \\"Counts in the one I carry. The one under the stone is not counts.\\" She turns the stick over in the fire. \\"It is names. Eleven years of who I told, on what day, in what words, and what they said back to me. The reeve twice. The captain before Reed, four times. Three aldermen. A miller. It is written fair, because I write everything fair, and there is a line ruled under each one so that nothing can be added later.\\" She looks at the flames rather than at you. \\"I have never shown it to anybody. I take it out about twice a year and read it through and put it back, and I have stopped being able to tell whether it is evidence or whether it is a grudge that I have been keeping tidy.\\"","choices":[{"label":"It is evidence.","next":"camp_ilse_evidence"},{"label":"It is a grudge. You know it is.","next":"camp_ilse_grudge"},{"label":"Read me one of the entries.","next":"camp_ilse_one_entry"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_evidence":[{"text":"\\"Evidence of what,\\" Ilse says, and it is not rhetorical; she waits. \\"No law was broken. A town declined to act on a warden''s advice, which a town is entitled to do, and eleven men said no in eleven perfectly ordinary sentences, and I wrote every one of them down and ruled a line under it.\\" She sets the stick aside. \\"That is not a case. It is a list of people who disappointed me, kept for eleven years in a fair hand, and I have known that since about the fourth year.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then let''s decide what happens to it.","conditions":[{"level_at_least":4}],"next":"the_second_book_choice"},{"label":"Read me one of the entries.","next":"camp_ilse_one_entry"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_grudge":[{"text":"\\"Yes,\\" Ilse says at once, and there is nothing defensive in it whatever. \\"That is the honest reading and it is why I have never shown it to anybody, because the first person who read it would say what you have just said and I would have to agree with them out loud.\\" She is quiet a moment. \\"Here is the part I cannot get past. Everything in it is true, and it is dated, and it would have been worth having four years ago. A thing can be a grudge and be the only record there is. Nobody has ever told me what one does with that.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then let''s decide what happens to it.","conditions":[{"level_at_least":4}],"next":"the_second_book_choice"},{"label":"Read me one of the entries.","next":"camp_ilse_one_entry"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_one_entry":[{"text":"\\"The second spring. Alderman Haddon Ferrers, at the market cross, in the afternoon, with two of his people standing off.\\" She does not need the book. \\"I said: eleven hundred, and four hundred of them cannot fight, and they are coming down because the deep is shut. He said: warden, if there were eleven hundred of anything on that hill we would know about it. I said: you do know about it, I have just told you. He said — and I have this word for word, because I wrote it in the road before I had got out of the square — he said, then write it down somewhere.\\" Ilse puts another stick on the fire, squarely. \\"So I did. That is the whole of the book and that is the whole of why there is one.\\"","choices":[{"label":"He got exactly what he asked for.","next":"camp_ilse_ferrers"},{"label":"Then let''s decide what happens to it.","conditions":[{"level_at_least":4}],"next":"the_second_book_choice"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_ferrers":[{"text":"\\"He did,\\" Ilse says. \\"He has had it for nine years and he does not know he has, and about once a season I catch myself hoping he finds out.\\" She looks at the fire. \\"That is not what a record is for. I am aware.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then let''s decide what happens to it.","conditions":[{"level_at_least":4}],"next":"the_second_book_choice"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"the_second_book_choice":[{"text":"Ilse goes and gets it. It takes her the better part of an hour, and she comes back with the oiled bag under her coat and puts it on the ground between you unopened, which costs her something to do. \\"Three things and I will not choose,\\" she says. \\"I have had eleven years to and I have not, and that is the answer to what I am.\\" She counts them off. \\"Reed can have it. She will read it, and she will act on it, because she is honest and it is the trouble with her — and six of the men in it are the men who vote her budget, and she will spend the rest of her career paying for the afternoon.\\" Two. \\"Or it goes in the fire, and eleven years of who was told goes with it, and the only account of what this town was warned is the one in their heads.\\" Three. \\"Or you carry it. Not me. It stops being under my stone and starts being in your pack, and I will have to ask you for it if I want it, and I do not know what that will do to me and I would like to find out.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Reed reads it.","effects":[{"set_flag":"ilse_second_book_fate","value":"read"},{"approval":{"ilse":14,"aldric":8,"sera":-6,"kessa":2}},{"xp":200}],"next":"the_names_to_reed"},{"label":"Burn it.","effects":[{"set_flag":"ilse_second_book_fate","value":"burned"},{"approval":{"ilse":10,"sera":8,"kessa":6,"aldric":-4}},{"xp":200}],"next":"the_names_burned"},{"label":"I''ll carry it.","effects":[{"set_flag":"ilse_second_book_fate","value":"kept"},{"approval":{"ilse":16,"sera":-4,"kessa":4}},{"xp":200}],"next":"the_names_carried"},{"label":"Put it back under the stone tonight.","next":"camp"}]}],"the_names_to_reed":[{"text":"Reed reads four pages standing up in the doorway of the watch house with her cloak still on, and then sits down on the step and reads the rest, and does not say anything for some while. Then she says that six of the names are on her own muster and that two of them signed her commission, and she asks Ilse whether she understands what she has handed over. Ilse says that she does. Reed says that she does not think so, and takes it anyway.","choices":[{"label":"Walk her back up the hill.","next":"camp"}]}],"the_names_burned":[{"text":"It takes about as long as a wet season''s kindling, which Ilse says out loud and resents. She stands over it the whole way and turns the last of it with the stick so that nothing survives in the ash that a person could read. Afterward she sits down and opens the carried book and writes up the day: weather, distance, what was on the road. Four lines. Nothing else.","choices":[{"label":"Sit with her a while.","next":"camp"}]}],"the_names_carried":[{"text":"She hands it over with both hands and lets go of it properly, which takes a second longer than it should, and then puts the empty oiled bag in the fire because she says she is not going to keep a bag for a book she has not got. \\"Ask me nothing about it for a month,\\" Ilse says. \\"After that you may ask me anything you like, and I will probably tell you, and I would rather that were a thing I chose in a month than a thing I said tonight.\\"","choices":[{"label":"A month, then.","next":"camp"}]}],"after_the_names_read":[{"text":"\\"Ferrers will hear inside a week and there will be a letter about the stipend that has not been paid in eleven years, and it will be about the stipend and it will not be about the stipend,\\" Ilse says. \\"Reed knew that on the step and took it anyway.\\" She shoulders the bow. \\"I have spent eleven years wanting one honest person to read the thing. I did not think about what it would cost the honest person and that is a failure of exactly the kind I have been accusing that town of.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then stand next to her when the letter comes.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":5}}],"end":true},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]}],"after_the_names_burned":[{"text":"\\"I could,\\" Ilse agrees. \\"Every word, from memory, inside a fortnight, and that is precisely the reason it had to go.\\" She turns a stick in the fire. \\"A book you can rewrite from memory is not a record. It is a thing you have been reciting. I have been reciting for eleven years and I have called it keeping watch.\\"","choices":[{"label":"You were keeping watch as well.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":5}}],"end":true},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]}],"after_the_names_kept":[{"text":"\\"One of them will,\\" Ilse says. \\"Not because he has changed. Because it will one day be cheaper to do the right thing than to argue with you about it, and I have decided that counts, and I have been eleven years deciding it.\\" She sets off up the ridge. \\"Take his out when he does. I want that book to be able to get shorter.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Understood.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":4}}],"end":true}]}],"camp_ilse_corran_stone":[{"expression":4,"text":"\\"There is not.\\" Ilse turns the stick in the fire. \\"Turf by the ford, a thorn that has got away from itself, and eleven years of me walking past it about twice a month.\\"\\n\\nShe is quiet long enough that you take it for the end of the answer, and it is not.\\n\\n\\"I know what I would cut. I have had it settled since the third year. His name, thirty-one years, and the word warden, and nothing else on it, because he would have called anything else an advertisement. The mason at Rivermark wants four gold and a fortnight, and I have had four gold twice.\\" She sets the stick down. \\"I did not go in. I am not going to pretend I know why, and I should be obliged if you did not offer me a reason.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_corran_stone"}],"choices":[{"label":"Then we cut it. I will carry the stone up the hill myself.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":7}}],"next":"camp_ilse_corran_cut"},{"label":"Four gold. Take it to the mason tomorrow.","conditions":[{"gold_at_least":4}],"effects":[{"take_gold":4},{"approval":{"ilse":4}}],"next":"camp_ilse_corran_bought"},{"label":"He would have called it a wasted afternoon.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-2}}],"next":"camp_ilse_corran_excuse"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_corran_cut":[{"expression":2,"text":"\\"It is nine miles and it is uphill for four of them,\\" Ilse says. \\"A stone that size is a hundred and forty pounds and you cannot roll it, because the last two miles are bracken over scree.\\"\\n\\n\\"I know.\\"\\n\\n\\"You do not know. You will.\\" She puts another stick on the fire, squarely. \\"Very well. Two days, a sledge, and one of us at each end of it, and we do the second half after dark, because the flies on that face in the afternoon are not to be borne.\\"\\n\\nA pause.\\n\\n\\"I have had that planned since the third year as well.\\"","choices":[{"label":"This month. Not in the spring.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":3}}],"next":"camp_ilse_corran_dated"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_corran_dated":[{"expression":2,"text":"\\"This month,\\" Ilse agrees. She takes out the small book and writes it down, dated, in the fair hand — the same hand as the counts, on the same ruled line. \\"There. Now it is a thing that is happening, rather than a thing I have settled.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_corran_bought":[{"expression":2,"text":"Ilse looks at the four gold in her palm for some while.\\n\\n\\"This is the easy half,\\" she says. \\"I want it understood that I know that. I have had the four gold twice and the difficulty was never the four gold.\\" She closes her hand on it. \\"It will do. A stone that got there for the wrong reason still has his name on it, and he was a practical man about that sort of thing.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_corran_excuse":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"He would,\\" Ilse says. \\"That is what I have told myself for eleven years. It is a very good line and it has kept a stone off a man for a decade.\\" She turns the stick over. \\"You did not have to hand it back to me.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_believed":[{"expression":3,"text":"\\"Nobody has.\\" She says it exactly as she says the weather. \\"Once, arguably. The captain before Reed sent two men up in the fourth year, and they went as far as the cut and came back and wrote that there was nothing — which there was not, on that day, at that hour, at the cut.\\" She turns a stick in the fire. \\"That is the whole of it. Eleven years of counts, given to eleven people, and the count has never once been the reason for anything.\\"\\n\\nA pause.\\n\\n\\"I stopped expecting it in the fourth year and I have gone on writing them for seven more, and I would rather you did not ask me to account for that, because I cannot.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_believed"}],"choices":[{"label":"Read me the count now. Whatever is in it, we walk on it tomorrow.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":6}}],"next":"camp_ilse_believed_read"},{"label":"Nobody acts on anything the first time.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-3}}],"next":"camp_ilse_believed_shrug"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_believed_read":[{"expression":2,"text":"She reads it out. It takes forty minutes and it is not interesting, and that is rather the point of it: dates, weather, counts, and the word nothing between them wherever nothing was there.\\n\\nAt the end she closes it and says nothing for a while.\\n\\n\\"You will not enjoy tomorrow,\\" she says. \\"It is nine miles for a thing that will almost certainly not be there.\\" And then, before that can be answered: \\"I should like to go anyway.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_believed_shrug":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"The first time,\\" Ilse repeats. \\"Yes. And the fourth. And the ninth.\\" She sets the stick aside, squarely. \\"I am aware people mean that kindly. It is an arithmetic that only works if you are not the one doing the counting.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_alone":[{"expression":5,"text":"Ilse works it out honestly, which takes a moment, because she is not going to hand you a number she has not checked.\\n\\n\\"A winter and about half the spring after it. The fifth year. The roads shut in the first week of the snow and did not open, and the salt stall does not come up the hill.\\" She turns the stick. \\"I had a system. I read the count book aloud in the evenings, the whole of it, from the start, so that the voice went on working. By about the fourth week I had stopped doing it for the voice.\\"\\n\\nShe puts the stick on the fire.\\n\\n\\"That is a fact about a winter. I should be obliged if you did not make it into anything.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_alone"}],"choices":[{"label":"Say nothing, and let her decide whether there is more.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":6}}],"next":"camp_ilse_alone_more"},{"label":"That is a terrible thing to hear.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-2}}],"next":"camp_ilse_alone_pity"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_alone_more":[{"expression":2,"text":"There is more, and it comes about a minute and a half later, in the same level voice.\\n\\n\\"I gave the counts names,\\" Ilse says. \\"The deer. Not all of them — four.\\" She does not look up. \\"I have never told anybody that, and I am aware of precisely how it sounds, and I am telling you because you did not ask a second question. That has not happened to me before.\\"\\n\\nShe puts another stick on.\\n\\n\\"The one with the split ear was called Corran. I am aware of that as well.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_alone_pity":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"It is a fact about weather,\\" Ilse says. \\"Do not make it a terrible thing. Then I have to manage you as well, and I have been managing you for four days already over the business at the ford.\\" There is no edge on it whatever, which is how you know it landed.","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_wrong":[{"expression":5,"text":"\\"The third year. The Ackley boy.\\" She does not have to look it up and does not pretend to. \\"There is a sett on the north face that has been empty since before I had the hill, and I told his father it was empty, because it was, and I had walked it in the March.\\" The stick turns. \\"He went up in the August with a lamp and two dogs and came down with his hand opened to the bone.\\"\\n\\n\\"An empty sett in March is not an empty sett in August. Everyone knows that. I knew it then. I said empty because it was true when I looked, and because I was in a hurry to be believed about the other thing.\\" She looks at the fire. \\"That is the whole of it. I write down what I am wrong about as well. It is the same book.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_wrong"}],"choices":[{"label":"You told me. Nobody makes you tell me these.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":5}}],"next":"camp_ilse_wrong_told"},{"label":"Everybody is wrong sometimes.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-3}}],"next":"camp_ilse_wrong_shrug"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_wrong_told":[{"expression":2,"text":"\\"Nobody does,\\" Ilse agrees. \\"It is in the book, and the book has been under a hearthstone for eleven years, so in practice nobody makes me tell anybody anything.\\" She turns the stick. \\"I told you because a count is worth what the counter is worth, and you are entitled to know what mine is before you walk somewhere on it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_wrong_shrug":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"Everybody is,\\" Ilse says. \\"His hand is not everybody''s hand.\\" She sets the stick down, squarely, and does not take up another. \\"That is the sentence people use to get out of the room. I have used it myself. I am not going to use it about the Ackley boy.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_years":[{"expression":4,"text":"\\"No.\\" Ilse considers leaving it there and decides not to. \\"It is not long for me and it is a great while for them, and that is the whole difficulty, and nobody has ever wanted it put that way round.\\"\\n\\nShe turns the stick.\\n\\n\\"The reeve who voted the stipend away is dead. His son is dead. His grandson keeps the toll-house at the second ford; he has been perfectly civil to me twice, and he does not know there was a stipend, or a warden before me, or a boundary walk that took two days.\\"\\n\\nA pause.\\n\\n\\"I have not been forgotten by people who decided to forget me. I have been outlived by a town, four times over, in a job it forgot it had.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_years"}],"choices":[{"label":"Then the hill is the only thing that remembers it with you.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":5}}],"next":"camp_ilse_years_hill"},{"label":"You will outlast all of it.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-2}}],"next":"camp_ilse_years_outlast"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_years_hill":[{"expression":2,"text":"\\"The hill does not remember anything,\\" Ilse says. \\"It only fails to change quickly.\\"\\n\\nAnd then, a good way further into the evening, without looking up: \\"That is very nearly the same thing, and I have been leaning on it for eleven years, so you may have the point.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_years_outlast":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"I shall,\\" Ilse agrees. \\"That is what everyone says, and they say it as though it were the consolation.\\" She puts a stick on the fire, squarely. \\"Consider what it is you have just told me I have to look forward to.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_teach":[{"expression":3,"text":"\\"The tour is an hour, and it is very good, and everybody enjoys it,\\" Ilse says. \\"The work is a different thing. The work is that you go out before light, at the same hour, on the same line, in whatever the weather is doing, and you write down what is there — and nine days in ten what is there is nothing, so you write nothing, and you go home.\\"\\n\\nShe looks at you properly, which she does not often do.\\n\\n\\"That is the entire discipline. There is no other part of it. People want the part where I tell them brown water means somebody is digging. Brown water only means anything because of eleven years of writing down that the water was clear.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_teach"}],"choices":[{"label":"Before light. Every day. And I carry the book.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":6}}],"next":"camp_ilse_teach_terms"},{"label":"When there is time for it.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":-2}}],"next":"camp_ilse_teach_later"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_teach_terms":[{"expression":2,"text":"\\"You will carry the book,\\" Ilse repeats, and the order of that sentence pleases her a good deal more than she is going to say. \\"Very well. Before light. You will be extremely bad at it for about three weeks and I am not going to make that easier for you, and somewhere around the twenty-second day you will see a thing on the line that I have not seen.\\"\\n\\nShe turns the stick over.\\n\\n\\"I should like to be there when you do.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Wake me an hour early. We start tomorrow.","effects":[{"approval":{"ilse":3}}],"next":"camp_ilse_teach_started"},{"label":"Back to the fire.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_teach_started":[{"expression":2,"text":"She wakes you an hour before light by standing where you are sleeping and saying your name once, which is how she does everything. The line takes two hours. There is nothing on it. She writes nothing, dated, in the fair hand, and hands you the book to carry back.","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"camp_ilse_teach_later":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"There is never time for it,\\" Ilse says. \\"That is not a complaint about you. It is the reason there has been one warden on this hill for forty-two years, and it will be none when I stop.\\" She turns the stick over and does not look up.","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"camp"}]}],"ilse_return_sorry":[{"expression":4,"text":"\\"You should,\\" Ilse agrees, with no heat at all. \\"That is not the difficulty. A great many people have said that to me at the top of this hill, and every one of them meant it, and I could not tell you what a single one of them did afterwards.\\"\\n\\nShe puts the book away.\\n\\n\\"Two things, and then I shall come down or I shall not. The first is a number.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Ask it.","next":"ilse_return_number"},{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]}],"ilse_return_ask":[{"expression":4,"text":"\\"Then you will not mind two questions,\\" Ilse says. She does not sit down and does not invite you to. \\"The first is a number.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Ask it.","next":"ilse_return_number"},{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]}],"ilse_return_number":[{"expression":4,"text":"\\"I told you how many are under that hill,\\" Ilse says. \\"I told you at a fire. I told it at a market cross before that, to a man who is now dead. I have told nine other people in eleven years, and not one of them could give it back to me a week later.\\"\\n\\nShe waits.\\n\\n\\"How many?\\"","choices":[{"label":"Eleven hundred. Four hundred of them cannot fight.","next":"ilse_return_number_right"},{"label":"A great many.","next":"ilse_return_number_wrong"},{"label":"I do not remember.","next":"ilse_return_number_honest"},{"label":"Leave it.","end":true}]}],"ilse_return_number_wrong":[{"expression":7,"text":"\\"A great many,\\" Ilse repeats. \\"Yes. That is what the alderman said. That is what the captain said. That is what everybody who has ever agreed with me has said, and agreement is not the same as having the number, and the number is the only thing I have.\\"\\n\\nShe opens the book again.\\n\\n\\"Come back up when you can say it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Ask me again.","next":"ilse_return_number"},{"label":"Back down the hill.","end":true}]}],"ilse_return_number_honest":[{"expression":5,"text":"\\"No,\\" Ilse says. \\"Nor did the reeve.\\"\\n\\nShe is quiet a moment, and then does the thing it costs her to do, and says it again.\\n\\n\\"Eleven hundred. Four hundred of them cannot fight. They are coming down because the deep is shut.\\" She closes the book. \\"That is the third time I have given you that. Say it back to me.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Eleven hundred. Four hundred of them cannot fight.","next":"ilse_return_number_right"},{"label":"Back down the hill.","end":true}]}],"ilse_return_number_right":[{"expression":2,"text":"Ilse says nothing at all for a moment.\\n\\n\\"Yes,\\" she says. \\"Thank you.\\"\\n\\nAnd then, because she is exact and will not let a kindness past unexamined: \\"That is not proof of anything. A person can learn a number. Which brings me to the second.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Go on.","next":"ilse_return_acted"}]}],"ilse_return_acted":[{"conditions":[{"any":[{"flag":"deep_shaft_fate"},{"flag":"deep_shaft_cleared"},{"flag":"wardens_count_fate"},{"flag":"hills_fate","equals":"escort"},{"flag":"hills_fate","equals":"reroute"}]}],"expression":2,"text":"\\"The second is not a question,\\" Ilse says. \\"It is a thing I have already checked, because I check everything.\\"\\n\\nShe opens the book to a page near the back and turns it so the light is on it, though she does not expect you to read the hand.\\n\\n\\"You went. Whatever else is between us — and there is a good deal — the count was the reason something happened, for the first time in eleven years, and it is written here with the date on it and a line ruled under it, the same as the eleven refusals.\\"\\n\\nShe closes it.\\n\\n\\"That is the entry I have wanted since I was given this hill. You are in it. I am not going to pretend it weighs nothing because I am cross with you.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then come down off the hill.","next":"ilse_return_comes"},{"label":"Stay, if the hill needs you.","end":true}]},{"expression":4,"text":"\\"The second is not a question either,\\" Ilse says. \\"It is a condition, and you will not care for it, and I am not going to soften it because you walked nine miles.\\"\\n\\nShe opens the book to a page near the back. There is nothing on it.\\n\\n\\"Eleven years. Eleven refusals. A line ruled under each. There is no entry anywhere in it that says somebody went. You have the number now, which is more than the reeve ever managed — and a number nobody walks on is a thing I already have a book full of.\\"\\n\\nShe puts it away.\\n\\n\\"Go and act on it. The shaft, the road, the escort; I do not much mind which, and I shall know which. Then come back up, and I shall come down.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Say what would count.","next":"ilse_return_terms"},{"label":"Then I will come back.","end":true}]}],"ilse_return_terms":[{"expression":4,"text":"\\"Anything that costs you the day,\\" Ilse says. \\"Go down the shaft and shut it, or sound it. Take Reed the count and make her sign for having had it. Walk the road with the wagons instead of behind them.\\" She almost shrugs and does not quite manage it. \\"It is not a test. It is the job. I have never once been able to explain the difference to anybody and I have given up trying.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back down the hill.","end":true}]}],"ilse_return_comes":[{"expression":2,"text":"Ilse walks the last quarter mile of the line first, because it is not finished, and writes down what is on it, which is nothing. Then the book goes inside her coat and she picks up the pack that has been standing ready by the shelter door for a good deal longer than she is going to admit to.\\n\\n\\"I am not soft about this,\\" she says, on the way down. \\"You will be told when you are wrong, and it will be in front of the others. That is the arrangement and it is the only one I have.\\"\\n\\nAt the second stile she stops.\\n\\n\\"You gave the number back. Nobody has ever given the number back.\\"","on_enter":[{"recruit":"ilse"},{"approval":{"ilse":15}},{"set_flag":"ilse_returned"}],"choices":[{"label":"Down the hill, then.","end":true}]}],"ilse_close":[{"conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","status":"active"},{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_locked":true}}],"text":"\\"I have been alone on this hill for eleven years and I had decided that was the shape of it,\\" Ilse says, to the fire, not to you. \\"I would like to revise that. I am telling you rather than asking you because I have forgotten how the asking goes.\\"","once":true,"choices":[{"label":"Ask me anyway.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Consider it revised.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Get some sleep.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","status":"active"},{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_locked":true}}],"text":"\\"I walked the boundary this morning out of habit and I was back before you woke,\\" Ilse says, \\"and I want to tell you that the whole of the last mile of it I was working out how to say a thing, and that I have got about four words.\\" She looks at the fire. \\"They are not good words. I have had eleven years of practice at weather.\\"","pool":"close","choices":[{"label":"Say the four words.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Walk it again tomorrow.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","status":"active"},{"companion":"ilse","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"ilse","romance_locked":true}}],"text":"Ilse has come in off the flank and sat down at the fire without being asked, and has plainly decided to do it, and is being extremely matter-of-fact about a thing she has not done in eleven years. \\"Ground and weather are done,\\" she says. \\"I have nothing left in either of my subjects.\\"","pool":"close","choices":[{"label":"Then start a third one.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Ground and weather will do.","end":true}]},{"text":"Ilse considers the fire for a while and then reports, \\"Nothing tonight,\\" in the voice she files weather under.","choices":[{"label":"Tomorrow, then.","end":true}]}],"romance_after":[{"pool":"afterglow","text":"Ilse walks the boundary at dusk the way she always has, but she has started walking it clockwise, which puts the fire — and you — on her right hand the whole way round. A warden keeps her sword hand free. She knows exactly what she has done with it.","choices":[{"label":"Walk it clockwise tomorrow, too.","end":true}],"conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}]},{"pool":"afterglow","text":"\\"Forty feet,\\" Ilse says, out of an hour of nothing. It is the distance she kept off every trail for eleven years. She is sitting close enough that her shoulder moves your sleeve when she breathes. \\"For the record. I have noticed.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Noted in the book.","end":true}],"conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}]},{"pool":"afterglow","text":"She has taken to reporting one thing every night that is neither ground nor weather. Tonight it is that the third subject is going better than the first two ever did. She says it exactly like a weather report, and then she stays where she is.","choices":[{"label":"Stay there.","end":true}],"conditions":[{"companion":"ilse","romance_stage":2}]},{"text":"Ilse says nothing at all, and stays exactly where she is, which is beside you.","choices":[{"label":"Good.","end":true}]}],"camp_ilse_fate":[{"text":"\\"Sealed is sealed,\\" Ilse says. \\"I mixed the mortar myself and I know what I put in it.\\" A pause the length of a log settling. \\"I walk the warren boundary in my head some nights, all the same. That stone is the one piece of ground I ever closed instead of watched. I have not decided which is the worse habit.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_fate_told"}],"choices":[{"label":"Watching suits you better.","end":true}],"conditions":[{"flag":"deep_shaft_fate","equals":"sealed"}]},{"text":"\\"We put a sound into the dark and the dark answered,\\" Ilse says, level as ever, \\"and now the answer is a thing I know, the way I know the fords and the bad ice.\\" She feeds the fire one stick, exactly. \\"A warden''s whole job is knowing what is on her ground. Nobody promised the knowing would be comfortable.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_ilse_fate_told"}],"choices":[{"label":"Better known than not.","end":true}]}]}}',0,0,0,NULL),
('inn_sleeper','Corbin Waite','Bargeman','Face down on the corner table of the Golden Flagon, and has been for two days. Not drunk. Stopped.','assets/images/npcs/farmer.png','corbin_waite',1,'{"start":"greeting","nodes":{"greeting":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"room_fate","equals":"work"}],"once":true,"text":"He is doing kegs, and he does them the way a man does a thing he has done ten thousand times: without looking, and slightly faster than seems safe.\\n\\n\\"Step''s done,\\" says Corbin Waite. \\"Yard gate wanted a shim, so that is done too. She has not asked me for either of them, which I have decided is her way of not saying anything.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Will you go back on the water?","next":"back_on_the_water"},{"label":"Leave him to it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"room_fate","equals":"paid"}],"once":true,"text":"The corner table is empty and wiped down. There is a river man''s knife on the bar — short, thick-backed, worn to nothing at the heel from nineteen years of sharpening — and Mara has not moved it.","choices":[{"label":"Leave it where it is.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"room_fate","equals":"road"}],"once":true,"text":"The corner table is empty. Somebody else has the fire seat within the hour and is welcome to it.","choices":[{"label":"Leave it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"quest":"a_room_for_the_night","stage":"what_he_needs"}],"text":"Corbin Waite has both hands round the bowl and has not started on it yet, which is a thing hungry men do — they wait until they are certain nobody is going to take it away.\\n\\n\\"You will want me to move on,\\" he says. \\"That is all right. I have been working up to it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Eat first. Nobody is moving you.","next":"he_eats"},{"label":"What are you waiting for?","next":"what_he_waits_for"},{"label":"Leave him to it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"quest":"a_room_for_the_night","status":"active"}],"text":"You have to say it twice, and the second time with a hand flat on the table rather than on him, and he comes up off his arms all at once like a man surfacing.\\n\\nHe is about fifty. His hands are ruined in the particular way a pole ruins hands. Four coppers are set out in a neat row on the table in front of him.\\n\\n\\"I have not had anything I did not pay for,\\" he says immediately. \\"I want that said first.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Nobody said you had. What is your name?","next":"his_name"},{"label":"You have been asleep on this table for two days.","next":"two_days"}]},{"text":"He does not stir. There is a small ale in front of him with two thirds of it left, four coppers set out in a neat row beside it, and he is breathing perfectly well.","choices":[{"label":"Leave him be.","end":true}]}],"two_days":[{"text":"\\"Two days,\\" he repeats, and thinks about it, and you can see him genuinely not have known. \\"Right. Well. That is a market week, and that is her fire seat, and I have had a table off her on a market week.\\"\\n\\nHe starts trying to stand and does not entirely manage it on the first go.","choices":[{"label":"Sit down. What is your name?","next":"his_name"}]}],"his_name":[{"text":"\\"Corbin Waite.\\" He says it the way a man gives a name to a clerk. \\"Flat boats out of Greyhythe. Nineteen years.\\"\\n\\nHe looks at the four coppers.\\n\\n\\"Nine days ago,\\" he says, \\"I put the pole down at the Greyhythe landing and did not pick it up again. I have not got a reason for you. I have been asked for one twice by people who were kind about it, and I did not have one either time.\\"\\n\\nMara has appeared at the end of the bar with a bowl of something and is standing there pretending to do accounts.","on_enter":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"a_room_for_the_night","stage":"what_he_needs"}}],"interjections":[{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric sits down across from him without being invited, which is the most tactful thing Aldric does."},{"companion":"kessa","conditions":[{"not":{"companion":"aldric","status":"active"}}],"text":"Kessa pushes the bowl across the table with one finger and goes back to the bar without saying anything."}],"choices":[{"label":"Eat that.","next":"he_eats"},{"label":"Why walk uphill?","next":"uphill"}]}],"he_eats":[{"text":"He eats the way a man eats who has stopped noticing that he has not: fast at first, and then very slowly, and then he puts the spoon down halfway through and sits with his hands round the bowl.\\n\\n\\"I have not eaten since Rivermark,\\" he says, and then hears it. \\"Since before Rivermark. I did not know that until you asked.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Why walk uphill?","next":"uphill"},{"label":"What do you want to happen next?","next":"what_he_wants"}]}],"uphill":[{"text":"Corbin Waite considers it seriously, which is more than most people would.\\n\\n\\"Because the road goes up,\\" he says. \\"That is not clever. I have been on flat water nineteen years and every place I have ever stopped has been level with every other place, and I wanted to be somewhere that was not.\\"\\n\\nHe turns the bowl a little.\\n\\n\\"And there is no water here,\\" he says. \\"There is the river down the stair, and that is a different river up here, and I can sit in this room and not hear it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"What happened on the water?","next":"what_happened"},{"label":"What do you want to happen next?","next":"what_he_wants"}]}],"what_happened":[{"text":"\\"Nothing,\\" says Corbin Waite. \\"That is the honest answer, it is a poor one, and I am sorry for it.\\"\\n\\nHe thinks about it anyway.\\n\\n\\"Nobody drowned. Nobody cheated me. I had a good boat and a good master and thirty-one shillings a month, and on the ninth of the month I made the landing at Greyhythe and put the pole in the rack, and my hands would not go back to it.\\" He looks at his hands as though they belong to somebody he is annoyed with. \\"Nineteen years. And they would not.\\"","choices":[{"label":"That happens to people.","next":"what_he_wants"}]}],"what_he_waits_for":[{"text":"\\"For it to come back,\\" says Corbin. \\"The wanting to. I thought that if I sat still somewhere warm it would come back on its own, the way a cramp goes.\\"\\n\\nHe looks at the door, which is the thing Mara said he does.\\n\\n\\"It has been nine days,\\" he says. \\"I am beginning to think a man has to go and fetch it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Eat first.","next":"he_eats"},{"label":"What do you want to happen next?","next":"what_he_wants"}]}],"what_he_wants":[{"text":"\\"A bed,\\" says Corbin Waite, after a while, \\"which I cannot pay for. Or something to do with my hands, which I would rather, and which I have not asked her for — because a man who asks for work off a table he has been asleep on for two days is asking for charity with extra steps.\\"\\n\\nHe puts the four coppers back in his pocket, having decided something.\\n\\n\\"Or the boat down,\\" he says. \\"There is one Thursday. That is not what I want. That is what I have got.\\"\\n\\nMara is still at the end of the bar, still not doing accounts.","interjections":[{"companion":"ilse","text":"Ilse, quietly, so that only you hear it: \\"He said the one he wants second. People do that.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Go and talk to Mara.","end":true}]}],"back_on_the_water":[{"text":"\\"Spring boats,\\" says Corbin. \\"I have told her twice and she has not written it down anywhere, so we shall see which of us is right.\\"\\n\\nHe sets the keg on its chocks and gets the angle right first time.\\n\\n\\"It came back,\\" he says, not looking up. \\"About the fourth day. I was carrying a crate up the area steps and I caught myself walking the load the way you walk one on a deck, and I stood there like a fool.\\" He straightens. \\"I would not have got that on a boat going down. You do not find a thing by going back to where you lost it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Leave him to it.","end":true}]}]}}',0,0,0,'sleeping'),
('ione_brack','Chart-Master Ione Brack','Chart-Master of Waerhaven','Licenses every pilot on this shore and holds every sounding of the Ythan Mere in her presses, and has not reported a theft from those presses because the theft would have to be described, and describing it would mean saying out loud which drawer it came from.','assets/images/npcs/sorcerer.png','sorcerer',1,'{"start":"greeting","nodes":{"greeting":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"charts_gone"},{"flag":"doren_fate","equals":"owned"}],"text":"Chart-Master Brack has the north wall''s presses open, all of them, and a young shipwright at the table with three drawers'' worth of the northern shore spread in front of him and a lamp of his own.\\n\\n\\"He asked,\\" she says, before you can. \\"That is all it ever wanted. Somebody to come to the front counter and ask, and be told no, and ask again in writing so that the no had to be signed.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Leave them to it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"doren_took_charts"}],"text":"Ione Brack has the north wall''s presses open — three of them, the three — and is going through them drawer by drawer with her rule and a lamp.\\n\\n\\"They are all here,\\" she says. \\"All three. Back in the right drawers in the right order, and I have checked every sheet against the index, and there is not a page missing.\\"\\n\\nShe closes one.\\n\\n\\"He put them back. Whoever it was put them back, which means he did not want the charts. He wanted what was on them, and he learnt it, and he gave me back the objects.\\"\\n\\nShe looks at you.\\n\\n\\"That is a very great deal more frightening than a theft, and I would rather you did not tell me his name.\\"","choices":[{"label":"\\"Then I will not.\\"","next":"she_does_not_want_it"},{"label":"\\"You should ask him yourself.\\"","next":"she_does_not_want_it"},{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"charts_gone"}],"text":"\\"You know,\\" says Ione Brack, and does not stop ruling the line she is ruling. \\"I have not reported it and I am not going to, and I would like to tell you it is because I am protecting somebody.\\"","choices":[{"label":"\\"Then why?\\"","next":"why_not_reported"},{"label":"\\"What was on them?\\"","next":"the_northern_shore"},{"label":"Another time.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"met_brack"}],"text":"\\"Back,\\" says the Chart-Master, without looking up. \\"The presses are shut and the pilots'' book is at the counter and the answer to whichever of those you were going to ask about is no.\\"","choices":[{"label":"\\"The north wall.\\"","next":"the_north_wall"},{"label":"Another time.","end":true}]},{"text":"The room is warm, which no other room in Waerhaven is, because the stove that keeps the vellum dry is fed before anybody in the building is. A tall woman is ruling a sounding line by lamp with a rule that has been in somebody''s hand for forty years.\\n\\n\\"Ione Brack, Chart-Master,\\" she says. \\"Every sounding of the Ythan Mere is in this room and none of it is for sale. If you want a pilot, the book is at the counter and the fee is fixed. If you want a chart, you want a pilot.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"met_brack"}],"choices":[{"label":"\\"What is on the north wall?\\"","next":"the_north_wall"},{"label":"\\"Who has asked you for the northern shore lately?\\"","next":"who_asked"},{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]}],"the_north_wall":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"charts_gone"}],"text":"\\"Three drawers,\\" Brack says. \\"You have had that.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"The northern shore,\\" says Brack, and her rule keeps moving, and her voice does not change at all, which is the tell. \\"Soundings from the Horn round to the Drennmark coast. Very old work, mostly. Nobody has run that shore in commerce since the Wyrdpines went bad.\\"\\n\\n\\"Which is why nobody asks for it. Which is why it is on the north wall, where the stove does not reach, which is a thing I have complained about in writing four times.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Look at the drawers, not at her.","check":{"skill":"investigation","dc":13,"on_success":"the_three_drawers","on_failure":"she_closes_it"}},{"label":"\\"Three of them shut a little too easily.\\"","tag":"SCRIBE","conditions":[{"origin":"scribe"}],"check":{"skill":"investigation","dc":10,"on_success":"the_three_drawers","on_failure":"she_closes_it"}},{"label":"Back.","next":"greeting"}]}],"the_three_drawers":[{"text":"Fourteen presses on the north wall, all of them stiff with damp and cold and forty years of not being opened. Eleven of them fight the hand.\\n\\nThree do not. Three run out sweet and shut sweet, because they have been opened and shut recently and often enough to wear the runners clean.\\n\\nBrack has stopped ruling.\\n\\n\\"Yes,\\" she says, to the wall rather than to you. \\"In the spring. Three. And I have not reported it.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"charts_gone"},{"xp":100}],"choices":[{"label":"\\"Why not?\\"","next":"why_not_reported"},{"label":"\\"What was on them?\\"","next":"the_northern_shore"}]}],"she_closes_it":[{"text":"Brack puts the rule down, walks the length of the north wall, and leans on it with her arms folded — in front of the presses, deliberately, the way you stand in a doorway.\\n\\n\\"It is cold on this side of the room,\\" she says pleasantly. \\"You will want the stove. Pilots'' book is at the counter.\\"\\n\\nShe stays there until you leave.","choices":[{"label":"Go.","end":true}]}],"why_not_reported":[{"text":"\\"Because a theft has to be described,\\" Brack says. \\"That is what a report is. It is a description.\\"\\n\\nShe comes back to the table and sits down, which she has not done since you came in.\\n\\n\\"To report it I write down which drawer, and which drawer says which shore, and the moment I write which shore, Lathmere has been told in a signed document that somebody in Waerhaven wants the northern soundings. And Lathmere has spent six years arranging not to be told anything about the north.\\"\\n\\n\\"So I would be reporting a theft of three charts and confessing a great deal more than that, on the League''s own paper, in my own hand.\\"","choices":[{"label":"\\"Who took them?\\"","next":"who_asked"},{"label":"\\"What was on them?\\"","next":"the_northern_shore"},{"label":"Back.","next":"greeting"}]}],"the_northern_shore":[{"text":"\\"Anchorages,\\" says Brack. \\"That is the honest answer and it is not the one you want, so here is the rest of it.\\"\\n\\n\\"Four inlets on the Drennmark coast that a deep hull can lie in. The ice line as it stood forty years ago. Two runs of soundings taken by a pilot named Orrow who went up there three times and came back twice.\\"\\n\\nShe folds her hands.\\n\\n\\"Nobody steals that to smuggle with. There is nothing up there to smuggle. You steal that if you intend to go, and to come back, and to be able to tell somebody else how.\\"","choices":[{"label":"\\"Who has been asking?\\"","next":"who_asked"},{"label":"Back.","next":"greeting"}]}],"who_asked":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"charts_gone"}],"text":"\\"Formally? Warden Vorn. Twice, in writing, and I refused her twice in writing, and the second refusal is the one I am least proud of.\\"\\n\\nBrack looks at the north wall.\\n\\n\\"Informally, this city has a great many people in it who can read a chart, and about nine of them work in a building where they would not have to explain themselves for being in a room with one.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back.","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"For the northern shore? Nobody, in nine years.\\"\\n\\nBrack rules another line.\\n\\n\\"And then twice, in one spring, in writing, by a Grey Warden of Drennmark who wanted to know whether her own coast is still where she left it. I refused her. It is not in my gift and she knew it was not, and she asked twice anyway, which is either stupidity or a woman making a record of having asked.\\"\\n\\n\\"It was the second one. She is not stupid.\\"","choices":[{"label":"\\"What is on the north wall?\\"","next":"the_north_wall"},{"label":"Back.","next":"greeting"}]}],"she_does_not_want_it":[{"text":"\\"I have refused that shore in writing twice this year,\\" says Ione Brack. \\"Both refusals are signed and both are in the book and both of them are correct.\\"\\n\\nShe shuts the last drawer.\\n\\n\\"And somebody read it anyway, and put it back, and now the fact that a person in Waerhaven knows the four inlets on the Drennmark coast exists in the world whether I have written it down or not.\\"\\n\\nShe puts the lamp out.\\n\\n\\"That is the whole of what a Charthouse is, you know. Not a room with vellum in it. A decision about which shores this city is able to reach. I have been making that decision for eleven years by not reaching for a drawer, and I have never once had to say it out loud, and I have just said it out loud.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]}]}}',0,1,0,NULL),
('jimmy_able','Jimmy Able','Thief','A good coat, a better knife, and the easy manner of a man who has never once been the one holding the bag when it was opened.','assets/images/npcs/jimmy_able.png','jimmy_able',1,'{"start":"hail","nodes":{"hail":[{"once":true,"text":"The block has one way in and a man sitting comfortably in it, which is not an accident. He has a good coat, a better knife laid across his knee where you can see it, and he stands up as if you were expected.\\n\\n\\"Jimmy Able,\\" he says, and does not offer a hand. \\"You''ll be the ones the Watch let through the door. That''s fine. We''re all down here for the same three reasons and none of them is each other.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Sit down a while.","conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"active"}],"next":"camp"},{"label":"What three reasons?","next":"three_reasons"},{"label":"We''re looking for children.","next":"children"},{"label":"Nothing from you.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"oldcity_broodmother_down"},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"active"}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"camp"}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"left"}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"hostile"}}],"once":true,"text":"He is on his feet and out of the chair before you are through the wall, and this time he does not sit back down.\\n\\n\\"Two years,\\" Jimmy says. \\"Two years I have been telling people about that shop and not one of them went, and I include myself in that, and I have thought about it every single week.\\"\\n\\nHe looks at the gap in the wall, and at the eight people behind him who are all pretending not to listen.\\n\\n\\"I would like to come with you. I want to say that badly, so that neither of us has to pretend I am doing you a favour.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Why?","next":"why_come"},{"label":"Then come.","effects":[{"recruit":"jimmy_able"}],"next":"he_comes"},{"label":"You have a block and eight people in it.","next":"you_have_a_block"}]},{"conditions":[{"quest":"oldcity_the_cutters_trove","stage":"opened_the_workshop"}],"once":true,"text":"Jimmy is on his feet before you are through the gap in the wall, and for once the easy manner is not quite fastened on.\\n\\n\\"You got in,\\" he says. \\"You actually got in.\\"\\n\\nHe looks at what you are carrying, and at the weight of it, and does the arithmetic he has been doing in his head for two years without ever once being willing to walk down there and do it properly.","choices":[{"label":"We got in. We''re keeping it.","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"oldcity_the_cutters_trove","stage":"took_the_trove"}}],"next":"keeping_it"},{"label":"We shut it again and left it.","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"oldcity_the_cutters_trove","stage":"left_it_sealed"}}],"next":"left_it"}]},{"conditions":[{"quest":"oldcity_the_short_tally","status":"active"},{"quest":"oldcity_the_short_tally","stage":"follow_the_stone"}],"once":true,"text":"He has followed your eye to the wall, and to the two courses of new dressed stone in it that are paler than everything around them and cut square where nothing else down here is.\\n\\n\\"Ah,\\" says Jimmy Able. \\"Yes.\\"\\n\\nHe does not bother denying it, which is either honesty or the most efficient available lie.\\n\\n\\"It''s lying in a heap thirty feet from here and the Works have more of it than they''ve hands to lay it. And we needed a wall, on account of the goblins. You''ll notice the goblins haven''t got in.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Dessel has been writing letters about it for eleven weeks.","next":"eleven_weeks"},{"label":"What''s it worth to you if I forget?","next":"worth_to_you"}],"on_enter":[{"set_flag":"oldcity_stone_traced"}]},{"text":"Jimmy is where he was, in the one chair, in the one doorway.\\n\\n\\"Still breathing,\\" he observes. \\"That''s better than most weeks.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Sit down a while.","conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"active"}],"next":"camp"},{"label":"Tell me about the cutter''s shop.","conditions":[{"not":{"quest":"oldcity_the_cutters_trove","status":"active"}}],"next":"the_cutters_shop","reoffer":true},{"label":"Goodbye.","end":true}]}],"three_reasons":[{"text":"\\"Old coin, old stones, and getting away from somebody.\\" He counts them off. \\"Everyone down here is one of those. The Works are the exception and I''ve never trusted them for it.\\"\\n\\n\\"You''re not running from anyone — you came in the front. So it''s coin or stones. And if it''s stones, I know where a great many of them are, and I''ll tell you for nothing, because I have wanted somebody else to go and get them for about two years.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the stones.","next":"the_cutters_shop"},{"label":"We''re looking for children.","next":"children"}]}],"children":[{"text":"The easy manner goes off him like a coat.\\n\\n\\"Not us,\\" he says. \\"I want that said first and I want it said flat. Not us, not ever, and if it were one of mine he''d go in the channel the same hour.\\"\\n\\nHe sits back down.\\n\\n\\"There''s a thing on the far ledge past the drop hole. We don''t go east of the hole. It came about a year back and the noise off that ledge changed and we stopped going, and I''d sooner you didn''t tell me what''s on the end of it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the stones.","next":"the_cutters_shop"},{"label":"Goodbye.","end":true}]}],"the_cutters_shop":[{"text":"\\"South of the low channel there''s a cutter''s shop. Sealed the night the City came down on it — not looted, not opened, sealed. Wheels still on the bench. Everything a man like that would have had in the wall on the night he stopped going home.\\"\\n\\nHe lets that sit.\\n\\n\\"And between it and the channel there are two caves of web, and in the second one there is something that took Corran Fitch off his feet and up into the roof in front of four of us, and none of the four of us saw it arrive. So. It''s yours, with my blessing, and I''ll not take a share.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Generous.","next":"generous"},{"label":"We''ll look at it.","end":true}],"on_enter":[{"start_quest":"oldcity_the_cutters_trove"},{"quest_stage":{"quest":"oldcity_the_cutters_trove","stage":"past_the_webs"}}]}],"generous":[{"text":"\\"It isn''t,\\" Jimmy says, cheerfully. \\"It costs me nothing and I have already decided I''m never going down there. If you come back up with it I''ll buy you a drink at the top of the stair and be genuinely pleased. If you don''t, I''ll have lost nothing but a rumour.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Understood.","end":true}]}],"eleven_weeks":[{"text":"\\"Eleven weeks,\\" Jimmy agrees. \\"That''s about right. He''s a careful man, Dessel. Rules his lines.\\"\\n\\nHe is watching your face rather than your hands, which is the tell that he has already decided how this goes.\\n\\n\\"Say it to him if you like. I''d not hold it against you. He''ll write it in a column and the Works will send a letter and by the time anybody comes down that stair with enough men, we''ll be in a different block with the same stone in the wall.\\"","choices":[{"label":"What''s it worth to you if I forget?","next":"worth_to_you"},{"label":"I''ll say it to him.","end":true}]}],"worth_to_you":[{"text":"He is delighted, and does not trouble to hide it.\\n\\n\\"Now that''s a conversation.\\"\\n\\nThe floorboards by the wall lift together, which means they have been cut to. What comes up is a chest with a good lock and a bad hinge, and what comes out of the chest is counted into your hand one coin at a time, so that you have to watch him do it.","choices":[{"label":"Take it.","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"oldcity_the_short_tally","stage":"took_their_price"}},{"approval":{"jimmy_able":6}}],"next":"took_it"},{"label":"Put it back.","next":"put_it_back","effects":[{"approval":{"jimmy_able":-4}}]}]}],"took_it":[{"text":"\\"Pleasure,\\" says Jimmy Able, and means it, and shuts the floor.","choices":[{"label":"Goodbye.","end":true}]}],"put_it_back":[{"text":"The coins go back one at a time, at the same speed, and he watches you the whole way.\\n\\n\\"Right,\\" he says. \\"Well. You''ll do what you''ll do.\\"\\n\\nThe knife has not moved off his knee the entire conversation.","choices":[{"label":"Goodbye.","end":true}]}],"keeping_it":[{"text":"\\"''Course you are.\\" He laughs, genuinely, and there is a beat afterwards where nine other people in this block do not laugh and are all watching from the windows.\\n\\nThen he sits back down and the beat passes.\\n\\n\\"Buy me that drink at the top of the stair,\\" he says. \\"I''ve earned the rumour.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Goodbye.","end":true,"effects":[{"approval":{"jimmy_able":5}}]}]}],"left_it":[{"text":"Jimmy stares at you for a long moment.\\n\\n\\"You got past the web,\\" he says slowly, \\"and through the door, and you put the door back.\\"\\n\\nHe shakes his head, and something in him settles that you cannot read.\\n\\n\\"There''s not one man in this block would have done that. Including me. Especially me.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Goodbye.","end":true,"effects":[{"approval":{"jimmy_able":10}}]}]}],"why_come":[{"text":"\\"Because I am forty-one and I run nine men in a sewer.\\" He says it lightly, which is how he says everything, and it does not quite come off. \\"That was a young man''s plan and I made it eleven years ago and I have not had a new one since.\\"\\n\\n\\"And because you went down there. I want to be near the next thing somebody does that I would not.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then come.","effects":[{"recruit":"jimmy_able"}],"next":"he_comes"},{"label":"Not yet.","end":true}]}],"you_have_a_block":[{"text":"\\"I have a block and eight people in it and every one of them would have it off me by Tuesday if they thought of it first.\\" Still light. Still not quite coming off. \\"That is not bitterness, it is the arrangement. I built it. It works.\\"\\n\\n\\"I would just rather be somewhere else while it does.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then come.","effects":[{"recruit":"jimmy_able"}],"next":"he_comes"},{"label":"Stay and hold it.","end":true}]}],"he_comes":[{"text":"He does not pack. He picks up the knife off the chair, puts it somewhere you do not see, and takes the coat off the nail, and that is the whole of it — a man who has been ready to leave for eleven years and has never once said so.\\n\\nAt the gap in the wall he stops and says something to the nearest of them, too quiet to hear. Whatever it is, the man laughs.\\n\\nNobody comes to the wall to watch him go.","choices":[{"label":"Come on.","end":true}]}],"camp":[{"text":"Jimmy has the fire side nobody wanted, same as ever, but he sits it differently since the business with the ninth man was settled — less like a man minding the door, more like a man who has finally worked out he is allowed to be in the room.","choices":[{"label":"There was a body in a side-way off Copper Wire Lane.","conditions":[{"not":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man"}}],"effects":[{"start_quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man"}],"next":"ninth_the_body"},{"label":"Nine men. Four years.","conditions":[{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"who_told_them"}],"next":"ninth_the_count"},{"label":"How did you come to run a gang?","next":"camp_how","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_how"}}]},{"label":"What do you make of the rest of us?","next":"camp_us","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_us"}}]},{"label":"I''ll take the door side tonight. You sleep.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_watch"}}],"next":"camp_jimmy_watch"},{"label":"The block. Now that it''s said.","conditions":[{"flag":"jimmy_fate"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_after_told"}}],"next":"camp_jimmy_after"},{"label":"Something has been sitting on you for days.","conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_locked":true}}],"next":"jimmy_close"},{"label":"Still counting?","conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}],"next":"romance_after"},{"label":"Nothing. Sleep.","end":true}],"conditions":[{"flag":"jimmy_fate"}]},{"text":"Jimmy has the fire side nobody wanted and is perfectly comfortable on it, which is a trick he has never explained.","choices":[{"label":"There was a body in a side-way off Copper Wire Lane.","conditions":[{"not":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man"}}],"effects":[{"start_quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man"}],"next":"ninth_the_body"},{"label":"Nine men. Four years.","conditions":[{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"who_told_them"}],"next":"ninth_the_count"},{"label":"How did you come to run a gang?","next":"camp_how","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_how"}}]},{"label":"What do you make of the rest of us?","next":"camp_us","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_us"}}]},{"label":"I''ll take the door side tonight. You sleep.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_watch"}}],"next":"camp_jimmy_watch"},{"label":"The block. Now that it''s said.","conditions":[{"flag":"jimmy_fate"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_jimmy_after_told"}}],"next":"camp_jimmy_after"},{"label":"Something has been sitting on you for days.","conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_locked":true}}],"next":"jimmy_close"},{"label":"Still counting?","conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}],"next":"romance_after"},{"label":"Nothing. Sleep.","end":true}]}],"camp_how":[{"text":"\\"Badly, and by accident, and eleven years ago.\\" He turns his hand over, looking for something on it that is not there. \\"There were four of us and a man called Corse who was in charge, and Corse was taken on the quay in front of all four of us, and afterwards the other three looked at me.\\"\\n\\n\\"I have never worked out why they looked at me. I have thought about it more than is healthy.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Because you were still standing there.","next":"camp_still_standing"},{"label":"Somebody has to be looked at.","end":true}],"on_enter":[{"approval":{"jimmy_able":2}},{"set_flag":"camp_jimmy_how"}]}],"camp_still_standing":[{"text":"That lands somewhere. He does not do anything with his face, but he stops looking at his hand.\\n\\n\\"Yes,\\" he says, after a while. \\"That is about the size of it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Goodnight, Jimmy.","end":true}],"on_enter":[{"approval":{"jimmy_able":6}}]}],"camp_us":[{"text":"\\"You are all extremely bad at this and it is restful.\\" He is delighted with the observation. \\"Nobody has priced me once. Nobody has worked out where I sleep relative to the way out. You have all simply decided I am here.\\"\\n\\nA beat.\\n\\n\\"It is going to take me a while to stop finding that suspicious.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Take your time.","end":true}],"on_enter":[{"approval":{"jimmy_able":4}},{"set_flag":"camp_jimmy_us"}]}],"ninth_the_body":[{"on_enter":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"the_body"}}],"text":"\\"Fitch,\\" Jimmy says immediately. \\"Corran Fitch. He went off with the box in the spring and the centipedes had him before we did, which I call a result for everybody.\\"\\n\\nIt comes out clean and complete and slightly too fast, the way a thing does when it has been said several times before to several different people.","choices":[{"label":"Who worked out he was skimming?","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"who_told_them"}}],"next":"ninth_who_told"},{"label":"Leave it.","end":true}]}],"ninth_who_told":[{"text":"\\"Everybody. It was obvious.\\" A shrug, easy as anything. \\"He was buying. You do not buy on our money without the rest of us noticing.\\"\\n\\n\\"Ask the block, if you like. They will all tell you the same.\\"","choices":[{"label":"I did ask the block.","next":"ninth_i_asked"},{"label":"All right.","end":true}]}],"ninth_i_asked":[{"text":"The easy manner does not go anywhere. It simply stops being aimed at you and starts being aimed at the fire.\\n\\n\\"And?\\"","choices":[{"label":"Every one of them heard it. None of them said it.","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"the_count"}}],"next":"ninth_the_count"},{"label":"Nothing worth repeating.","end":true}]}],"ninth_the_count":[{"text":"\\"Nine,\\" Jimmy agrees. \\"Four years. Eleven names.\\"\\n\\nHe does not pretend not to follow. That is the thing about him you keep underestimating: he is not slow, he is simply never the one who says it first.\\n\\n\\"You want to know whether I arrange it. Whether there is always one of them who is going to be the one, and whether I know which, and whether I know it early.\\"\\n\\nThe fire does something. Nobody moves.\\n\\n\\"Yes,\\" he says.","choices":[{"label":"Then say it to them. Not to me.","next":"ninth_say_it_to_them"},{"label":"I''m not going to repeat it.","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"kept_it_quiet"}}],"next":"ninth_kept_quiet"},{"label":"They should hear it from me, then.","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"told_them_myself"}}],"next":"ninth_told_them"}]}],"ninth_say_it_to_them":[{"text":"\\"To the eight of them.\\" He says it as if testing whether the words will hold weight. \\"In the room. Standing up.\\"\\n\\n\\"They will not kill me. I want to be clear that I have already done that arithmetic, because that is the whole of my problem and I am doing it right now in front of you.\\"\\n\\nHe puts his hands on his knees.\\n\\n\\"All right.\\"","choices":[{"label":"I''ll come with you.","effects":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"jimmy_the_ninth_man","stage":"made_him_say_it"}}],"next":"ninth_confessed"}]}],"ninth_confessed":[{"text":"He does it exactly as described: the room they sleep in, standing up, no coat. It takes him four minutes and he does not once make it charming, which is the most difficult thing you have ever watched anybody do.\\n\\nTwo of them leave that night.\\n\\nAfterwards, on the channel, he says: \\"That is going to get me caught inside a year.\\" And then, further along, and not to you: \\"Worth it, probably.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Probably.","end":true}]}],"ninth_kept_quiet":[{"text":"\\"Thank you,\\" Jimmy says, in the easy way he thanks everybody, and that is the last thing he says for a long time.\\n\\nThe block stays nine. It will not be the same nine in a year, and both of you now know that, and only one of you is going to do anything about it, and it is not going to be him.","choices":[{"label":"Goodnight.","end":true}]}],"ninth_told_them":[{"text":"You say it to the eight of them with him standing in the room, which is the only honest way to do it and is not a kind one.\\n\\nHe does not deny it. He does not say anything at all. He looks at the eight of them for a while, working out what they will do, because that is the only thing he has ever known how to do — and then he goes out through the gap in the wall, and the block is his, and he is not in it.","choices":[{"label":"Let him go.","end":true}]}],"romance_one":[{"on_enter":[{"romance":{"companion":"jimmy_able","stage":1}}],"text":"\\"Right,\\" says Jimmy. \\"Yes. I am going to do this badly and I would like that on the record in advance, because doing things badly is not something I have any practice at and I would hate for you to think it came naturally.\\"\\n\\nHe stops. Starts again, and this time without the manner on it, which is a different voice entirely and one you have not heard.\\n\\n\\"I would like to stay. That is the whole of it. I have never wanted to stay anywhere and I have been extremely comfortable about that for eleven years.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then stay.","next":"romance_two"},{"label":"Say it again when you''ve slept on it.","end":true}]}],"romance_two":[{"on_enter":[{"romance":{"companion":"jimmy_able","stage":2}}],"text":"\\"Then here is the part I am actually frightened of,\\" he says, cheerfully, and it is not a lie and it is not quite a joke either.\\n\\n\\"There will come a night where the sensible thing is to be somewhere else. It will be obvious. I will see it about an hour before anybody else does — that is the one thing I am genuinely good at — and I will have to decide, in that hour, on my own, with nobody watching.\\"\\n\\nHe turns his hand over, looking for the thing that is not on it.\\n\\n\\"I do not know what I will do. I want you to know that I do not know, because everybody who has ever been in a room with me has been told I did know, and that has always been the lie.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then I''ll be watching.","end":true},{"label":"Decide it now, and hold to it.","end":true}]}],"romance_after":[{"text":"\\"Still here,\\" Jimmy agrees. \\"Eleven weeks. I have counted, which I am aware is not the behaviour of a relaxed man.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Count on.","end":true}],"pool":"afterglow","conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}]},{"pool":"afterglow","text":"He has the fire side nobody wanted, and has moved along it until the gap between you is not a gap by anyone''s measure, and has said nothing about having moved. For a man who narrates everything he does, the silence is the announcement.","choices":[{"label":"Budge up, then.","end":true}],"conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}]},{"pool":"afterglow","text":"He is asleep on the wrong side of the fire — the side with the dark behind it — and has been for hours. Eleven years of arranging never to have his back to anything, and he has handed the watching of it to you without a word being said.","choices":[{"label":"Take the watch.","end":true}],"conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}]},{"text":"Jimmy pats the ground beside him as if he had been saving it, which — eleven weeks of sitting in exactly the same spot — he has.","choices":[{"label":"Budge up.","end":true}]}],"jimmy_close":[{"conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"active"},{"companion":"jimmy_able","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_locked":true}}],"once":true,"text":"\\"I have worked out what is wrong with me,\\" Jimmy announces, to the fire.\\n\\n\\"I have spent eleven years making sure I am never the one who is left holding anything. And it turns out that if you do that for long enough you end up not holding anything.\\"\\n\\nHe is not looking at you, which from him is enormous.","choices":[{"label":"Hold something, then.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"That''s a young man''s problem.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Get some sleep, Jimmy.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"active"},{"companion":"jimmy_able","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_locked":true}}],"pool":"close","text":"He has taken the side of the fire between you and the dark again. He has done it four nights running and he has an explanation ready for it, and nobody has asked.","choices":[{"label":"Nobody asked you to do that.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Let him have it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"jimmy_able","status":"active"},{"companion":"jimmy_able","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"jimmy_able","romance_locked":true}}],"pool":"close","text":"\\"I have been trying to work out what I would take,\\" Jimmy says, out of nothing. \\"If I went. Tonight. What I would actually pick up on the way past.\\"\\n\\nHe seems genuinely puzzled by the answer.\\n\\n\\"The coat. That is the entire list. Eleven years.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Make a longer list.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"It''s a good coat.","end":true}]},{"text":"Jimmy looks at you, and looks at the fire, and produces his most charming shrug, which is the one he uses when charm is the wrong tool and he knows it.","choices":[{"label":"Goodnight, Jimmy.","end":true}]}],"camp_jimmy_watch":[{"text":"Jimmy opens his mouth to make it a joke, and does not find one, which you would have said was not possible.\\n\\n\\"Eleven years,\\" he says instead, \\"and the number of people who have offered me that is now one.\\" He moves to the warm side like a man expecting the floor to object, and is asleep in four minutes flat.","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_jimmy_watch"},{"approval":{"jimmy_able":4}}],"choices":[{"label":"Goodnight, Jimmy.","end":true}]}],"camp_jimmy_after":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"jimmy_fate","equals":"confessed"}],"text":"\\"Four minutes,\\" Jimmy says. \\"Eleven years of being charming about it, and the truth took four minutes and cost me two men.\\" He turns his hand over, looking at the same nothing as ever. \\"Cheap,\\" he decides, and for once the lightness holds all the way to the end of the word.","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_jimmy_after_told"}],"choices":[{"label":"Cheap at twice the price.","end":true}]},{"text":"\\"Nine men,\\" Jimmy says, apropos of the fire. \\"Same nine, for now. You kept it and I watched you keep it, and I want you to know that watching a person hold a thing shut on your behalf is a new experience for me, and I am handling it extremely well.\\" He is not, quite. It is closer than he has ever come.","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"camp_jimmy_after_told"}],"choices":[{"label":"It stays kept.","end":true}]}]}}',0,1,0,NULL),
('joss_frayle','Joss Frayle','Carter','He hauls stone on the west road eleven months of the year and stops at the ford twice, in the same two weeks, and puts a river-stone against the standing stone, and goes on.','assets/images/npcs/fighter.png','joss_frayle',3,'{"start":"hail","nodes":{"hail":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"ford_dead_named"}],"text":"He is at the stone with his hand flat on the new cutting, going down the list with one finger, and he has been doing that for a while before you got here.\\n\\n\\"Nineteen,\\" Joss Frayle says. \\"I knew there were nineteen. I''ve known there were nineteen for four years.\\" He does not take his hand off. \\"I didn''t know the other eighteen were called anything.\\"","expression":3,"choices":[{"label":"They were.","next":"they_were"},{"label":"Leave him to it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"ford_fate","equals":"cleared"}],"once":true,"text":"\\"It runs clean,\\" Joss says. He is standing in the shallows in his boots watching the water go over laid stone the way it was built to. \\"Four years of everybody going round the fouled part and calling that the crossing.\\"\\n\\nHe looks at the west bank for a moment and then does not.","choices":[{"label":"It''s a road again.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"quest":"the_ford_itself","stage":"the_standing_stone"}],"text":"He has a river-stone in his hand and he is not putting it down.\\n\\n\\"You''ve worked out it isn''t a milestone,\\" he says. \\"Right. Sit down on the block, then, because I''m not doing this standing up and I''m not doing it twice.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Sit down.","next":"the_account"}]},{"conditions":[{"quest":"the_ford_itself","stage":"the_four_rectangles"}],"text":"A big man in carter''s leathers has stopped his cart on the near bank, which nobody does, and walked down to the standing stone with a river-stone in his hand.\\n\\nHe puts it against the foot of the stone with the others. There are hundreds of them.\\n\\n\\"Don''t mind me,\\" he says. \\"I''ll be four minutes and then I''ll be gone eleven months.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"met_frayle"}],"choices":[{"label":"What are the four bare patches on the far bank?","next":"the_four"},{"label":"What''s the stone for?","next":"the_four"},{"label":"Take your four minutes.","end":true}]},{"text":"A carter has stopped on the near bank, which nobody using this crossing does, and gone down to the flat grey stone at the water''s edge with a river-stone in his fist.\\n\\nHe sets it against the foot with the others. There are a great many others.","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"met_frayle"},{"start_quest":"the_ford_itself"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric has stopped walking. He does not say anything and he does not come any closer to the water."},{"companion":"ilse","text":"Ilse: \\"Four rectangles on the far bank. Grass to the edges and then nothing. That is burnt ground and it is four years old.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"What''s the stone for?","next":"the_four"},{"label":"Leave him to it.","end":true}]}],"they_were":[{"text":"\\"Aye,\\" he says. \\"Well.\\" He takes his hand off the stone and looks at it. \\"I put one of these here twice a year for four years and I never once thought about the other eighteen as people with names. That''s mine to carry and I''ll carry it.\\"\\n\\nHe picks up the next river-stone.","choices":[{"label":"Safe road, Frayle.","end":true}]}],"the_four":[{"text":"Joss Frayle straightens up and looks across at the west bank for a long moment.\\n\\n\\"Fever-huts,\\" he says. \\"Four of them. Fourth winter back. Travellers stopping at the crossing, and it went through them, and then it started going through the carters, so they put the sick on the west bank in huts because a river is a thing a fever won''t cross.\\"\\n\\nHe wipes his hands on his leathers.\\n\\n\\"That''s what everybody who uses this road knows. Every one of them. And every one of them waters upstream of it and not one of them will say the word out loud, and I''ve been trying to work out for four years whether that''s shame or just how people are.\\"","on_enter":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"the_ford_itself","stage":"the_standing_stone"}},{"set_flag":"ford_huts_known"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric has not moved and does not speak."},{"companion":"kessa","text":"Kessa: \\"A river''s not a thing a fever won''t cross.\\" Frayle: \\"No. It isn''t. They knew that too.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Who''s the stone for?","next":"the_account"},{"label":"Not today.","end":true}]}],"the_account":[{"text":"\\"My sister,\\" Joss says. \\"Bettony. She was in the third hut, and she was one of the ones that wasn''t dying — she had the wasting kind, the slow one, and the slow one takes about a fortnight and you can come out the other side of it if somebody sits with you.\\"\\n\\nHe puts his hand flat on the stone.\\n\\n\\"Somebody sat with her. I know that much and I''ve never known who. And then the huts went up, all four, on the same night, and after that I stopped being able to find anybody who''d talk about the second week at all.\\"\\n\\nA long pause. The river works at the laid stones.\\n\\n\\"There''s no cutting on this stone because nobody could agree what to put on it. So I bring one of these twice a year. It''s not much of a system.\\"","interjections":[{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric turns and walks up the bank to the horses and stands with them. He does not come back down until this is over."},{"companion":"ilse","text":"Ilse: \\"Nineteen?\\" Frayle: \\"Nineteen. Eleven that were going and eight that weren''t. I''ve had four years to be sure of that number and I''m sure of it.\\""},{"companion":"sera","text":"Sera: \\"Somebody gave the order to fire the huts. Orders like that get written down. That is not comfort, it is just true.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Then we''ll put the names on it. All nineteen.","next":"named"},{"label":"The crossing''s fouled with the old timbers. We''ll clear it.","next":"cleared"},{"label":"I''m sorry. That''s all I''ve got.","next":"left"}]}],"named":[{"text":"It takes three days and it is done a name at a time: Frayle gives you eleven off the top of his head and stops, and the rest come off carters on the west road, one and two at a time, most of them at the fold at the drovers'' rest, most of them from men who have to be asked twice and then cannot stop.\\n\\nNineteen. Cut into the flat face of the standing stone in a hand that will embarrass any mason who ever sees it, and which will last as long as the stone.\\n\\nIt is the first thing this place has said in four years.","on_enter":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"the_ford_itself","stage":"named_the_dead"}}],"interjections":[{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric reads the list from the top down, twice, and puts his hand on one of them and then takes it off again."},{"companion":"kessa","text":"Kessa did the second day''s cutting because your hands had gone. She did not offer and did not ask; she took the chisel."}],"choices":[{"label":"Nineteen.","end":true}]}],"cleared":[{"text":"The huts went into the river when they came down, and the burnt timbers went into the bed of the ford, and for four years everybody has been crossing round the fouled part and calling that the crossing.\\n\\nIt is two days of cold, ugly work with ropes and a borrowed team. What comes out is charred oak, four cart-loads of it, and one hut door with its latch still on.\\n\\nAfterwards the ford runs clean over laid stone from bank to bank and will take a wagon at any hour. It is worth more to the west road than anything else you have done out here, and Frayle stands in the shallows watching it for a long time without saying anything at all.","on_enter":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"the_ford_itself","stage":"cleared_the_crossing"}}],"interjections":[{"companion":"sera","text":"Sera: \\"Four cart-loads. Four years. Nobody in Rivermark has ever costed that against the price of a day''s work.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Get the team off the bank.","end":true}]}],"left":[{"text":"\\"Aye,\\" Joss says. \\"Well. It''s most of what anyone''s got.\\"\\n\\nHe puts the river-stone down against the foot of the standing stone with the others, and gets back on the cart, and goes west at a trot like everybody else does.","on_enter":[{"quest_stage":{"quest":"the_ford_itself","stage":"left_the_ford"}}],"choices":[{"label":"Cross.","end":true}]}]}}',0,1,0,NULL),
('kessa','Kessa Dunmar','Mercenary','Half-orc mercenary, drinking alone at the end of the bar, back to the wall.','assets/images/npcs/kessa.png','kessa',1,'{"start":"greeting","nodes":{"greeting":[{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"left"}],"text":"She is at the end of the bar with her back to the wall, exactly where you found her, and she has been there long enough that the innkeeper has stopped clearing round her. She does not get up.\\n\\n\\"Thought you''d be further on than this by now,\\" Kessa says.","choices":[{"label":"I came to ask you back.","next":"kessa_return_ask"},{"label":"I am sorry.","next":"kessa_return_sorry"},{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate","equals":"sold"}],"once":true,"text":"There is nobody at the end of the bar. Mara has cleared the cup away and put the stool back under, and she does not mention it, and she does not have to.","choices":[{"label":"Leave it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"quarry_fate","equals":"ash"}],"once":true,"text":"Kessa is on the wall by the east gate with the axe across her knees, watching the road out of town rather than the road into it. \\"Four hundred,\\" she says. \\"That''s what it went for. Nine years of being told what a person''s worth on paper and I''d never once seen a whole town priced.\\" She does not look round. \\"I''m not leaving. Don''t make that mean more than it does — I''ve no roof and no paper out on me, and those are the only two things I''ve ever needed.\\"","choices":[{"label":"You could go anywhere.","next":"ash_kessa_stays"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"quarry_fate","equals":"steel"}],"once":true,"text":"Kessa is cleaning the axe, which does not need it. \\"Job''s a job,\\" she says. \\"We said we''d finish it and we finished it. I don''t need it to have been nice.\\" A beat. \\"The elf''s not talking to me. That''s fine. She''s not wrong to.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Do you think we were right?","next":"right_and_finished"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"quarry_fate","equals":"pact"}],"once":true,"text":"\\"I''ll say this once and then never again,\\" Kessa says. \\"I''d have taken the hall. You didn''t. Nobody''s dead who''d be alive if I''d had my way, and about forty are alive who wouldn''t.\\" She shrugs, badly. \\"I don''t have to like the sums to do them.\\"","choices":[{"label":"That''s generous.","next":"not_generous"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_house_fate","equals":"favour"}],"once":true,"text":"\\"He wrote it in a book,\\" Kessa says. \\"Not the forty-one. Us. Date, hand, and a line for what we''re owed to do and when, and the when''s blank.\\" She turns the copied list over without reading it, because she cannot. \\"I''ve spent nine years getting a number off my back and I have watched you put a blank one on it. And I asked you to. I know I asked you to.\\"","choices":[{"label":"It''s a favour, not a debt.","next":"kessa_the_blank_line"},{"label":"You have the names.","next":"kessa_the_blank_line"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_house_fate","equals":"taken"}],"once":true,"text":"Kessa has the register open on the table in front of her, upside down, which she has not noticed. \\"Read me one,\\" she says. \\"Any one. Not mine. I want to hear a name off it that isn''t mine, because up to about an hour ago the whole thing was still a story I was telling myself.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Read her a name.","next":"kessa_read_a_name"},{"label":"It''s upside down, Kessa.","next":"kessa_read_a_name"}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_house_fate","equals":"lie"}],"once":true,"text":"\\"Right,\\" Kessa says, and that is the whole of it for about a minute. Then: \\"Mine''s settled. That''s what I went in for and that''s what I''ve got, and I''d have said the same to anyone who asked me on any day of the last nine years.\\" She picks the gauntlet up. \\"Forty of them, though. I''d like to stop being able to count.\\"","choices":[{"label":"You did what you came to do.","next":"kessa_let_it_lie_after"},{"label":"We can go back.","next":"kessa_let_it_lie_after"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"quest":"kessa_the_house_that_bought_her","status":"active"}],"text":"Kessa has the clerk''s copy folded into a square in her fist and has plainly had it there a while. \\"Forty-one,\\" she says. \\"That''s the number I keep going back to. Not ninety. Forty-one.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me again what the clerk read you.","next":"camp_kessa_the_list_who"},{"label":"Then we go to the counting house.","next":"kessa_house_office"},{"label":"Not yet.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"quest":"kessa_debt","status":"active"}],"text":"Kessa has her back to the wall again and both hands flat on the table. \\"Man in the green coat by the hearth,\\" she says, without moving her head. \\"Don''t look. He''s been here since noon and he''s not drinking.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Who is he?","next":"who_is_finch"},{"label":"I''ll deal with it.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate","equals":"paid"}],"once":true,"text":"Kessa has both hands flat on the table and her back to the room, which in the whole time you have known her she has not done once. She catches you noticing. \\"Yeah,\\" she says. \\"I''ve been sat like this twenty minutes finding out what it''s like.\\"","choices":[{"label":"And?","next":"after_paid"},{"label":"Take your time.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate","equals":"fought"}],"once":true,"text":"The axe is in three pieces on the table, which is what Kessa does when she wants her hands busy and her eyes on the door. \\"He''s not dead and he''s not paid,\\" she says. \\"So it''s a thing that''s still happening, and I''d rather say that out loud than have you work it out off my face in a month.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then it''s still happening to both of us.","next":"after_fought"},{"label":"You''d rather be hunted than owned.","next":"after_fought"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"kessa","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_locked":true}}],"text":"\\"You keep your word,\\" Kessa says, apropos of nothing, halfway through cleaning a gauntlet. \\"That''s it. That''s the whole of what I was going to say. I''ve been working out how to say it for about nine days.\\"","choices":[{"label":"That took nine days?","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"So do you.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Get some sleep.","end":true}],"once":true},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"}],"text":"\\"Where are we going and who''s in the way,\\" Kessa says. It is not impatience. It is the entire conversation she prefers to have.","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}],"text":"Kessa has taken the seat next to yours rather than the one facing the door, which for her is roughly a declaration read from a balcony.","choices":[{"label":"You''re facing away from the door.","next":"romance_two"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}],"text":"The strap on your pack has been mended. It is a good repair and it is in her thread, which is the wrong colour, and she has not moved it to the inside where it would not show.","choices":[{"label":"You mended my strap.","next":"romance_two"},{"label":"Say nothing about it.","end":true},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}],"text":"\\"I''ve been thinking about the smithy again,\\" Kessa says, out of nothing at all, halfway through a mouthful. \\"Hinges. Barrel hoops.\\" She swallows. \\"And I''ve stopped putting only one person in it, and I''ve decided not to be embarrassed about that, and I''d rather you heard it in daylight than worked it out.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Put me in it, then.","next":"romance_two"},{"label":"Hinges it is.","end":true},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}],"text":"She has taken the watch again, and taken it early, and taken it on the side of the camp you are sleeping on. None of those three is an accident and she would argue about all of them.","choices":[{"label":"Come and sit down.","next":"romance_two"},{"label":"Let her stand it.","end":true},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"kessa","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_locked":true}}],"text":"Kessa has been about to say something for two days. You can watch her get to the front of it and then find a strap that needs doing. \\"Not yet,\\" she says, when she catches you waiting. \\"I''ve nearly got it in an order.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Say it out of order.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Take your time.","end":true},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"kessa","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_locked":true}}],"text":"\\"I''ve worked out what it is,\\" Kessa says, apropos of nothing, over the top of the gauntlet. \\"It''s that I''ve never had to think past the end of a contract before and I''ve started doing it, and it''s making me clumsy, and I''ve decided to tell you that rather than be clumsy quietly.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Go on, then.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Be clumsy. It suits you.","next":"romance_one"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"}],"text":"Kessa has the whetstone out and is not using it, which is her version of pacing. \\"Say a thing,\\" she says. \\"Any thing. I''ve been in my own head since this morning and it''s a small house.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"}],"text":"\\"I ate, I slept about five, the axe is sound and the strap''s mended,\\" Kessa says, before you have opened your mouth. \\"That''s the whole report. You get round to asking it eventually and I thought I''d save us the middle.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"}],"text":"Kessa is standing where she can see the door, eating something out of a cloth, which is how she eats. \\"Go on,\\" she says round it. \\"I can chew and be told things.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"}],"text":"\\"There''s a man out there watching this place who isn''t watching this place,\\" Kessa says, without pointing at anything. \\"Don''t turn round. He''ll be gone in an hour and he''ll turn out to be nobody and I''ll have been wrong, and I''d still rather have said it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"}],"text":"Kessa has her boots off, which happens about once a fortnight and which she treats as a serious lapse in security. \\"Make it quick,\\" she says. \\"I feel wrong.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"}],"text":"She is counting something under her breath and stops when you get close, which means it was the exits again. \\"Habit,\\" she says, not apologising for it. \\"Right. What.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"sera","status":"active"}],"text":"Kessa jerks her chin at the far side of the room, where Sera is doing something quiet with a wax tablet. \\"I''m not going to make a thing of it,\\" she says, making a thing of it. \\"I just want it on record that I know exactly what she is.\\"","choices":[{"label":"She''s useful.","next":"about_sera"},{"label":"So does she, about you.","next":"about_sera"},{"label":"Drop it.","end":true},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"aldric","status":"active"}],"text":"\\"Your brother said a thing to me this morning about mercy,\\" Kessa says, \\"and I''ve carried it round all day like a stone in a boot, and I want it noted that I haven''t decided he''s wrong.\\"","choices":[{"label":"What did he say?","next":"about_aldric"},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"companion":"ilse","status":"active"}],"text":"\\"The warden was out before it was light. Counting.\\" Kessa turns the gauntlet over. \\"Came back, wrote it down, told nobody. Eleven years of that.\\" A beat. \\"That''s the part that gets me and I''d thank you not to repeat it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell her yourself.","next":"about_ilse"},{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate","equals":"paid"}],"text":"Kessa has the stool turned so her back is to the door, and has not turned it back. \\"Still doing it,\\" she says, when she sees you see. \\"On purpose. It''s practice.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate","equals":"fought"}],"text":"\\"Two in the yard last night who weren''t drinking,\\" Kessa says. \\"Gone by first light. That''s the third town.\\" She does not appear troubled by it. \\"Saying it so it''s said, and so it isn''t a surprise to anybody later.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"ledger_fate","equals":"burned"}],"text":"\\"Two carters at the bar had it that the mill''s books went in a grate,\\" Kessa says. \\"They reckon the reeve did it and they reckon he''s clever for it.\\" She turns the cup she is not drinking from. \\"Nobody''s ever going to know what that cost her. That''s the bit that sits wrong.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"ledger_fate","equals":"reed"}],"text":"\\"Wagon went to the assize lockup at dawn,\\" Kessa says. She does not pick the gauntlet back up, which is the tell. \\"I said what she was and I was right about it, and I''ve spent the week finding out that being right doesn''t do anything at all.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"ledger_fate","equals":"sold"}],"text":"\\"There''s a man in this town paid you sixty gold to make a problem stop being a problem,\\" Kessa says, \\"and I''ve spent all week trying to work out how that''s different from a factor buying paper, and I can''t get there.\\" She shrugs, badly. \\"I''m not going anywhere. I''d just stopped being able to keep it behind my teeth.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"hills_fate","equals":"ambush"}],"text":"\\"Eleven carters walked into Rivermark with their wagons and their teeth,\\" Kessa says. \\"That''s the whole of it and nobody will ever write it down.\\" She tests the edge with her thumb. \\"I''ve been in four companies that did a road badly. That one we did right.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"hills_fate","equals":"escort"}],"text":"\\"Six days on a wagon box and not one arrow,\\" Kessa says. \\"Worst work there is. I''d take it every time.\\" She flexes the signing hand. \\"Nobody buys you a drink for a road where nothing happened. That''s the job and it''s why nobody wants it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"hills_fate","equals":"reroute"}],"text":"\\"Road''s moved and the raids have stopped, which means they were never about the road,\\" Kessa says. \\"Somebody was reading the manifests before the wheels turned.\\" She sets the stone down. \\"I don''t like a plan that works because the other side let it work.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"deep_shaft_fate","equals":"sealed"}],"text":"\\"Forty feet of hill on top of it and I still won''t sleep on that side of a camp,\\" Kessa says. \\"I told the warden. She said that was sensible.\\" A pause. \\"That was not the answer I was after.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"deep_shaft_fate","equals":"sounded"}],"text":"\\"I''ve killed a fair number of things and never once had one coming *up* at me,\\" Kessa says. \\"Down, at a wall, at a gate — that''s a thing defending. That one was going somewhere.\\" She turns the axe over. \\"I want to go back down and I know exactly how stupid that is.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_house_fate","equals":"favour"}],"text":"Kessa has the clerk''s list in her shirt and takes it out about four times an evening to look at a thing she cannot read. \\"Thirty-nine to go,\\" she says. \\"I''ve got a man in Handel''s writing to the two I know where they are. Costs me a silver a letter and I''d pay ten.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_house_fate","equals":"taken"}],"text":"\\"Somebody''s going to come and ask for that book back,\\" Kessa says, evenly. \\"That''s fine. That''s a thing with a door on it and a person behind the door.\\" She goes back to the gauntlet. \\"Nine years I had a thing coming that had nobody behind it. This is the better one.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_house_fate","equals":"lie"}],"text":"Kessa is at the end of the bar with her back to the wall, out of habit rather than need, and she has stopped turning the stool round. \\"Don''t,\\" she says, before you have said anything. \\"I know what I know. Ask me about the road.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"pool":"settled","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"counting_house_marked"}],"text":"\\"He didn''t shout and he didn''t send anybody,\\" Kessa says, for about the fourth time this week. \\"He sat down and squared his blotter.\\" She turns the gauntlet over. \\"Nine years of men who shouted. I''d not understood until then that the shouting was the cheap end of it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the debt.","next":"the_debt_talk"},{"label":"What do you make of the others?","next":"the_others"},{"label":"Sit down a while.","next":"camp"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","status":"active"},{"flag":"kessa_returned"}],"pool":"settled","text":"\\"You came and got me,\\" Kessa says, apropos of nothing at all, days later and a long way from the point. \\"I''d have sat in that chair. I want you to know I''d genuinely have sat in it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"I know.","end":true}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"met_kessa"}],"text":"The half-orc at the end of the bar has not touched the cup in front of her and has paid for four. She looks at you once, all the way down, and goes back to the wall.","choices":[{"label":"You''re waiting for someone.","next":"the_pitch"},{"label":"Nothing.","end":true}]},{"text":"The half-orc at the end of the bar does not look up. \\"I''m not for hire on a Tuesday,\\" she says, to the cup, \\"and you''re not from here, so you don''t know that''s a joke.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"met_kessa"}],"choices":[{"label":"Then when are you for hire?","next":"the_pitch"},{"label":"Leave her alone.","end":true}]}],"the_pitch":[{"text":"\\"Kessa Dunmar. Nine years under three different captains and all three companies are gone, which people take badly until they hear the years.\\" She turns the cup around. \\"I work for whoever says a number and then pays the number. That''s the whole of my politics.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Come with us.","effects":[{"recruit":"kessa"}],"next":"she_joins"},{"label":"You''ve been sitting here four days. Somebody''s coming for you.","check":{"skill":"insight","dc":13,"on_success":"she_admits_the_debt","on_failure":"she_shuts_it_down"}},{"label":"Maybe later.","end":true}]}],"she_admits_the_debt":[{"text":"Kessa looks at you properly for the first time. \\"Ninety gold,\\" she says. \\"Sold on twice. The company that made me sign it doesn''t exist and the paper still does, which I''m told is how paper works.\\" She shrugs. \\"Yes. Somebody''s coming. I''d rather be moving when he gets here.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"kessa_debt_known"}],"choices":[{"label":"Then move with us.","effects":[{"recruit":"kessa"}],"next":"she_joins"},{"label":"Not my problem.","end":true}]}],"she_shuts_it_down":[{"text":"\\"No,\\" Kessa says. \\"Try that again and we''ll have a different afternoon.\\" She has not moved and nothing about her has changed and you believe her completely.","choices":[{"label":"Fair. Come with us anyway.","effects":[{"recruit":"kessa"}],"next":"she_joins"},{"label":"Leave it.","end":true}]}],"she_joins":[{"text":"\\"Right,\\" says Kessa, and stands, and is a great deal larger standing. \\"Terms. You say what you want done. If I won''t do it I say so at the time, out loud, in front of everyone, and not afterward in a sulk. And you pay what you said you''d pay.\\" She puts a hand out. \\"That''s it. That''s all of it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Agreed.","next":"terms_agreed"},{"label":"What won''t you do?","next":"what_she_wont_do"}]}],"terms_agreed":[{"text":"She shakes on it once, hard, and then goes to get her gear from behind the bar, where it has been for four days, packed.","choices":[{"label":"Good.","end":true}]}],"what_she_wont_do":[{"text":"\\"People who can''t fight back,\\" Kessa says. \\"That''s the list. It''s a short list and I''ve never had to explain it twice to anyone I stayed with.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Agreed.","next":"terms_agreed"}]}],"the_debt_talk":[{"conditions":[{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate","equals":"paid"}],"text":"\\"Paid,\\" Kessa says. \\"Don''t. I''ve thought of about four ways to say the thing and they''re all worse than not saying it.\\" She looks at the door, and then deliberately does not. \\"I owe you. That''s a different word than the one I had before and I like it better.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"},{"label":"Finch bought your paper. Who from?","next":"camp_kessa_the_list"}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate","equals":"fought"}],"text":"\\"Finch walked out of that yard without a mark on him and made sure I saw him do it,\\" Kessa says. \\"So it''s not done. It''s just moved.\\" She tests the axe edge. \\"Better than owing, though. I''d rather be hunted than owned, and I''ve been both.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"},{"label":"Finch bought your paper. Who from?","next":"camp_kessa_the_list"}]},{"conditions":[{"flag":"kessa_debt_known"}],"text":"\\"Ninety gold and a man in a green coat,\\" Kessa says. \\"That''s the shape of it. I''m not asking you to pay it. I''m telling you because you''ll find out when he walks in, and I''ve decided I''d rather you heard it from me.\\"","choices":[{"label":"We''ll deal with him when he comes.","next":"back_to_it"},{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"There''s a debt,\\" Kessa says. \\"There''s always a debt. Ask me when it''s standing in the room and not before.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"kessa_debt_known"}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]}],"back_to_it":[{"text":"\\"Good,\\" she says, and that is the end of it as far as she is concerned, and she goes back to the gauntlet.","choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]}],"who_is_finch":[{"text":"\\"Garrow Finch. Buys paper off dead companies at a quarter and collects it at full.\\" Kessa''s hands have not moved off the table. \\"He''s not the problem. He''s polite and he''s careful and he brought three people who aren''t. They''re in the yard.\\"","on_enter":[{"set_flag":"met_garrow"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"sera","text":"Sera, not looking up: \\"Ninety gold. I heard. It''s a bad debt on a dead company''s book and he''ll take sixty if you make him wait.\\""},{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric: \\"Then we pay him.\\" Kessa: \\"With what, brother, the sun-disc?\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"I''ll talk to him.","end":true},{"label":"What do you want to happen?","next":"what_she_wants"}]}],"what_she_wants":[{"text":"Kessa is quiet for a second, which for her is a long time. \\"I want it over,\\" she says. \\"Any way it goes over. I''ve had it nine years and I''ve stopped being able to tell what I''d do without it.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Then we''ll end it.","end":true}]}],"about_sera":[{"text":"\\"She kept books for a man who was starving this town on purpose, and she did it for four gold a quarter and a threat, and she''d do it again tomorrow for the right threat.\\" Kessa shrugs. \\"That''s not a slander. Ask her. She''ll agree with me. That''s the part I can''t get past.\\"","interjections":[{"companion":"sera","text":"Sera, from across the room, without looking up: \\"I would agree with you. I''d also have got us out of the granary loft alive, which you were not going to.\\""},{"companion":"aldric","text":"Aldric: \\"She was coerced.\\" Kessa: \\"Everyone''s coerced, brother. That''s what a town is.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"She was frightened. You''ve been frightened.","check":{"skill":"persuasion","dc":13,"on_success":"kessa_concedes","on_failure":"kessa_digs_in"}},{"label":"Leave it.","next":"back_to_it"}]}],"kessa_concedes":[{"text":"\\"...Fine,\\" Kessa says, after a while. \\"Fine. I''ve signed a thing I couldn''t read because a man in a tent said sign it. I''m not going to be friends with her. I''ll stop saying it where she can hear.\\"","on_enter":[{"approval":{"sera":5}}],"choices":[{"label":"That''ll do.","next":"back_to_it"}]}],"kessa_digs_in":[{"text":"\\"Don''t,\\" Kessa says. \\"Don''t do the thing where you explain someone to me. I was there when they took the second company''s pay and I know exactly what a frightened clerk is worth in a bad week.\\"","on_enter":[{"approval":{"kessa":-3,"sera":-3}}],"choices":[{"label":"Leave it.","next":"back_to_it"}]}],"the_others":[{"text":"\\"The brother''s got something in his pack he won''t open and something in his head he won''t say, and he''s still the steadiest one here.\\" Kessa counts them off on the gauntlet. \\"The elf''s right about the goblins and she''s going to get us all killed being right about it. The clerk I''ve covered.\\"","conditions":[{"companion":"aldric"},{"companion":"ilse"},{"companion":"sera"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"ilse","text":"Ilse: \\"Being right has never killed anyone. Being right too late has.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"The brother''s got something in his pack he won''t open and something in his head he won''t say, and he''s still the steadiest one here.\\" Kessa counts them off on the gauntlet. \\"The elf''s right about the goblins and she''s going to get us all killed being right about it.\\"","conditions":[{"companion":"aldric"},{"companion":"ilse"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"ilse","text":"Ilse: \\"Being right has never killed anyone. Being right too late has.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"The brother''s got something in his pack he won''t open and something in his head he won''t say, and he''s still the steadiest one here.\\" Kessa counts them off on the gauntlet. \\"The clerk I''ve covered.\\"","conditions":[{"companion":"aldric"},{"companion":"sera"}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"The elf''s right about the goblins and she''s going to get us all killed being right about it.\\" Kessa counts them off on the gauntlet. \\"The clerk I''ve covered.\\"","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse"},{"companion":"sera"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"ilse","text":"Ilse: \\"Being right has never killed anyone. Being right too late has.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"The brother''s got something in his pack he won''t open and something in his head he won''t say, and he''s still the steadiest one here.\\"","conditions":[{"companion":"aldric"}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"The elf''s right about the goblins and she''s going to get us all killed being right about it.\\"","conditions":[{"companion":"ilse"}],"interjections":[{"companion":"ilse","text":"Ilse: \\"Being right has never killed anyone. Being right too late has.\\""}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"The clerk I''ve covered.\\"","conditions":[{"companion":"sera"}],"choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]},{"text":"\\"Ask me when I''ve watched them work.\\" Kessa turns the gauntlet over in her hands. \\"I don''t judge anybody by what they say they''ll do.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Back","next":"greeting"}]}],"romance_one":[{"text":"\\"Nine days, yes,\\" Kessa says. \\"I''ve had two people in nine years I could say a thing like that to and both of them are dead, so you''ll excuse the practice.\\" She is not looking at you. \\"That''s not a question. I''m not asking you a question. I''m telling you where I''ve got to.\\"","on_enter":[{"romance":{"companion":"kessa","stage":1}}],"choices":[{"label":"I''d like you to ask me the question.","next":"romance_two"},{"label":"Understood.","end":true}]}],"romance_two":[{"text":"\\"Right,\\" Kessa says, and then does not say anything for a while, and then: \\"I''m bad at the middle bit. I''m good at deciding and I''m good at afterward. It''s the middle that gets me.\\" She puts the gauntlet down. \\"So take that as decided, and be patient about the middle.\\"","on_enter":[{"romance":{"companion":"kessa","stage":2}}],"choices":[{"label":"I can do that.","end":true}]}],"right_and_finished":[{"text":"\\"Right''s not a thing I get paid to know,\\" Kessa says. \\"Finished is.\\" She holds the axe up to the light and squints at nothing. \\"But I''ll tell you what I keep thinking about. She met us in the doorway. She said she would and then she did. I''ve served under three captains and not one of them would have.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]}],"not_generous":[{"text":"\\"It''s not generous, it''s arithmetic,\\" Kessa says. \\"Generous is what you do when you''ve got spare. I''ve never had spare in my life.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Leave her to it.","end":true}]}],"camp":[{"conditions":[{"quest":"kessa_debt","status":"completed"}],"text":"Nobody has come up the road in eleven days. Kessa has noticed that, the way she notices everything with a door in it, and tonight she is sitting where the heat is instead of where the dark is. \\"Sit down,\\" she says. \\"I''m not doing anything.\\"","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the axe.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_axe"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_axe"},{"label":"Three captains, three companies.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_companies"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_companies"},{"label":"What do you do when this is finished?","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","approval_at_least":15},{"any":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_after"}},{"all":[{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_after_fate"}}]}]}],"next":"camp_kessa_after"},{"label":"What did you put your mark on?","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","approval_at_least":40},{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_the_mark"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_the_mark"},{"label":"Tell me about Finch.","conditions":[{"flag":"met_garrow"},{"any":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_finch"}},{"all":[{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_finch_fate"}}]}]}],"next":"camp_kessa_finch"},{"label":"You''ve been halfway into a sentence for two days.","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","approval_at_least":30},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}},{"not":{"companion":"kessa","romance_locked":true}}],"next":"kessa_close"},{"label":"Come sit by me.","conditions":[{"companion":"kessa","romance_stage":2}],"next":"romance_after"},{"label":"Get some sleep.","end":true},{"label":"Who told Finch to come for you?","conditions":[{"flag":"kessa_debt_fate"},{"not":{"quest":"kessa_the_house_that_bought_her","status":"completed"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_the_list"},{"label":"Read me another name off the list.","conditions":[{"flag":"kessa_names_known"}],"next":"camp_kessa_a_name"},{"label":"You paid a man two silver to read to you.","conditions":[{"flag":"kessa_list_known"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_letters"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_letters"},{"label":"Thirty-one of the Ninth. Do you have the names?","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_kessa_the_mark"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_thirty_one"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_thirty_one"},{"label":"You do that with your hand when the paper comes up.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_hand"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_hand"},{"label":"I will take the watch with you.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_watch"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_watch"},{"label":"Why are you still here?","conditions":[{"flag":"camp_kessa_watch"},{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_useful"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_useful"},{"label":"What happens when you walk into a room.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_half"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_half"}],"pool":"after"},{"conditions":[{"quest":"kessa_debt","status":"completed"}],"pool":"after","text":"The whetstone is out and the axe does not need it, which is what she does instead of sitting still. \\"Nobody''s come up the road,\\" Kessa says. \\"I''ve checked it twice tonight and there was nothing to check either time.\\" She makes room on the log anyway.","choices":[{"label":"Tell me about the axe.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_axe"}}],"next":"camp_kessa_axe"},{"label":"Three captains, three companies.","conditions":[{"not":{"flag":"camp_kessa_companies"}}],"next":"camp_kessa